1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
5. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Mar Mar Apartments", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment in Pula offering a fully equipped kitchen, free WiFi, free parking, and a convenient location close to Valkane Beach, the Arena, and other main city attractions.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment for two people is quite welcoming, tidy, clean, and cared for down to the smallest details.", "Cool apartment, great location, very nice landlords and excellent service", "We are currently staying in the MarMar apartments. It is extremely clean and tidy.  We met the wife and she showed us around the apartment and were everything is.  Honestly no complaints at all - both her and Mario have been so friendly and helpful and considerate. The only thing I would add, though it doesnt affect the review or amount of stars, but from personal experience of owning rental units - I would provide papertowel and serviettes/napkins.  Something so minor. But so far, we are loving the apartment! Great experience and great comfort.  The bed is so extremely comfortable. 10/10 all around :)"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "fish", "pasta", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "MORE fish-food", "phone": "+385 52 211 549", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 11:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "47", "addr:street": "Rizzijeva", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A casual seafood-focused restaurant, serving homemade and Mediterranean dishes with an emphasis on seafood, fish, shellfish, pasta, and daily local specialties.", "reviews": ["Very spartan environment compensated by the quality of the products served. There is no menu: the fish is chosen directly from the fridge counter and is always fresh. Istrian Malvasia of the house very good. Definitely not cheap, but the quality of the dishes deserves the price. In short, a real seafood restaurant where fish is the real and only protagonist, without frills or platitudes. For us it is now a must at every step of our journey to Pula.", "We were in Fish food More at least 7 times during last 3 weeks. The reason of coming back was an incredible service Sandra has provided together with an outstanding seafood pasta. Well done! Worth every penny.", "Probably the best local restaurant you’ll find in Pula. They serve only the freshest fish and seafood, offering a truly local experience. The staff is wonderfully authentic – knowledgeable, passionate, and genuinely caring. The location itself has remained just as it was decades before the restaurant opened, which gives it a unique and timeless charm. You simply share what you feel like eating, and they will prepare it in a way that creates a meal to remember for a lifetime. I warmly recommend this place to anyone visiting Pula – it’s the essence of a true Mediterranean and Istrian experience."], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Furia Restaurant", "phone": "+385 97 683 9992", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-15:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A local seafood spot inside Pula’s market building, Furia is known for fresh, fast, and affordable fish dishes and simple Adriatic specialties.", "reviews": ["A bit spartan, but very good. Fish definitely fresh and very tasty. Friendly and friendly staff.", "Very freshly prepared, very tasty and at a more than fair price on an outdoor terrace. Highly recommended!!", "4 stars. Located on the top floor of the marketplace building. Offers seating inside the building or on the balcony. Food was nice and fresh. Understandably not everything on the menu was in season / available. We had the octopus salad and a couple of pieces of fish. Fresh and cooked well. Washed down with a lovely glass of local white wine. €30 for 2 people. Can't fault the value. Happily recommend this place.", "A place to eat fish in centre of town. They have wild fish in daly offer, as well as grown. Prices are totally acceptable. The staff is amazing, chef is encrideble! Sometimes you have to wait for the table a while, but it is completely worth it. Every time we ate here it was great 🤍🌊🌞"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Dva ferala", "phone": "+385 52 223 365", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-21:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "32", "addr:street": "Kandlerova", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual restaurant in city center, located on the main street near the cathedral, serving grilled dishes, seafood, meat plates, and other Mediterranean-style local favorites in a relaxed setting with a terrace.", "reviews": ["We had a double fish platter . It did not disappoint. The selection was incredible. We would like to draw particular attention to the tuna. As well traveled as we are , nothing tasted like it . Incredible! My husband got a standing aviation for filleting the fish. Wine came in a tumbler , which complimented the fish beautifully. Thank you! We felt very welcome", "We went to eat there twice during the holidays, once truffle noodles and Plescavica. Both were excellent. Good draft beer, what more could you want:)", "The fish platter was excellent! Very fresh and delicious! The service was great! The drinks were good too!Highly recommended!"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "grill", "seafood", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Galeb", "phone": "+385 52 386 361", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Su 10:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "37", "addr:street": "Osječka", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual bistro and grill restaurant serving grilled meat dishes, ćevapi, steaks, mixed platters, fried and grilled squid, whole fish, and seafood specialties.", "reviews": ["Service courteous, eat very delicious at a relatively low price and the beer is on tap. What more could you want", "The service was excellent, always there when you needed something. The food was fresh and extremely delicious, the music was nice, and the overall atmosphere was calm.", "I had the seafood pasta and it was absolutely delicious. It was a very light red cream sauce. I don’t know all the different kinds of seafood that was in it, but there was a big variety and it was delicious. I eat here on August 13 and it was quite warm outside, and I sat on the patio which is covered and shaded and has bands and wasfine to sit in. I’ll be a bit warm. Service was OK but just fine. It’s off the beaten path, so it felt not so part of the hustle and bustle with a little more private."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Valkane", "phone": "+385 52 387 589", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Lungomare", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant on the Lungomare promenade, next to the tennis courts, serving Croatian and Istrian cuisine with terrace seating.", "reviews": ["We had some of the best food in Croatia at this restaurant, it was amazing. We had tuna steak and calamari which were both amazing!! The service was sensational as well, the waitress even offered her jacket to me as the breeze was a bit cool. I could recommend this restaurant highly enough based on our experience.", "One of the best places to eat! The food is fresh and absolutely fantastic, the atmosphere is wonderful,good price and Marijana is truly the best waitress in all of Europe. Thank you for everything! See you next year❤️", "Lovely restaurant, one of the few in the area with waterfront location. Popular with locals and tourist, great food at reasonable prices. Black rice seafood risotto, and meat plate (mixed grill) were really nice."], "price": null}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "pizza", "seafood", "pasta", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Restaurant Boschetto", "phone": "+385 91 121 2058", "opening_hours": "Mo 11:30-20:00; Tu-We off; Th 11:30-17:00; Fr-Su 11:30-20:00", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A relaxed restaurant in Verudela, close to the beach, serves Mediterranean and Istrian cuisine with a focus on fresh fish, seafood, pasta, and local specialties in a green, peaceful setting.", "reviews": ["Perfect place in the the forest shade for lunch/dinner. Good food and good prices. No fine dining, but the sea food and fish and pizzas are excellent. Service staff is very friendly and accomodating.", "We were there a few times during our stay in Verudela. The food was tasty and the portions were big enough! You have a plenty of choice for different dishes, pizza, calamari, octopus, fish ….also the waiters were polite and friendly. I recommend it!", "We were very hungry after spending the whole morning at Ambrela beach and visiting Aquaria, so restaurant Boschetto was the first option. The restaurant was full, only a few free seats in the sun. But after a while we were able to move. The menu is extensive - pizza, meat, fish, salads, seafood. We had a small beer, I had tagliatelle with seafood and my boyfriend chose cevabcici with fries and ajvar. The portions were large, the prices very reasonable. The staff took very good care of us, thank you very much."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "pasta", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Admiral", "phone": "+385 97 744 7461", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Jelušićev prilaz", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual seafood-focused restaurant, serving fresh Adriatic fish, calamari, mussels, shrimp, pasta, and mixed platters, with friendly service and generous portions.", "reviews": ["A great welcome from the staff. Great atmosphere, very relaxed and the staff attentive. Our food was delicious. I had stuffed calamari which was tender and very tasty. My partner had sea bass cooked perfectly. Shame we didn’t have room for dessert!", "Very well, I haven't written reviews in years , here is fascinated by the professional approach to each guest and serving sea dishes as art 🐟🧘🏽‍’”beautiful dishes and portions worthy of giants 😂thank you and low bow chefs 💜🙏🏽", "Very nice restaurant in the neighborhood we stayed in. Good tastes, hearty portions, great Service and very nice staff. We ate here three times during our week. Pasta frutti di mare, risotto frutti di mare, fish plateter and mixed grill were the dishes we ate. You have to try fish flatter, sooooo good flavors and lots of food! Very affordable we thought.", "Great! The food is super good, and the hosts are the best! In my opinion its the best restaurant in Pula. We went here a few times and everytime we went here we went home with a satisfied feeling! Would definetly recommend!"], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "truffles", "wine", "desserts", "gluten_free", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Boccaporta", "phone": "+385 52 506 266", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 11:00-23:00; Su 12:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "18", "addr:street": "Dolinka", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A traditional Istrian tavern, known for local specialties, generous portions, seafood and meat dishes, and a warm, family-style atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Been here for 2 nights in a row. Lots of seafood choices. We ordered scallops and pasta with cuttlefish and mushrooms. One of the best meal I ever had. House white wine is really nice.", "Thoughtful Service, we had a small child with us and were given some books/games to entertain him. We tasted the veal shank which was juicy and tasty (as well as abundant). During dinner we were enlivened by live music, guitar and accordion, pleasant and not at all intrusive. We will return", "Very friendly waiter who helped us choose delicious dishes from the menu. The beef cheek gnocci was excellent, meat was so tender with a perfectly rich sauce. The cuttlefish pasta was interesting with a well balanced sauce. However, the star of the whole meal was the tiramisu - probably the best dessert I've had this year, I couldn't stop talking about it during our whole Europe trip."], "price": null}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Gina", "phone": "+385 98 254 421", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 13:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "23", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.5, "description": "Osteria Gina features nine tables with a view of the sea and pine forest. Everything here begins with a foundation in natural wines, along with a menu that pairs perfectly with them.", "reviews": ["The most unique place I have ever dined in. The owner cooks, serves and is so personal. Only dines a couple guests in his home and need a reservation to eat but worth it. One of the most memorable and amazing dinners I have ever had. If you love unique places, great food, and amazing atmosphere.", "The food was delicious! The steak melted in your mouth and the restaurant itself had a lovely warm atmosphere. Try the lavender ice cream - delicious! Maybe not the cheapest but well worth it. Staff were also great - friendly, helpful and offered recommendations", "Had a wonderful dinner at cosy and rustic Osteria Gina. Being warmly welcomed by the Chef he offered us three choises from fish and meat list. I chose pork neck and filet while my partner had fish. Both choises were delicious, as was also the red and white wine. We left happily after grappas from the House and interesting discussions with the Chef."], "price": "high"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["croatian", "local", "seafood", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Cementara", "phone": "+385 99 835 2503", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Revelanteova", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local bistro, offering affordable daily lunch menus, homemade dishes, seafood and meat specialties, and relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["Very good food and very affordable! It feels very local but there isn't a lot to see around so go there if you're on a walk. Also the waitress was very helpful and cute. 10/10 would go again", "Our accommodation was nearby, so we ended up here by chance. The tomato salad, rump steak with pepper sauce and fries (€13), and the tagliatelle with truffles (€15) were all excellent and very tasty. The prices are absolutely unbeatable. The staff is super friendly. You sit on a small terrace overlooking a parking lot. That's the only downside. Otherwise, a definite thumbs up for authentic, delicious Croatian cuisine.", "A hidden gem in the Docklands. Simple, but the food is fantastic and beautifully presented. We had grilled fish, calamari, and truffle pasta. The service was also very friendly (only Croatian spoken)."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
4. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Villa Nicole", "tags": ["guest_house", "villa", "pool", "wellness", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "garden"], "description": "Spacious wellness villa in Pula with a private pool, sauna, jacuzzi, garden, and family-friendly outdoor facilities, offering a peaceful stay a short drive from the city centre and nearby beaches.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We stayed there for a week and would go back in a heartbeat. The host was incredibly nice, everything was clean, air-conditioned, and new. Plenty of space for eight people. The beach and shops are just a stone's throw away. Simply a top-notch place!", "Booking with Kristina was incredibly easy. All our questions beforehand were answered very quickly. Her husband, Sandi, showed us around the house upon arrival; he was also super friendly and easygoing. The kitchen was very well-equipped. They even delivered dishwasher tablets to our door. We felt very comfortable and can wholeheartedly recommend the house and the owners. While you do need a car to get to the beaches, restaurants, and shops, everything is easily accessible. Thank you so much for the wonderful stay!"]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
6. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
7. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
8. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
10. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["bakery", "breakfast", "coffee", "pizza", "sandwiches", "desserts", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mlinar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-20:00; Sa 06:30-15:00; Su 07:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A casual Mlinar cafe next to the city market, offering baked goods, pastries, sandwiches, and self-service coffee in a simple indoor seating area. It is a convenient spot for a quick breakfast, snack, or coffee break in the city center.", "reviews": ["Everything I've gotten to eat at any Mlinar has been delicious and a good price. I usually avoid chains, but they're just so good!", "Unfortunately the coffee is produced by an automatic machine... So nothing really special The food is okeish, I cannot complain. If you are hungry and you cannot find anything else around, this place will be fine.", "Good bakery, but coffe is overpriced (2 eur for coffe in paper cup?). 🙄Price of yoghurt is also quite high (1.8 eur) - I remember the times then normal price was 0.4 eur (few years ago). 🤑 I had a chicken burek here and I was suprised that I liked it more than traditional one ( with beef )"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "music"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cinderela", "phone": "+385 52 540 777", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "23A", "addr:street": "Pazinska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-running café known for quality coffee, drinks, music, and a lively yet relaxed atmosphere, with regular events and a comfortable terrace.", "reviews": ["We had coffee, it was delicious. Food bought from the bakery across the street can be eaten in the café.", "Good tasting espresso, and they also have things like oat-milk for a cappuccino if you can't handle the cow milk.", "Great for a coffee break or getting with friends. My car service is nearby so I usually wait there to pick up my car."], "price": "low"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "brunch", "breakfast", "burgers", "desserts", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cabahia", "phone": "+385 91 640 6330", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-24:00; Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Širolina", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-standing Veruda café recently refreshed into a snack bar, known for quality coffee, a wide beer selection, brunch dishes, burgers, bao buns, tortillas, desserts, and a relaxed local atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Great food, atmosphere, staff, and prices. I paid €12.80 for two bao buns, sweet potato fries, and a small macchiato. The other day I ordered a veggie tortilla and a hot dog with guacamole sauce via Wolt—each one better than the other. My sincere recommendation for this place!", "Currently the best snack bar in Pula, especially considering they offer a wide range of breakfast/brunch options that lean on the healthier side. The prices are also affordable and justified. The tortilla is large and excellent, the English muffin is my top choice, and the croque madame is also great. Any reviews below 4–5 stars aren’t accurate and can easily be ignored, because every time I’ve been here, it’s been even better than the previous visit.", "Excellent food, great service—an exceptionally kind and professional waiter. A warm and nicely decorated space, which is unfortunately unnecessarily crowded with tables."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "desserts", "ice_cream"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Barbados", "phone": "+385 99 349 0555", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-22:00; Su 07:30-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed cafe in Max City shopping center, ideal for short breaks, long coffee sessions, and casual meetups. With a sunny terrace and laid-back atmosphere, it is a nice place to enjoy coffee, drinks, or a quiet moment with a book or newspaper.", "reviews": ["Great spot for coffee, they also have a fantastic cake selection, I like to come here every time I'm at the mall. The staff is very kind, especially the young female waiter and the young male waiter, both so so kind. I reccomand this spot to anyone passing through, by far the best coffee in the mall", "Great service. Katarina was very helpful and kind. 5/5", "They have real milkshakes made with any flavor ice cream they have! Wonderful"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "ice_cream", "sandwiches", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Milan 1967", "phone": "+385 52 383 296", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-19:00; Sa 07:00-14:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Trg 1. Svibnja", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A popular café by the city market, known as a longtime local meeting spot for coffee, juices, desserts, and light snacks.", "reviews": ["For my taste best coffee in pula and the lemonade fab, staff are friendly and the best thing they are now open till 6pm during the week so after the beach I can get another coffee. Thank You 😊 …", "A great place to sit and watch people pass by. Very friendly waitresses. Selection of snacks and cakes. Fountain nearby where kids can play without danger.", "Nice coffee, desserts and service, a bit expensive though. Atmosphere could be more cosy (for my taste)"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 91 462 9061", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 2.5, "description": "A popular coffee spot in Max City on Stoja, perfect for a coffee break or relaxing after shopping, with Leggiero sandwiches, Torterie Macaron desserts, a spacious terrace, and both smoking and non-smoking areas.", "reviews": ["Since my last visit to this place, I’ve noticed a more positive atmosphere, a friendlier approach, and more efficient service, which wasn’t the case in previous months. You can see the effort and the desire for improvement, and I hope they will continue at this pace and keep the quality staff who create the best impression.", "I really enjoyed coffe here. Don't know what people are talking about. The stuff isn't annoying with questions but always there if you need them. You should definitely try their macarons. But there MUST be more people on the shift. Two people (one mixing, one serving) cannot cope with two terraces and a place inside. But this is a question for the owners, not the employees..", "Besides the fact that the quality has declined over the past few years, from now on you’ll get a slice of cake for €4.10 served in a plastic container with a plastic fork. Top-notch service, no doubt! From today on, I’ll be avoiding this place."], "price": "high"}}
7. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}
8. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "desserts", "gluten_free", "vegan"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cafe Frei", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-21:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Jurja Žakna", "rating": 4.6, "description": "An international coffee bar located in the Kaufland complex and known for a wide range of world-inspired coffee drinks, teas, smoothies, cakes, and take-away options.", "reviews": ["This has become my regular spot for a morning coffee. The coffee is really good (regular, haven’t tried with alternative milks etc.), and they have some variations too. Oit of those I tried a few and they were also amazing. My kid had hot chocolate and it was delicious. I can only but recommend.", "One of the best coffee you can drink in Pula town. The one on the picture is the matcha pistacchio, very delicious. Service and waitress are top of the tops. Very nice looking place, good atmosphere, calm and tidy. You can choose between a variety of coffee, ice cream and desserts. I am very satisfied and can only recommend it. Go for it, 5 stars!", "Absolutely amazing service and coffee to die for. I've been coming to Pula for years on end. I'm yet to find better tasting coffee."], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "sandwiches", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kukuriku", "phone": "+385 52 210 498", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 07:00-23:00; Fr-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su 07:30-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A relaxed city-center café, offering coffee, cocktails and casual sweet and savory snacks in a pleasant outdoor setting.", "reviews": ["Nice place, friendly waiter and really tasty food", "Loved this place! It has really good chocolate croissants and the cappuccino is also very good.", "Nice place in city center. A bit pricey. Aperol spritz 8eur, Hugo the same. Staff was nice and professional."], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "pancakes", "waffles", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pulačinka", "phone": "+385 52 825 825", "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 14:00-22:00; We-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy dessert and pancake cafe in the center of Pula, known for sweet and savory pancakes, waffles, churros, and other treats. Guests can customize their own pancake with a wide range of spreads, toppings, fruit, biscuits, and chocolate bars, making it a popular spot for breakfast, dessert, or a casual snack.", "reviews": ["We had very tasty dessert here, a giant pancake and a wafle. Both were packed with sweet things full of calories 😀 You can select from pre-set variations of sweet or salty pancakes, or you can create your own version.", "This creperie is absolutely amazing! The pistachio sauce is the best I’ve ever had – rich, creamy, and full of flavor. On top of that, the staff are incredibly friendly and attentive, which makes the whole experience even better. Highly recommended!", "We have tried churros and custom pancake. Churros were good, but not the best that we had. But pancake was almost perfect. It was done quickly without saving on ingredients. There are many different ingredients to choose from and you can mix as much as you want. Prices are high but it is normal for Pula I guess..", "I've eaten here a palačinka with my girlfriend and it was the most Nutella I ate in a long time. Then, she had a blood sugar spike so powerful she drove 360 km without any pause. Recommended before long road trips 👍🏻"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
2. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park žrtava fašizma", "tags": ["park", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Neighbourhood park in Šijana, Pula, with a children’s playground, benches, and a pleasant green space for everyday relaxation.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
10. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "Dječje igralište Viška ulica", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Neighbourhood playground in Pula with basic play equipment, a fenced play area, and a family-friendly setting near Fort Casoni Vecchi and St. Paul’s Church.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "SWEET APARTMENT TONY", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Comfortable apartment in Pula with a terrace, balcony, free private parking, and a fully equipped kitchen, set a short drive from the Arena.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Family was help-full and kind. Even gave us a homemade cake :) We had all we needs in their apartment. Close to the apartment is shopping mall with all variety of shops. 3 min by car, maybe 10 by foot.", "Everything was perfect! The owner was super helpful and friendly! They helped us with bringing the suit see and provided everything we needed. The apartment is super well equipped and kids friendly. Supermarket, city center and beaches are nearby. The best part was AC in this hot summer! Sofa bed could be better but manageable", "Very nice apartment with big bathroom, well equipped kitchen, air conditioning in each room, large terrace."]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "MONTE ZARO", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern hostel in Pula with private bathrooms, breakfast, free parking, and a convenient location close to city attractions.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["We were here in August 2025 And it was perfect, receptionists were always nice and helpfull, the breakfast was delicious, the room was clean, new and quite nice. The location is perfect, we were 10 minutes away from the city center. So basically, i recommend this hostel to anyone, who don’t want to Pay big cash, but do want to spend time in comfort accommodation.", "Nice apartment for one night stay. Walking distance from city centre, Arena. Useful kitchen. Good value for money.", "Perfect location if you want to explore the city of Pula by foot. The room was clean and the staff was very helpful. Walls are quite thin and you can hear other people in the hall."]}}
9. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Studio 7even Ground Floor", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "free_parking"], "description": "Compact ground-floor studio apartment with a double bed, private bathroom, dining area, and equipped kitchen, suitable for a comfortable stay near beaches and the city center.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Quiet location, in a ground-floor apartment building; parking is not exclusive, but available and convenient; the owner was very kind and provided all the necessary information for our stay; the studio apartment was clean and well-equipped. Excellent value for money.", "The house is very welcoming and has everything you need. They even left us some snacks and water. All the necessary appliances are there. There are no linen changes.", "Small but well-maintained apartment. Just a few minutes' drive from the beaches and the city center."]}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
6. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
8. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
9. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Camp Brioni", "tags": ["camp", "seaside", "beach", "family_friendly", "sports"], "description": "Seaside campsite near Pula set in a pine forest, with a long pebble beach, views of the Brijuni Islands, and a wide range of sports and accommodation options.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Camp neat and clean. Sanitary facilities are regularly cleaned and toilet paper is never lacking. Staff friendly. The downside is that the WI FI doesn't work, nor does the data network. Not for Telemach users or Telekom users. It's like there's a dead pocket for the signal there. Pizzeria RR is excellent, as is the Mistral bar, where they have top-notch burgers. The downside of these two bars is that payment is only possible with cash and not with a card.", "We rented a mobile home and had a wonderful 12 days. We would gladly do it again.", "Toilets were super clean! Very friendly welcome. Quite large, but you don't notice that because of the different sections on the grounds. Just outside the campsite is a very long, well-maintained beach with beach bars that seems to go on forever. A bike or moped is recommended, or I think you can also take the bus to explore the surrounding area. The pebble beach in section 'A' does have a lot of large boulders, but just outside the campsite (past the small harbor) is also pleasant. €95 for 2 nights for 2 people with a dog, electricity on the second row with a sea view."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "meat", "vegetarian", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Epulon Food & Wine", "phone": "+385 98 949 9023", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Epulonova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A stylish wine and food bar in central Pula, Epulon combines traditional Istrian cuisine with seasonal, more refined dishes, with a strong focus on local ingredients, wines, tapas, and a relaxed indoor terrace setting.", "reviews": ["Hospitality was excellent. Service and food was delicious. I felt like at home.", "Great restaurant, food was delicious and very friendly stuff...", "The place is spectacular for an outing of any kind. The atmosphere is very nice and refined. The furniture, the sweetness of the wench... all perfect. Good prices.", "Absolutely LOVED the place! The waitress was lovely, easy to talk to and helped me pick exactly what I wanted. I came back the second time because of her:) The food was delicious and nicely served. I didn't have to wait much. The atmosphere, music - everything was great. This place is a hidden gem, recommend to those who'd like to eat and relax 💎"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "pasta", "cocktails", "coffee", "desserts", "wine"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Yacht Restaurant & Lounge Bar", "phone": "+385 91 633 3359", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "17", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A stylish seaside bar and restaurant in a tourist resort in Pula, set by the hotels and the sea, offering local and international dishes, drinks, coffee, and desserts.", "reviews": ["Great place with lovely food and cocktails and a great view. We always managed to secure a table without a reservation and staff were helpful", "We enjoyed this restaurant so much that we returned a few nights later to try it again. The views are spectacular. The food was delicious and the staff were friendly and knowledgeable about the food and wine. The only downside was the toilets were a bit grubby.", "Lovely little restaurant overlooking the sea and surrounding area in Pula. Firstly the staff and service was excellent! Everyone was so welcoming, our waiter had brilliant recommendations which we went for and the food was so good! The local white wine was so nice too! Desert and coffees were also lovely of course and the view from our table was awesome! We had a really lovely evening which was made better by the staff and the setting. Thank you all!"], "price": "high"}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "wine", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Gina", "phone": "+385 98 254 421", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 13:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "23", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.5, "description": "Osteria Gina features nine tables with a view of the sea and pine forest. Everything here begins with a foundation in natural wines, along with a menu that pairs perfectly with them.", "reviews": ["The most unique place I have ever dined in. The owner cooks, serves and is so personal. Only dines a couple guests in his home and need a reservation to eat but worth it. One of the most memorable and amazing dinners I have ever had. If you love unique places, great food, and amazing atmosphere.", "The food was delicious! The steak melted in your mouth and the restaurant itself had a lovely warm atmosphere. Try the lavender ice cream - delicious! Maybe not the cheapest but well worth it. Staff were also great - friendly, helpful and offered recommendations", "Had a wonderful dinner at cosy and rustic Osteria Gina. Being warmly welcomed by the Chef he offered us three choises from fish and meat list. I chose pork neck and filet while my partner had fish. Both choises were delicious, as was also the red and white wine. We left happily after grappas from the House and interesting discussions with the Chef."], "price": "high"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "meat", "wine", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Popaj", "phone": "+385 97 731 9175", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Maksimijanova", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A cozy restaurant in old town known for grilled meat, fresh seafood, and classic Croatian dishes. With its charming outdoor terrace, friendly service, and menu featuring fish platters, tuna steak, calamari, and local wine, it is a great spot for a relaxed meal in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Great location, no waiting time at dinner (7pm). Staff is very good and the atmosphere was nice, pretty quiet outside. We took meat plate and calmari, which had no taste but sauces gave them some flavours. The mussel was good.", "Very good service, waiter and waitress are really kind and speak multiple languages, English and Italian very well! Food amazing, very fulfilling and well served and tasty! Calamari in different ways are always very soft and so so good! They do as well this honey grappa flavoursome! Thank you so much!", "we kinda stumbled upon this place while searching for a restaurant to feast for dinner. its nestled in a little corner so there’s space for privacy if you prefer it, ambiance is pretty top notch. the food was not too bad, but the lack of variety and not-so-crispy calamari takes a star away from a perfect 5 rating. the wait staff and owners were very pleasant and friendly though, we really enjoyed their service!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "pasta", "wine", "cocktails", "hotel_restaurant"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Vela Nera", "phone": "+385 52 300 620", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "3b", "addr:street": "Franje Mošnja", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A stylish hotel restaurant in Šišan near Pula, serving Mediterranean and Istrian cuisine, local wines, cocktails, business lunches, and catering in an elegant setting.", "reviews": ["Everything was impressive, we stayed for a couple of days and we had a really good time. In addition the food from the breakfast and the restaurant was delicious with an excellent presentation. Finally, the staff was super friendly and really professional!", "This is a gem! A great family run hotel with amazing food. The service is just wonderful with an attitude that makes everything possible. I stayed 8 nights in a very spacious super clean room. I enjoyed the pool and the fabulous food. It was truly a home away from home. For me the location was great, easy drives into the main tourist areas for work while I could enjoy the off the beaten track feel of the calm village. I am hoping to go back for leisure with my family.", "Went for food as part of our wedding anniversary celebrations. The service was fantastic, the food was absolutely brilliant. We had beef steak and tuna steak which were both cooked to perfection. The deserts were wonderful, apple strudel and a chocolate souffle. Great evening in a fantastic setting to watch the sun go down over a tasty bottle of wine which was superbly recommended by our waiter."], "price": "high"}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "pizza", "pasta", "grill", "meat", "cocktails", "coffee"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "E&D lounge", "phone": "+385 52 213404", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "22", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A seasonal bistro and lounge bar on Verudela in Pula, offering Mediterranean dishes, pizza, pasta, seafood, meat dishes, cocktails, and a relaxed terrace with a sea view.", "reviews": ["Really nice place, we had pizza which was really good and reasonably priced. Drinks are a bit spenny compared to the local bars/restaurants, but the staff are so lovely and patient with us as we tried to muddle through with our terrible Croatian. There's even a friendly cat around!", "We came in the middle of the day and were offered a surprisingly good selection of food, coffee and ice cream. The view from the terrace is fab as the bar is within walking distance of a beach. There is also a modern art display just in front of it.", "I only had a coffee after a walk around the coast, but cappuccino was good and good value. Staff were friendly. The views were beautiful."], "price": null}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "regional", "istrian", "pasta", "grill", "meat", "seafood"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Konoba Veruda", "phone": "+385 52 721 302", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 11:00-22:00; Su 11:00-17:00", "addr:housenumber": "27", "addr:street": "Tomasinijeva", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A traditional tavern in Veruda serving authentic Istrian cuisine in a warm, rustic setting. The menu focuses on homemade pasta, goulash, grilled meat, seafood, truffle dishes, and other local specialties, making it a great place to try classic regional food.", "reviews": ["The atmosphere of the place, ambient, and friendliness of our waitress was so wonderful. But even more impressive was the amazing food! Marvelous experience", "We took a chance on this place and were completely blown away by the quality and quantity of food. Our final dinner in Pula before heading home was amazing. The steaks and fish dishes are superior and everything prepared with care and attention. The mangold side (which we thought was spinach) is devine. We were treated to free shots of the home-brewed liquor before leaving. Fabulous!", "If you're visiting Pula and looking for a spot with great service, generous portions, and good value for money, this restaurant is a must-try. Conveniently located near our hotel, it offered a welcoming atmosphere. While it's not within walking distance of the city center, it's easily accessible via bus 2A, taking only about 10-15 minutes. The food was delicious, with portions larger than expected, making it perfect for those with a hearty appetite. Overall, this place combines quality dining with affordability, making it a top recommendation for anyone visiting Pula."], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "pizza", "pasta", "seafood", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Imperium Bistro", "phone": "+385 98 219 530", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "8", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Elegant bistro on Forum square that combines long-standing local tradition with a more modern kitchen, offering refined Mediterranean and seasonal dishes in the heart of Pula.", "reviews": ["With a new manager and chef at the helm, this restaurant is on a trajectory towards success in 2024 and beyond. Their innovative approach to food and hospitality, coupled with a commitment to excellence in every aspect of their operation, sets them apart as a standout destination for food lovers and connoisseurs alike. 💪💪🍻❤️", "Nice restaurant with very romantic atmosphere. The location is amazing. Had seafood plate and loved all the seafood options, but the potatoes tasted weird, for which I am giving a bit less. But the local Istrian delicacies were very tasty! Prosciutto was also amazing.", "This restaurant is superb. You cannot fault it. Service and food were all so good. Our dishes were excellent and the food that was brought to the tables around us looked amazing too. We had traditional Istrian cuisine. I could’ve stayed there all day. This place is a must visit if you’re visiting Pula. Thanks again.", "Really good food, served in a nice manner. The location is also nice, in the old town of Pula. The restaurant is officially closing at 22 hrs, but if you are already at the table, you can continue to enjoy your food without stress (pics made at 22:45 hrs :) ). Thank you for an exquisite evening!"], "price": null}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "pizza", "pasta", "burgers", "salads", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Oliva", "phone": "+385 52 590 781", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-20:00", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant in the Verudela resort complex, set next to the pools and offering a varied menu of Istrian dishes, seafood, grilled meat, pizza, salads, pasta, burgers, and desserts in a relaxed holiday setting.", "reviews": ["This place is lovely. It’s sunny and right by the shore, with a beautiful sea view from inside. The service is friendly and fast - no long waiting times for food, which is a big plus. The Croatian dishes are delicious, the cocktails are great, and the prices are very reasonable. A perfect spot to relax, enjoy good food, and take in the view. Highly recommend!", "The location is just wonderful with great views and a feeling of space. We have eaten here now 3 times and each time the service has been good and the food excellent. The range of options available mean you should find something to your liking. Definitely recommended", "Oh my gosh never ever have I gotten the service this place offered me! Especially for a pool lounge! I asked if I could get some plastic cups for my water so I could drink it at the pool and they bring me the cups with ice 🧊 . It’s a kindness and this place is full of these little gestures! Amazing staff on a beautiful spot! Every visit was 5 stars!! Good cocktails ! Good food good icecream and a customer service focused on delivering the extra holiday feel!! I am a fan!"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["regional", "mediterranean", "italian", "croatian", "grill", "meat", "pasta", "seafood", "wine", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Konoba Bocun", "phone": "+385 99 505 2278", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 16:00-23:00, Sa-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "24", "addr:street": "Šijanska Cesta", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A traditional tavern surrounded by greenery and close to Šijana Forest. Konoba Bocun offers a blend of traditional Istrian and international cuisine, with homemade pasta, truffle dishes, grilled specialties, creative seasonal meals, and a strong selection of quality local wines in a warm, authentic setting.", "reviews": ["This place is located outside the chaos of the city and it is really a shame that it does not enjoy wide visibility. The location is very nice and cared for, the staff is very kind and attentive, you eat good fish (I did not taste the meat so I can not say). Prices are in line with other restaurants. I recommend it if you do not want too much confusion and eat in peace", "Konoba Bocun was a wonderful surprise. The food was absolutely delicious, fresh, and full of authentic flavors with some twist. Service was super, super friendly and fast, making us feel welcome and relaxed the whole time.", "We were pleasently surprised with this restaurant, from the road you cannot say it has such great atmosphere. The stuff is super nice and food delicious. We had tuna stake that melted on the mouth and home made gnocchi with deer, 2 glasses of teran, bottled water and home made bread for 45 eur. We will certainly visit again.", "A perfect meal. The salad with cuttlefish was amazing also the sea bass filled with shrimp and spinach + the dessery with truffles was really really good! Perfect experience"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "brunch", "breakfast", "burgers", "desserts", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cabahia", "phone": "+385 91 640 6330", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-24:00; Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Širolina", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-standing Veruda café recently refreshed into a snack bar, known for quality coffee, a wide beer selection, brunch dishes, burgers, bao buns, tortillas, desserts, and a relaxed local atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Great food, atmosphere, staff, and prices. I paid €12.80 for two bao buns, sweet potato fries, and a small macchiato. The other day I ordered a veggie tortilla and a hot dog with guacamole sauce via Wolt—each one better than the other. My sincere recommendation for this place!", "Currently the best snack bar in Pula, especially considering they offer a wide range of breakfast/brunch options that lean on the healthier side. The prices are also affordable and justified. The tortilla is large and excellent, the English muffin is my top choice, and the croque madame is also great. Any reviews below 4–5 stars aren’t accurate and can easily be ignored, because every time I’ve been here, it’s been even better than the previous visit.", "Excellent food, great service—an exceptionally kind and professional waiter. A warm and nicely decorated space, which is unfortunately unnecessarily crowded with tables."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "desserts", "cocktails", "city_center", "breakfast", "brunch"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Aperitivo bar Galerija", "phone": "+385 98 435 580", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-17:00", "addr:housenumber": "26", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A charming cafe located right above the Pula Arena, ideal for breakfast, coffee, cocktails, drinks, or ice cream with a unique historic backdrop. Its setting next to the ancient amphitheater makes it a great stop for a relaxed break in one of the city’s most iconic spots.", "reviews": ["A beautiful place next to the walls of the Great Arena. The service was very friendly and fast, and the food was even better. We had breakfast and got coffee with it and freshly squeezed orange included in the price, the croissants were warm and wonderful with cappuccino. Really worth a visit, all compliments and wonderful experience 🥐", "Friendly service. Cool atmosphere. There's a restroom inside. 🚻", "And it's great here. We climbed up and ordered ice cream for the kids. The ice cream was super tasty and the portions were large. The service was friendly. The garden by the Colosseum was great. I recommend it."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Green", "phone": "+385 52 356 444", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Su 14:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot in Pula’s city center, known for burgers, toast sandwiches, tortillas, salads, and quick meals.", "reviews": ["Great service. We had a Fried Chicken Wrap which was very delicious and perfectly rolled. Even spread filling from top to bottom. Perfect place for a fast snack to go.", "We ordered a falafel and chicken wrap. Both super good quality and value for money. Also the toast were large, can easily share one for 2 kids.", "Perfect food whatever you take, for the price and quality is far ahead best place to eat in Pula. Went to few restaurants but Green is far ahead comparing quality, amount you get and prices. Nothing but best for Green.👏🏼"], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "brunch", "salads", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Street Food Two", "phone": "+385 52 203 236", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "2A", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A modern street food spot in the city center of Pula, offers fresh, colorful, and healthier fast meals, with plenty of salads, bowls, burritos, and vegetarian options.", "reviews": ["Fresh, delicious and surprisingly versatile – highly recommended! The food was consistently fresh and top-quality – you immediately notice that they work with high-quality ingredients. The Service was super friendly, attentive and competent. We were particularly surprised by the selection of vegetarian dishes, which is really great by Croatian standards. Vegan options are also available and lovingly prepared. A place that perfectly combines pleasure, quality and hospitality.", "As a vegetarian finding healthy, vegan and vegetarian options in Croatia is simply too rare to be picky. However, this spot is simple, very nice and the food super fine. We had the tofu poke and the kids the tortellini. Everyone was happy. The staff was extremely friendly!", "Some great fresh healthy options here and amazing tasting food. We had the chickpea patties and tofu poke bowl which was so delicious! Flavours were fab & lovely staff!", "Yum, yum, yum. So fresh and cooked with love. Our first time trying this (we are new to Pula and it's close to our apartment) and it really delivered . I had the prawn and pumpkin risotto and my husband ordered the beef burrito. The taste was great and the portion large, the price reasonable for how much food you get. The service was positive and the server was smiling and happy. Quick stop, we hardly waited. We will be back. Thank you for a lovely, healthy lunch."], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "ice_cream", "coffee"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Stoja Fast Food", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot near the beach in Stoja, offering burgers, sandwiches, coffee, soft drinks, ice cream, with covered outdoor seating and sea views.", "reviews": ["Great little fast food restaurant, with very fair prices and decent choice of food, drink and ice-cream. Parking nearby (free). Had food went for a swim and returned for ice-cream and cold drink", "Best Ice cream in Pula and around. Coffee is out of this world good. Food is great as well. Very pleasent place and staff is very kind, especially young blond server. We are very frequent guests and our friends are very pleased as well.", "Amazing food, waiters came quickly the ice cream is very good, yiu cab pay by cash or card"], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "brunch", "burgers", "music", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "The Shipyard Pub", "phone": "+385 91 181 0630", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 08:00-02:00; Fr 08:00-03:00; Sa 10:00-03:00; Su 10:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Svetog Teodora", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Lively pub on the Riva with burgers, pub food, cocktails, beer, and a spacious terrace. A popular evening spot known for music, DJ sets, quiz nights, and other events in a casual, social atmosphere.", "reviews": ["We stayed here once for a drink and once for dinner. The Service was fast, friendly and accommodating in both cases. The Aperol Spritz was just as delicious as the burgers. These were juicy with very tasty sauces and the caramelized onions rounded it off with a great taste. The fries were also well seasoned and perfectly crispy. The dressing of the ceasar salad was a bit unusual and not quite typical but also incredibly delicious, we would love to come back. Value for money was also reasonable, so what more could you want.", "Friendly and efficient staff with delicious food. The burger was very good and my wife really enjoyed the noodles. Worth a stop. Plenty of seating inside and the vibes were relaxing.", "Great little bar in the heart of Pula! The atmosphere is warm and relaxed, and the staff were incredibly friendly. The music was just right for chatting without shouting, and prices were very reasonable compared to other spots in town. Perfect place to stop for a drink after sightseeing. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a cozy and authentic bar experience in Pula"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Nozi 7", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 05:00-23:00; We-Su 05:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A casual café at Pula’s bus station, suitable for a quick coffee, soft drink, beer, or short stop while waiting for transport.", "reviews": ["This coffee is very close to the bus station. It's clean. The service is quick. The prices are very good 👍 It is a very good place to take a coffee when waiting for your bus :)", "Took the shuttle bus from Pula airport to Pula bus station. 30 kuna (£3.30) each. 15 mins. Hour to kill before bus to heaven ( Rovinj) so popped into this lovely cafe with attached bakery opposite. First beer of the holiday. Great place to wait. Also toilet in bus station has a pay turnstile unlike here. Tabke service for drinks; go to bakery for food. Excellent value. 88Kuna / £10 for 2 coffee and 4*0.33l beers."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["bakery", "breakfast", "coffee", "pizza", "sandwiches", "desserts", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mlinar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-20:00; Sa 06:30-15:00; Su 07:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A casual Mlinar cafe next to the city market, offering baked goods, pastries, sandwiches, and self-service coffee in a simple indoor seating area. It is a convenient spot for a quick breakfast, snack, or coffee break in the city center.", "reviews": ["Everything I've gotten to eat at any Mlinar has been delicious and a good price. I usually avoid chains, but they're just so good!", "Unfortunately the coffee is produced by an automatic machine... So nothing really special The food is okeish, I cannot complain. If you are hungry and you cannot find anything else around, this place will be fine.", "Good bakery, but coffe is overpriced (2 eur for coffe in paper cup?). 🙄Price of yoghurt is also quite high (1.8 eur) - I remember the times then normal price was 0.4 eur (few years ago). 🤑 I had a chicken burek here and I was suprised that I liked it more than traditional one ( with beef )"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Green", "phone": "+385 52 356 444", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Su 14:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot in Pula’s city center, known for burgers, toast sandwiches, tortillas, salads, and quick meals.", "reviews": ["Great service. We had a Fried Chicken Wrap which was very delicious and perfectly rolled. Even spread filling from top to bottom. Perfect place for a fast snack to go.", "We ordered a falafel and chicken wrap. Both super good quality and value for money. Also the toast were large, can easily share one for 2 kids.", "Perfect food whatever you take, for the price and quality is far ahead best place to eat in Pula. Went to few restaurants but Green is far ahead comparing quality, amount you get and prices. Nothing but best for Green.👏🏼"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "brunch", "breakfast", "burgers", "desserts", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cabahia", "phone": "+385 91 640 6330", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-24:00; Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Širolina", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-standing Veruda café recently refreshed into a snack bar, known for quality coffee, a wide beer selection, brunch dishes, burgers, bao buns, tortillas, desserts, and a relaxed local atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Great food, atmosphere, staff, and prices. I paid €12.80 for two bao buns, sweet potato fries, and a small macchiato. The other day I ordered a veggie tortilla and a hot dog with guacamole sauce via Wolt—each one better than the other. My sincere recommendation for this place!", "Currently the best snack bar in Pula, especially considering they offer a wide range of breakfast/brunch options that lean on the healthier side. The prices are also affordable and justified. The tortilla is large and excellent, the English muffin is my top choice, and the croque madame is also great. Any reviews below 4–5 stars aren’t accurate and can easily be ignored, because every time I’ve been here, it’s been even better than the previous visit.", "Excellent food, great service—an exceptionally kind and professional waiter. A warm and nicely decorated space, which is unfortunately unnecessarily crowded with tables."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
7. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "pancakes", "waffles", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Pulačinka", "phone": "+385 52 825 825", "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 14:00-22:00; We-Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A cozy dessert and pancake cafe in the center of Pula, known for sweet and savory pancakes, waffles, churros, and other treats. Guests can customize their own pancake with a wide range of spreads, toppings, fruit, biscuits, and chocolate bars, making it a popular spot for breakfast, dessert, or a casual snack.", "reviews": ["We had very tasty dessert here, a giant pancake and a wafle. Both were packed with sweet things full of calories 😀 You can select from pre-set variations of sweet or salty pancakes, or you can create your own version.", "This creperie is absolutely amazing! The pistachio sauce is the best I’ve ever had – rich, creamy, and full of flavor. On top of that, the staff are incredibly friendly and attentive, which makes the whole experience even better. Highly recommended!", "We have tried churros and custom pancake. Churros were good, but not the best that we had. But pancake was almost perfect. It was done quickly without saving on ingredients. There are many different ingredients to choose from and you can mix as much as you want. Prices are high but it is normal for Pula I guess..", "I've eaten here a palačinka with my girlfriend and it was the most Nutella I ate in a long time. Then, she had a blood sugar spike so powerful she drove 360 km without any pause. Recommended before long road trips 👍🏻"], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Scaletta", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "free_parking", "near_attractions"], "description": "Quaint hotel in central Pula near the Arena, offering comfortable rooms, breakfast, parking, and easy access to the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Small hotel ,central -5' from the amphitheater ,10' from the historic center of the pleasant town of Pula to walk along the tree-lined Rambla between arches small squares churches from the soaring bell towers to the port.Like the city - bright clean and cozy -so the small hotel in retro style ', slightly French proves safe and fulfilling. It is true that the external stairs lead to the familiar reception and that breakfast is served on the room overlooking the street, -I think a former very chic restaurant whose dishes and crockery now serve an essential breakfast - but the pleasure is given by the central heart just a stone's throw from the Colosseum, magnificent!", "We cannot thank the lovely owners enough for all their help with finding a car for us yesterday. The hotel is a real find and value for money and close to the ferry and the city centre. Lovely breakfast also."]}}
9. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Nozi 7", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 05:00-23:00; We-Su 05:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A casual café at Pula’s bus station, suitable for a quick coffee, soft drink, beer, or short stop while waiting for transport.", "reviews": ["This coffee is very close to the bus station. It's clean. The service is quick. The prices are very good 👍 It is a very good place to take a coffee when waiting for your bus :)", "Took the shuttle bus from Pula airport to Pula bus station. 30 kuna (£3.30) each. 15 mins. Hour to kill before bus to heaven ( Rovinj) so popped into this lovely cafe with attached bakery opposite. First beer of the holiday. Great place to wait. Also toilet in bus station has a pay turnstile unlike here. Tabke service for drinks; go to bakery for food. Excellent value. 88Kuna / £10 for 2 coffee and 4*0.33l beers."], "price": "low"}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Zvonimira", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "playground", "family_friendly", "memorial"], "description": "Peaceful waterfront park in Pula with shaded benches, a children’s playground, and cultural landmarks including the Marulić monument and the Balašević bench.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A beautiful green space with several seating areas offering stunning views of the sea, shaded by beautiful trees. The lawn is beautiful and well-kept, and the surrounding area is very clean. Definitely a recommended spot for a lovely stroll."]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Vila Lovorka", "tags": ["hotel", "villa", "national_park", "island", "garden", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach"], "description": "Elegant seaside villa on Veliki Brijun with sea views towards Valbandon and Pula, offering spacious accommodation, a spa area, a Mediterranean garden, and a peaceful stay enriched by historic stone fragments.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": null}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Ribarska Koliba Resort", "tags": ["hotel", "resort", "coastal", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pool", "restaurant", "events"], "description": "A stylish seaside resort in Pula known for its long hospitality tradition, elegant rooms and scenic setting near Marina Veruda and Marina Bunarina. It offers a quiet stay close to beaches, the aquarium and major city sights, with modern amenities such as free WiFi, parking and a pool area.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I've been here a few times, with friends and family and I've been very satisfied every time. The rooms are spacious, clean and well laid out. The breakfast is excellent with a lot of choice and a beautiful view of the marina. The staff is friendly and fantastic, to be commended for their flexibility regarding check-in and check-out and all the necessary services and information. Real value for money!", "Lovely euro boutique hotel that exceeds expectations. Great close in views of the marina from the third floor. Rooms are great, functional and have all the amenities. Very nice outdoor deck. On site Michelin restaurant is a bonus. You will have to Uber bus or drive to the Pula old town. There is a fine sea walk and beaches nearby and a few luxury hotels with nice eating options. Recommended.", "Incredible stay. We stayed for 5 nights as part of our honeymoon journey throughout Croatia. We were kindly upgraded to the 'Fuoco 1' apartment and it was superb, immaculately clean, spacious with fantastic views of the marina from the private balcony. The staff were so friendly and helpful when my wife required some medical attention for her infected insect bite they signposted us to the tourist hospital. We dined at the on-site restaurant twice because the quality of food was so good and was reasonably priced. Aperol spritz only 8€ as an example. Highly reccomended and we hope to visit again in future anniversaries."]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
10. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Modo", "tags": ["hotel", "seaside", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "restaurant"], "description": "A modern seaside hotel in Pula set between the bays of Stoja and Valovine, offering sea-view rooms with balconies, free WiFi, free parking and easy access to nearby beaches. Its quiet location and convenient connection to the city make it suitable for families, couples and business travellers.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Great little hotel in a great location. The staff is very professional and friendly. The premises are modernly decorated and clean. A rich selection of food for breakfast.", "Cosy hotel, spacious room with balcony overlooking the sea. The manager on our arrival was friendly and explained what to visit in Pula and nearby. In addition he suggested (and we went there on the last day) to visit Motovun, castle and village where you eat dishes with truffles. The breakfast of the hotel is great, varied both savory and sweet. At night absolute silence, very relaxing.", "The location was amazing ! We had a balcony that was perfect for watching the sunsets . We easily walked into town ( there also is a bus option ) the rooms were clean and comfortable . My only negative was the AC shut off randomly . The front desk said it turned off every 2 hours and needed to be reset . This was not a great for a cool night sleep without getting up a number of times to reset the AC . Breakfast was very good and it was lovely to eat out on the deck . Staff was friendly and helpful ."]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
4. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}
7. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
8. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
9. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}

