7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
9. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Karmen", "tags": ["hotel", "national_park", "island", "historic", "coastal", "near_beach", "family_friendly"], "description": "Historic seaside guesthouse on Veliki Brijun, offering simple rooms with park or sea views, old-world charm, and a peaceful stay in Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 3.9, "reviews": ["This island is beautiful and has a sense of peace, even on August 15th! The property still has its 1960s furnishings, but it's clean and charming. The terrace overlooking the sea is truly beautiful and relaxing. It's true that there's no air conditioning or mini-bar, but they provided us with a couple of fans, and we managed just fine. What can I say? The island is so beautiful, it's absolutely worth it.", "Wonderful, spacious rooms, just the right amount of nostalgia. In fact, everything is reminiscent of the 60s and 70s and I think it really is from that era, except for the beds, which are new and very comfortable. Again, it's kind of logical that it should stay that way. Everything is very clean. Breakfast is perfect. Staff is very friendly.", "Great view from the balcony, 70s flair – anyone who embraces that will enjoy a lovely and relaxing holiday. Clean and the room is cleaned daily. The only drawback is the lack of air conditioning. The buffet food at Hotel Neptun is excellent."]}}
10. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
6. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
8. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
9. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Camp Brioni", "tags": ["camp", "seaside", "beach", "family_friendly", "sports"], "description": "Seaside campsite near Pula set in a pine forest, with a long pebble beach, views of the Brijuni Islands, and a wide range of sports and accommodation options.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Camp neat and clean. Sanitary facilities are regularly cleaned and toilet paper is never lacking. Staff friendly. The downside is that the WI FI doesn't work, nor does the data network. Not for Telemach users or Telekom users. It's like there's a dead pocket for the signal there. Pizzeria RR is excellent, as is the Mistral bar, where they have top-notch burgers. The downside of these two bars is that payment is only possible with cash and not with a card.", "We rented a mobile home and had a wonderful 12 days. We would gladly do it again.", "Toilets were super clean! Very friendly welcome. Quite large, but you don't notice that because of the different sections on the grounds. Just outside the campsite is a very long, well-maintained beach with beach bars that seems to go on forever. A bike or moped is recommended, or I think you can also take the bus to explore the surrounding area. The pebble beach in section 'A' does have a lot of large boulders, but just outside the campsite (past the small harbor) is also pleasant. €95 for 2 nights for 2 people with a dog, electricity on the second row with a sea view."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Vila Lovorka", "tags": ["hotel", "villa", "national_park", "island", "garden", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach"], "description": "Elegant seaside villa on Veliki Brijun with sea views towards Valbandon and Pula, offering spacious accommodation, a spa area, a Mediterranean garden, and a peaceful stay enriched by historic stone fragments.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": null}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Ribarska Koliba Resort", "tags": ["hotel", "resort", "coastal", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pool", "restaurant", "events"], "description": "A stylish seaside resort in Pula known for its long hospitality tradition, elegant rooms and scenic setting near Marina Veruda and Marina Bunarina. It offers a quiet stay close to beaches, the aquarium and major city sights, with modern amenities such as free WiFi, parking and a pool area.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I've been here a few times, with friends and family and I've been very satisfied every time. The rooms are spacious, clean and well laid out. The breakfast is excellent with a lot of choice and a beautiful view of the marina. The staff is friendly and fantastic, to be commended for their flexibility regarding check-in and check-out and all the necessary services and information. Real value for money!", "Lovely euro boutique hotel that exceeds expectations. Great close in views of the marina from the third floor. Rooms are great, functional and have all the amenities. Very nice outdoor deck. On site Michelin restaurant is a bonus. You will have to Uber bus or drive to the Pula old town. There is a fine sea walk and beaches nearby and a few luxury hotels with nice eating options. Recommended.", "Incredible stay. We stayed for 5 nights as part of our honeymoon journey throughout Croatia. We were kindly upgraded to the 'Fuoco 1' apartment and it was superb, immaculately clean, spacious with fantastic views of the marina from the private balcony. The staff were so friendly and helpful when my wife required some medical attention for her infected insect bite they signposted us to the tourist hospital. We dined at the on-site restaurant twice because the quality of food was so good and was reasonably priced. Aperol spritz only 8€ as an example. Highly reccomended and we hope to visit again in future anniversaries."]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
10. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Modo", "tags": ["hotel", "seaside", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "restaurant"], "description": "A modern seaside hotel in Pula set between the bays of Stoja and Valovine, offering sea-view rooms with balconies, free WiFi, free parking and easy access to nearby beaches. Its quiet location and convenient connection to the city make it suitable for families, couples and business travellers.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Great little hotel in a great location. The staff is very professional and friendly. The premises are modernly decorated and clean. A rich selection of food for breakfast.", "Cosy hotel, spacious room with balcony overlooking the sea. The manager on our arrival was friendly and explained what to visit in Pula and nearby. In addition he suggested (and we went there on the last day) to visit Motovun, castle and village where you eat dishes with truffles. The breakfast of the hotel is great, varied both savory and sweet. At night absolute silence, very relaxing.", "The location was amazing ! We had a balcony that was perfect for watching the sunsets . We easily walked into town ( there also is a bus option ) the rooms were clean and comfortable . My only negative was the AC shut off randomly . The front desk said it turned off every 2 hours and needed to be reset . This was not a great for a cool night sleep without getting up a number of times to reset the AC . Breakfast was very good and it was lovely to eat out on the deck . Staff was friendly and helpful ."]}}

1. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Mozaik - Kažnjavanje Dirke", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula featuring the Roman mosaic of the Punishment of Dirce, a rare and finely preserved mythological floor mosaic discovered near St. Mary Formosa.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Kind of hard to find. You have to go around the back of the main street and through a parking lot. It almost looks like you are walking into someone's driveway. It is not well lit so if you want better pictures, go during the day.", "Very nice but looks like in a hidden area. You can follow the sign as well as use Google Maps. You may enter any time during the day at no charge.", "Absolutely go and see it - a beautifully preserved mosaic from I believe the 2nd or 3rd century AD within it's own protective room. No entry fee or anything; just observe the mosaic from street level and it is about 3-4 feet below street level. A little bit off the beaten track and the street signs aren't clear, but regardless it's a quiet and nice area so definitely make the detour."]}}
2. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
3. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Dvojna vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula with two arched passages, notable stone decoration, and direct links to some of the city’s key archaeological sites.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Nice looking arch together with the walls in the heart of Pula. Reminds me like I'm in Italy. However, it would just need to be cleaned from the black patina that has accumulated on it over time so it can look even nicer.", "Indeed, the two gates look identical. The fact that they are about a thousand years old is fascinating.", "A pair of twelfe entrances in ancient roman and mediaval Pula...but if you want to know more - hire a local licenced tour guide..."]}}
4. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
5. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Arena Pula", "tags": ["amphitheatre", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "landmark", "events", "concerts"], "description": "Roman amphitheatre from the 1st century and one of Pula’s most iconic landmarks, known for its monumental architecture, rich history, and major cultural events.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Incredibly well preserved ruins in a very cool part of town. So much to see around and inside. They also use the middle for various things. They had an ice rink there when I went.", "Pula is a small town, so seeing such a grandiose structure from the era of the great Roman Empire here is both unexpected and impressive. There are far fewer visitors than at the Roman Colosseum, so everyone has the unique opportunity to find a secluded spot, stand, and reflect on eternity, on how times, customs, and games have changed over the centuries. Don't miss the small but fascinating museum located in the arena's underground chambers—it's dedicated primarily to olive oil production in Istria.", "Gorgeous arena. A must see when in Pula. Beautiful weather helped to get some beautiful shots. More than 2000 years old and one of six biggest amphitheatres still standing.. breathtakingly stunning.", "What a site to see! Amazing roman arena built between 27–68 AD. Sixth largest in the world. There is a fee to enter and you are free to walk around once inside. There are QR codes that provide a self guided tour using your phone. Bring ear buds or headphones for the audio. This is one of the best preserved amphitheaters in the world. This is a must see."]}}
6. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
7. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Četvrt Sv. Teodora u Puli", "tags": ["board", "archaeological_site", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions", "roman"], "description": "A historic quarter in the northeastern corner of Pula’s old town, known for its exceptionally rich archaeological layers that reveal nearly 3,000 years of urban history. Excavations uncovered remains from prehistoric times, Roman temples, a domus, baths, early Christian churches and one of the largest amphora finds in the Mediterranean, making this area one of the city’s most important archaeological zones.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["A discovery of numerous remains from various cultural periods during the three-thousand-years long history of the city of Pula. They're pretty old and run down, not taller than a foot or two; only worth walking through if you're already in the area.", "A true hidden gem in the heart of Pula. The San Teodoro neighborhood is a fascinating archaeological site, where you literally walk through centuries of history: from Roman ruins to the Middle Ages, passing by the Temple of Hercules and the ancient amphorae discovered there. It's not a huge area nor overly touristy, but it's perfect for those who love archaeology and want to discover something authentic and peaceful. I recommend a guided tour to fully appreciate it!"]}}
8. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
9. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Malo rimsko kazalište", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "historic", "events", "concerts", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman theatre in the heart of Pula, dating back to the 1st century, today restored as a unique open-air archaeological site and performance venue that combines ancient heritage with contemporary cultural events.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I attended a Ludovico Einaudi concert at the Small Roman Theatre in Pula and it was amazing. The venue is intimate and historic, giving the performance a magical atmosphere. Perfect for enjoying music up close in a unique setting.", "Really not much to be seen here, just an outdoor amphitheatre that's typically empty otherwise; the route here appears a bit difficult, seems like you're walking on private property inbetween buildings.", "Awesome venue for concerts. It's best to bring your own seat cushion or pillow for comfort!"]}}
10. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Rimski mauzolej", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "ancient", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Ancient remains of an octagonal Roman mausoleum dating from the 1st century, located near the Twin Gates, the Archaeological Museum of Istria and the old city walls. Only the lower part is preserved today, but it still reflects the architectural elegance and funerary traditions of Roman Pula, making it an interesting stop for visitors exploring the city’s archaeological heritage.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["The mausoleum is actually a funerary monument, it should only be understood for this purpose. What is still visible is the base of the one used by the Romans, it being much taller, richly ornamented and placed outside the walls of the Roman city for reasons related to the legislation of the time regarding the burial of the dead. All the explanations, photographs and sketches help you understand and imagine what this construction was. Currently it is in a small park, across the road from the Gemini Gate", "This octagonal wonder from the 1st century stands as a testament to Pula's rich Roman roots. It's right by a few buildings / cafe, and beside the park - aside from the stone structure itself, not much to see or do.", "Everyone's running towards the double arch opposite... hmm... I found the octagonal mausoleum much better. Unfortunately, the explanatory plaque is missing. It's easily accessible. It's an excavation, and you're looking down at the structure from above!"]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "brunch", "salads", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Street Food Two", "phone": "+385 52 203 236", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "2A", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A modern street food spot in the city center of Pula, offers fresh, colorful, and healthier fast meals, with plenty of salads, bowls, burritos, and vegetarian options.", "reviews": ["Fresh, delicious and surprisingly versatile – highly recommended! The food was consistently fresh and top-quality – you immediately notice that they work with high-quality ingredients. The Service was super friendly, attentive and competent. We were particularly surprised by the selection of vegetarian dishes, which is really great by Croatian standards. Vegan options are also available and lovingly prepared. A place that perfectly combines pleasure, quality and hospitality.", "As a vegetarian finding healthy, vegan and vegetarian options in Croatia is simply too rare to be picky. However, this spot is simple, very nice and the food super fine. We had the tofu poke and the kids the tortellini. Everyone was happy. The staff was extremely friendly!", "Some great fresh healthy options here and amazing tasting food. We had the chickpea patties and tofu poke bowl which was so delicious! Flavours were fab & lovely staff!", "Yum, yum, yum. So fresh and cooked with love. Our first time trying this (we are new to Pula and it's close to our apartment) and it really delivered . I had the prawn and pumpkin risotto and my husband ordered the beef burrito. The taste was great and the portion large, the price reasonable for how much food you get. The service was positive and the server was smiling and happy. Quick stop, we hardly waited. We will be back. Thank you for a lovely, healthy lunch."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "healthy", "brunch", "breakfast", "international", "vegan", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kavana Lattiera", "phone": "+385 91 537 4711", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00; Sa-Su 09:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Trg Kralja Tomislava", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A modern cafe in Veruda known for specialty coffee, healthy breakfasts, smoothie bowls, homemade cakes, and a relaxed neighborhood atmosphere. Inspired by Berlin-style coffee culture, it is a popular spot for morning coffee, brunch, fresh juices, and casual meetups on the square.", "reviews": ["We stopped at Kavana Lattiera and really enjoyed the atmosphere. The coffee and desserts were excellent, and the place has a very nice vibe for sitting down and relaxing. One thing that stood out, though, was the wait time – we had to wait more than 30 minutes for our order, and it felt like we had been forgotten for a while. Once everything finally arrived, the quality made up for it, but the service could definitely be more attentive.", "Great place with a fresh and healthy offer! The menu is full of delicious options made from quality ingredients — from smoothie bowls and sandwiches to great breakfast choices. The açaí bowl is especially tasty and definitely worth trying. Perfect spot for a relaxed coffee or a healthy meal.", "During the vacation with my girlfriend (who only eats vegetarian and gluten free) in Croatia, we went a couple of times here. What a nice place and so many locals went there as well. The menu was only on Croatian and we had to translate but that was not a problem at all. The service, the food, everything is so nice here. And the best thing is, it’s open until 4 pm.", "Very interesting establishment set amongst apartments and shops. Inside it's a whole different feel to the outside and to what I have seen in Pula, which is very comforting and reminds me of other international cafes, and those special couple of cafes in Zagreb too. The food is so good, healthy and very thoughtful recipes. Veg will be happy. Oat milk available."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "kebab", "burgers", "fries", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Adi", "phone": "+385 52 383 756", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 09:00-02:00,; Sa 10:00-02:00; Su 18:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "6", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A simple city-centre fast food spot best known for its kebabs, with quick service and classic takeaway options like tortillas, burgers and fries.", "reviews": ["Food was great. Service was fast and personalized. They accommodated my food allergy. No air conditioning so its a little hot inside.", "Really good kebab, one of the best in Pula.", "Favorite kebab spot in Pula! The food is excellent, the lepinja especially is very good here. The spot is no frills takeout, but always extremely clean and very fast. Cheap too! We love Kebab Adi!"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "SWEET APARTMENT TONY", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Comfortable apartment in Pula with a terrace, balcony, free private parking, and a fully equipped kitchen, set a short drive from the Arena.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Family was help-full and kind. Even gave us a homemade cake :) We had all we needs in their apartment. Close to the apartment is shopping mall with all variety of shops. 3 min by car, maybe 10 by foot.", "Everything was perfect! The owner was super helpful and friendly! They helped us with bringing the suit see and provided everything we needed. The apartment is super well equipped and kids friendly. Supermarket, city center and beaches are nearby. The best part was AC in this hot summer! Sofa bed could be better but manageable", "Very nice apartment with big bathroom, well equipped kitchen, air conditioning in each room, large terrace."]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "MONTE ZARO", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern hostel in Pula with private bathrooms, breakfast, free parking, and a convenient location close to city attractions.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["We were here in August 2025 And it was perfect, receptionists were always nice and helpfull, the breakfast was delicious, the room was clean, new and quite nice. The location is perfect, we were 10 minutes away from the city center. So basically, i recommend this hostel to anyone, who don’t want to Pay big cash, but do want to spend time in comfort accommodation.", "Nice apartment for one night stay. Walking distance from city centre, Arena. Useful kitchen. Good value for money.", "Perfect location if you want to explore the city of Pula by foot. The room was clean and the staff was very helpful. Walls are quite thin and you can hear other people in the hall."]}}
9. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Studio 7even Ground Floor", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "free_parking"], "description": "Compact ground-floor studio apartment with a double bed, private bathroom, dining area, and equipped kitchen, suitable for a comfortable stay near beaches and the city center.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Quiet location, in a ground-floor apartment building; parking is not exclusive, but available and convenient; the owner was very kind and provided all the necessary information for our stay; the studio apartment was clean and well-equipped. Excellent value for money.", "The house is very welcoming and has everything you need. They even left us some snacks and water. All the necessary appliances are there. There are no linen changes.", "Small but well-maintained apartment. Just a few minutes' drive from the beaches and the city center."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["chinese", "asian", "meat", "seafood", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Peking", "phone": "+385 52 392 256", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "21", "addr:street": "Monte Paradiso", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A long-running Chinese restaurant, offering a broad menu of classic Chinese dishes including noodles, rice, duck, beef, pork, chicken, seafood, soups, and fried starters, with dine-in and takeout options.", "reviews": ["Staying in Pula for a few days and the restaurant is very close by, I read the reviews which are certainly mixed but thought we would give it a try. It seems that there is one guy cooking and one lady serving so we had to wait a long time for drinks and food but the food when it arrived was lovely, one of the best Chinese meals we’ve ever had. Give the place a try but expect a wait for your food! Just have a beer whilst waiting 😉", "Very good food. Good Chinese with lots of choice. Would recommend it to anyone. Nice service. The outside terrace is a bit dated and noisy due to the amount of cars that drive past so it is recommended to eat inside and it looks nice there.", "Ordered a takeaway away to be delivered. Came within 30 minutes. Nice food and very good value for money with big portions."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "burgers", "meat", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Odisej", "phone": "+385 52 223 288", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-23:00; Sa-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Arsenalska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual grill restaurant with a terrace, offering hearty meat dishes, burgers, barbecue specialties, and a comfortable setting for relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["We were welcomed the minute we sat down. Got the menus and she took the order after a few minutes of deciding what to eat. We chose the mean plate for 2. When we got it it was huge. Took some time to finish for sure. It tasted great. I can only recommend.", "First of all, best service ever! You are really friendly greated here and get all the recommendations you need from beer over food. We had the grill plate for two persons and we couldn' finish it. A lot of meat, fresh typical bread, fries and dips. You can get a taste of croatia over here! Recommended!", "Big generous portions of freshly grilled meat - exactly what you need for a traditional lunch in a place not filled with tourists."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "burgers", "meat", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Smoked", "phone": "+385 91 510 2567", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "67", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual BBQ restaurant with a terrace, offering smoked and grilled meats, burgers, ribs, steaks, vegan options, desserts, and a good selection of drinks.", "reviews": ["Amazing experience on this restaurant..the food was perfect,meat was more than impressive from the quality to the way of been cooked.service was also perfect but the food..the food was more than everything..", "Awesome place! The platter for two was super tasty and the crème brûlée was just perfect. Everything was great — definitely coming back next time we’re in Pula!", "We had a fantastic experience at Smoked Bar & BBQ in Pula. The food was outstanding – cooked to perfection, beautifully presented, and full of rich, smoky flavours. Every dish had great attention to detail and was bursting with taste. The service was equally impressive: friendly, attentive, and made the whole evening feel really relaxed and welcoming. If you’re in Pula and love quality BBQ with excellent flavours and presentation, this is definitely a spot worth visiting!"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "barbecue", "meat", "cevapi", "burgers", "brunch", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Batak", "phone": "+385 52 511 511", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 11:00-23:00; Sa 09:00.23:00; Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.5, "description": "Modern grill restaurant in Pula City Mall offering a wide range of meat dishes, steaks and comfort food in a stylish, contemporary setting.", "reviews": ["Very good food and excellent service. We had ćevapi and the stuffed pork steak. The ćevapi were juicy and well grilled, with soft lepinja. The stuffed pork steak was rich and well prepared. Homemade potatoes with melted cheese and crispy bacon were a great side. Apple tart was a solid dessert, not too sweet. Service was the highlight. Fast, professional, and friendly. Make a reservation, this place gets busy.", "Everything we had was amazing! Everything. You must do reservation over web page. Fancy but with very REASONABLE prices! Quality! I was more than surprised over the whole package! You cannot compare this prices and quality to some / most restaurants in Pula. We’ve been in Zagreb in one od your restaurants couple of years ago, but this one left us speechless. Compliments 😻👏🏻🥇", "We went in for a light meal, food was fantastic. What stands out even more was their service. Extremely friendly and kind service! We really loved the time spent there. Interiors were cozy and elegant! And in the end, they also gave a little peppa pig present for my little daughter!"], "price": "high"}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "grill", "seafood", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Galeb", "phone": "+385 52 386 361", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Su 10:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "37", "addr:street": "Osječka", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual bistro and grill restaurant serving grilled meat dishes, ćevapi, steaks, mixed platters, fried and grilled squid, whole fish, and seafood specialties.", "reviews": ["Service courteous, eat very delicious at a relatively low price and the beer is on tap. What more could you want", "The service was excellent, always there when you needed something. The food was fresh and extremely delicious, the music was nice, and the overall atmosphere was calm.", "I had the seafood pasta and it was absolutely delicious. It was a very light red cream sauce. I don’t know all the different kinds of seafood that was in it, but there was a big variety and it was delicious. I eat here on August 13 and it was quite warm outside, and I sat on the patio which is covered and shaded and has bands and wasfine to sit in. I’ll be a bit warm. Service was OK but just fine. It’s off the beaten path, so it felt not so part of the hustle and bustle with a little more private."], "price": null}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Dva ferala", "phone": "+385 52 223 365", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-21:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "32", "addr:street": "Kandlerova", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual restaurant in city center, located on the main street near the cathedral, serving grilled dishes, seafood, meat plates, and other Mediterranean-style local favorites in a relaxed setting with a terrace.", "reviews": ["We had a double fish platter . It did not disappoint. The selection was incredible. We would like to draw particular attention to the tuna. As well traveled as we are , nothing tasted like it . Incredible! My husband got a standing aviation for filleting the fish. Wine came in a tumbler , which complimented the fish beautifully. Thank you! We felt very welcome", "We went to eat there twice during the holidays, once truffle noodles and Plescavica. Both were excellent. Good draft beer, what more could you want:)", "The fish platter was excellent! Very fresh and delicious! The service was great! The drinks were good too!Highly recommended!"], "price": null}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["croatian", "local", "seafood", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Cementara", "phone": "+385 99 835 2503", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Revelanteova", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local bistro, offering affordable daily lunch menus, homemade dishes, seafood and meat specialties, and relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["Very good food and very affordable! It feels very local but there isn't a lot to see around so go there if you're on a walk. Also the waitress was very helpful and cute. 10/10 would go again", "Our accommodation was nearby, so we ended up here by chance. The tomato salad, rump steak with pepper sauce and fries (€13), and the tagliatelle with truffles (€15) were all excellent and very tasty. The prices are absolutely unbeatable. The staff is super friendly. You sit on a small terrace overlooking a parking lot. That's the only downside. Otherwise, a definite thumbs up for authentic, delicious Croatian cuisine.", "A hidden gem in the Docklands. Simple, but the food is fantastic and beautifully presented. We had grilled fish, calamari, and truffle pasta. The service was also very friendly (only Croatian spoken)."], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["vegetarian", "self_service", "daily_menu"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Biberon Fine Food", "phone": "+385 99 731 0226", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:30-18:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Šijanska cesta", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A self-service restaurant in the Konzum shopping center, offering ready-made daily meals with quick service and convenient parking.", "reviews": ["Self-service canteen with already made food. No waiting, parking available. The portions are not large and prices are not that cheap.", "Food is good, prices are fair, except for the drinks, service is just fine, soup should be with more ingredients and denser. But comparing to other places, excelent"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Ovine", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal"], "description": "Abandoned Austro-Hungarian coastal fort in the Valovine area, known for its atmospheric tunnels, overgrown walls, and striking rooftop views over the sea.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["It was a small ruin with an entrance, a hallway, some rooms and a tunnel to a small katacomb. The dark tunnel which looks like the entrance of a katacomb has a slight slope and is slippery. Unfortunately some of the rooms were used as toilets - no understanding for that... The parking lots are kind off in front of fort and very busy. So make shure to plan your visit in the morning.", "Nothing special about this place, I have only visited the exterior though. I don't know if I suggest the visit. There is a civil guard near the entrance", "A fortification overgrown in the rock. Large areas are empty and dark. For those who enjoy extreme sports, this is for you."]}}
3. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
5. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Tragovi dinosaura", "tags": ["attraction", "geopaleontological_site", "prehistoric", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A remarkable geopaleontological attraction where preserved dinosaur footprints reveal that ancient reptiles once walked this area around 130 to 100 million years ago. More than 200 footprints have been discovered across Brijuni, with visitor-accessible tracks on Veliki Brijun offering a rare and valuable glimpse into the prehistoric past.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["At first glance, nothing 'special' but when do you ever see real dinosaur footprints? I thought it was cool that they had a matching dinosaur statue next to it. If you're on the island, you should stop by there, too.", "Traces 100 million years old. Super exciting.", "It was simply amazing to see something like that. When and where else do you get the chance to admire original dinosaur footprints!? And the best part was, I was completely alone there (off-season, early June, around 5 pm), simply wonderful."]}}
6. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
10. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Punta Christo", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "underground", "events", "military_history"], "description": "Circular fort built in the late 1800s with underground rooms, also a venue for music festivals.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["chinese", "asian", "meat", "seafood", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Peking", "phone": "+385 52 392 256", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "21", "addr:street": "Monte Paradiso", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A long-running Chinese restaurant, offering a broad menu of classic Chinese dishes including noodles, rice, duck, beef, pork, chicken, seafood, soups, and fried starters, with dine-in and takeout options.", "reviews": ["Staying in Pula for a few days and the restaurant is very close by, I read the reviews which are certainly mixed but thought we would give it a try. It seems that there is one guy cooking and one lady serving so we had to wait a long time for drinks and food but the food when it arrived was lovely, one of the best Chinese meals we’ve ever had. Give the place a try but expect a wait for your food! Just have a beer whilst waiting 😉", "Very good food. Good Chinese with lots of choice. Would recommend it to anyone. Nice service. The outside terrace is a bit dated and noisy due to the amount of cars that drive past so it is recommended to eat inside and it looks nice there.", "Ordered a takeaway away to be delivered. Came within 30 minutes. Nice food and very good value for money with big portions."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "brunch", "breakfast", "burgers", "desserts", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cabahia", "phone": "+385 91 640 6330", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-24:00; Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Širolina", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-standing Veruda café recently refreshed into a snack bar, known for quality coffee, a wide beer selection, brunch dishes, burgers, bao buns, tortillas, desserts, and a relaxed local atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Great food, atmosphere, staff, and prices. I paid €12.80 for two bao buns, sweet potato fries, and a small macchiato. The other day I ordered a veggie tortilla and a hot dog with guacamole sauce via Wolt—each one better than the other. My sincere recommendation for this place!", "Currently the best snack bar in Pula, especially considering they offer a wide range of breakfast/brunch options that lean on the healthier side. The prices are also affordable and justified. The tortilla is large and excellent, the English muffin is my top choice, and the croque madame is also great. Any reviews below 4–5 stars aren’t accurate and can easily be ignored, because every time I’ve been here, it’s been even better than the previous visit.", "Excellent food, great service—an exceptionally kind and professional waiter. A warm and nicely decorated space, which is unfortunately unnecessarily crowded with tables."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["croatian", "local", "seafood", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Cementara", "phone": "+385 99 835 2503", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Revelanteova", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local bistro, offering affordable daily lunch menus, homemade dishes, seafood and meat specialties, and relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["Very good food and very affordable! It feels very local but there isn't a lot to see around so go there if you're on a walk. Also the waitress was very helpful and cute. 10/10 would go again", "Our accommodation was nearby, so we ended up here by chance. The tomato salad, rump steak with pepper sauce and fries (€13), and the tagliatelle with truffles (€15) were all excellent and very tasty. The prices are absolutely unbeatable. The staff is super friendly. You sit on a small terrace overlooking a parking lot. That's the only downside. Otherwise, a definite thumbs up for authentic, delicious Croatian cuisine.", "A hidden gem in the Docklands. Simple, but the food is fantastic and beautifully presented. We had grilled fish, calamari, and truffle pasta. The service was also very friendly (only Croatian spoken)."], "price": "low"}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Green", "phone": "+385 52 356 444", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Su 14:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot in Pula’s city center, known for burgers, toast sandwiches, tortillas, salads, and quick meals.", "reviews": ["Great service. We had a Fried Chicken Wrap which was very delicious and perfectly rolled. Even spread filling from top to bottom. Perfect place for a fast snack to go.", "We ordered a falafel and chicken wrap. Both super good quality and value for money. Also the toast were large, can easily share one for 2 kids.", "Perfect food whatever you take, for the price and quality is far ahead best place to eat in Pula. Went to few restaurants but Green is far ahead comparing quality, amount you get and prices. Nothing but best for Green.👏🏼"], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Furia Restaurant", "phone": "+385 97 683 9992", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-15:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A local seafood spot inside Pula’s market building, Furia is known for fresh, fast, and affordable fish dishes and simple Adriatic specialties.", "reviews": ["A bit spartan, but very good. Fish definitely fresh and very tasty. Friendly and friendly staff.", "Very freshly prepared, very tasty and at a more than fair price on an outdoor terrace. Highly recommended!!", "4 stars. Located on the top floor of the marketplace building. Offers seating inside the building or on the balcony. Food was nice and fresh. Understandably not everything on the menu was in season / available. We had the octopus salad and a couple of pieces of fish. Fresh and cooked well. Washed down with a lovely glass of local white wine. €30 for 2 people. Can't fault the value. Happily recommend this place.", "A place to eat fish in centre of town. They have wild fish in daly offer, as well as grown. Prices are totally acceptable. The staff is amazing, chef is encrideble! Sometimes you have to wait for the table a while, but it is completely worth it. Every time we ate here it was great 🤍🌊🌞"], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
2. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
5. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "MONTE ZARO", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern hostel in Pula with private bathrooms, breakfast, free parking, and a convenient location close to city attractions.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["We were here in August 2025 And it was perfect, receptionists were always nice and helpfull, the breakfast was delicious, the room was clean, new and quite nice. The location is perfect, we were 10 minutes away from the city center. So basically, i recommend this hostel to anyone, who don’t want to Pay big cash, but do want to spend time in comfort accommodation.", "Nice apartment for one night stay. Walking distance from city centre, Arena. Useful kitchen. Good value for money.", "Perfect location if you want to explore the city of Pula by foot. The room was clean and the staff was very helpful. Walls are quite thin and you can hear other people in the hall."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Greenhill", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "garden"], "description": "Modern one-bedroom apartment in Pula with a terrace, garden, free parking, and airport transfer, located close to the Arena and city centre.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Very nicely furnished apartment, has everything you need for a good vacation, very friendly hosts, always at hand for any questions.", "The apartment itself was equipped with everything I needed for more stay and more. It was located really close to the city which meant getting to it was no issue.", "Very nice host. I can only recommend this place. :) Thank you for everything"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
9. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}

1. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
2. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Četvrt Sv. Teodora u Puli", "tags": ["board", "archaeological_site", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions", "roman"], "description": "A historic quarter in the northeastern corner of Pula’s old town, known for its exceptionally rich archaeological layers that reveal nearly 3,000 years of urban history. Excavations uncovered remains from prehistoric times, Roman temples, a domus, baths, early Christian churches and one of the largest amphora finds in the Mediterranean, making this area one of the city’s most important archaeological zones.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["A discovery of numerous remains from various cultural periods during the three-thousand-years long history of the city of Pula. They're pretty old and run down, not taller than a foot or two; only worth walking through if you're already in the area.", "A true hidden gem in the heart of Pula. The San Teodoro neighborhood is a fascinating archaeological site, where you literally walk through centuries of history: from Roman ruins to the Middle Ages, passing by the Temple of Hercules and the ancient amphorae discovered there. It's not a huge area nor overly touristy, but it's perfect for those who love archaeology and want to discover something authentic and peaceful. I recommend a guided tour to fully appreciate it!"]}}
3. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
6. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
7. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Malo rimsko kazalište", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "historic", "events", "concerts", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman theatre in the heart of Pula, dating back to the 1st century, today restored as a unique open-air archaeological site and performance venue that combines ancient heritage with contemporary cultural events.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I attended a Ludovico Einaudi concert at the Small Roman Theatre in Pula and it was amazing. The venue is intimate and historic, giving the performance a magical atmosphere. Perfect for enjoying music up close in a unique setting.", "Really not much to be seen here, just an outdoor amphitheatre that's typically empty otherwise; the route here appears a bit difficult, seems like you're walking on private property inbetween buildings.", "Awesome venue for concerts. It's best to bring your own seat cushion or pillow for comfort!"]}}
8. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
9. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Arheološki muzej Istre", "tags": ["museum", "archeology", "historic", "city_center"], "description": "Major archaeological museum in Pula focused on Istria’s heritage, with collections and exhibitions across multiple locations while its main building is under renovation.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Learning something new is amazing. Those tunnels were built long time ago even before my grandpa's time. Just to see that things are not always what seems to be, gives you time to reflect and appreciate what you have now. History is teaching us a good lesson let's don't make the same mistake again. If visit Pula this location gives you a 360 view over the city. The Colosseum is on the East side of the fort.", "Pretty great museum if you like history and museums, there's a few rooms on the main level of the citadel. Otherwise, I'd say it's nothing special and the other levels and underground of the citadel are more fascinating.", "Hilltop fort in the center of the city. It now houses a museum dedicated, by in large to the occupation of the city, and of Croatia, in second world war. The upper levels provide for excellent view points of the city. It's not expensive to enter and worth a visit during your time in Pula."]}}
10. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "kebab", "burgers", "fries", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Adi", "phone": "+385 52 383 756", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 09:00-02:00,; Sa 10:00-02:00; Su 18:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "6", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A simple city-centre fast food spot best known for its kebabs, with quick service and classic takeaway options like tortillas, burgers and fries.", "reviews": ["Food was great. Service was fast and personalized. They accommodated my food allergy. No air conditioning so its a little hot inside.", "Really good kebab, one of the best in Pula.", "Favorite kebab spot in Pula! The food is excellent, the lepinja especially is very good here. The spot is no frills takeout, but always extremely clean and very fast. Cheap too! We love Kebab Adi!"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Nozi 7", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 05:00-23:00; We-Su 05:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A casual café at Pula’s bus station, suitable for a quick coffee, soft drink, beer, or short stop while waiting for transport.", "reviews": ["This coffee is very close to the bus station. It's clean. The service is quick. The prices are very good 👍 It is a very good place to take a coffee when waiting for your bus :)", "Took the shuttle bus from Pula airport to Pula bus station. 30 kuna (£3.30) each. 15 mins. Hour to kill before bus to heaven ( Rovinj) so popped into this lovely cafe with attached bakery opposite. First beer of the holiday. Great place to wait. Also toilet in bus station has a pay turnstile unlike here. Tabke service for drinks; go to bakery for food. Excellent value. 88Kuna / £10 for 2 coffee and 4*0.33l beers."], "price": "low"}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Green", "phone": "+385 52 356 444", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Su 14:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot in Pula’s city center, known for burgers, toast sandwiches, tortillas, salads, and quick meals.", "reviews": ["Great service. We had a Fried Chicken Wrap which was very delicious and perfectly rolled. Even spread filling from top to bottom. Perfect place for a fast snack to go.", "We ordered a falafel and chicken wrap. Both super good quality and value for money. Also the toast were large, can easily share one for 2 kids.", "Perfect food whatever you take, for the price and quality is far ahead best place to eat in Pula. Went to few restaurants but Green is far ahead comparing quality, amount you get and prices. Nothing but best for Green.👏🏼"], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "ice_cream", "coffee"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Stoja Fast Food", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot near the beach in Stoja, offering burgers, sandwiches, coffee, soft drinks, ice cream, with covered outdoor seating and sea views.", "reviews": ["Great little fast food restaurant, with very fair prices and decent choice of food, drink and ice-cream. Parking nearby (free). Had food went for a swim and returned for ice-cream and cold drink", "Best Ice cream in Pula and around. Coffee is out of this world good. Food is great as well. Very pleasent place and staff is very kind, especially young blond server. We are very frequent guests and our friends are very pleased as well.", "Amazing food, waiters came quickly the ice cream is very good, yiu cab pay by cash or card"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "burgers", "meat", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Odisej", "phone": "+385 52 223 288", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-23:00; Sa-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Arsenalska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual grill restaurant with a terrace, offering hearty meat dishes, burgers, barbecue specialties, and a comfortable setting for relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["We were welcomed the minute we sat down. Got the menus and she took the order after a few minutes of deciding what to eat. We chose the mean plate for 2. When we got it it was huge. Took some time to finish for sure. It tasted great. I can only recommend.", "First of all, best service ever! You are really friendly greated here and get all the recommendations you need from beer over food. We had the grill plate for two persons and we couldn' finish it. A lot of meat, fresh typical bread, fries and dips. You can get a taste of croatia over here! Recommended!", "Big generous portions of freshly grilled meat - exactly what you need for a traditional lunch in a place not filled with tourists."], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
6. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "brunch", "salads", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Street Food Two", "phone": "+385 52 203 236", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "2A", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A modern street food spot in the city center of Pula, offers fresh, colorful, and healthier fast meals, with plenty of salads, bowls, burritos, and vegetarian options.", "reviews": ["Fresh, delicious and surprisingly versatile – highly recommended! The food was consistently fresh and top-quality – you immediately notice that they work with high-quality ingredients. The Service was super friendly, attentive and competent. We were particularly surprised by the selection of vegetarian dishes, which is really great by Croatian standards. Vegan options are also available and lovingly prepared. A place that perfectly combines pleasure, quality and hospitality.", "As a vegetarian finding healthy, vegan and vegetarian options in Croatia is simply too rare to be picky. However, this spot is simple, very nice and the food super fine. We had the tofu poke and the kids the tortellini. Everyone was happy. The staff was extremely friendly!", "Some great fresh healthy options here and amazing tasting food. We had the chickpea patties and tofu poke bowl which was so delicious! Flavours were fab & lovely staff!", "Yum, yum, yum. So fresh and cooked with love. Our first time trying this (we are new to Pula and it's close to our apartment) and it really delivered . I had the prawn and pumpkin risotto and my husband ordered the beef burrito. The taste was great and the portion large, the price reasonable for how much food you get. The service was positive and the server was smiling and happy. Quick stop, we hardly waited. We will be back. Thank you for a lovely, healthy lunch."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "healthy", "brunch", "breakfast", "international", "vegan", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kavana Lattiera", "phone": "+385 91 537 4711", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00; Sa-Su 09:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Trg Kralja Tomislava", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A modern cafe in Veruda known for specialty coffee, healthy breakfasts, smoothie bowls, homemade cakes, and a relaxed neighborhood atmosphere. Inspired by Berlin-style coffee culture, it is a popular spot for morning coffee, brunch, fresh juices, and casual meetups on the square.", "reviews": ["We stopped at Kavana Lattiera and really enjoyed the atmosphere. The coffee and desserts were excellent, and the place has a very nice vibe for sitting down and relaxing. One thing that stood out, though, was the wait time – we had to wait more than 30 minutes for our order, and it felt like we had been forgotten for a while. Once everything finally arrived, the quality made up for it, but the service could definitely be more attentive.", "Great place with a fresh and healthy offer! The menu is full of delicious options made from quality ingredients — from smoothie bowls and sandwiches to great breakfast choices. The açaí bowl is especially tasty and definitely worth trying. Perfect spot for a relaxed coffee or a healthy meal.", "During the vacation with my girlfriend (who only eats vegetarian and gluten free) in Croatia, we went a couple of times here. What a nice place and so many locals went there as well. The menu was only on Croatian and we had to translate but that was not a problem at all. The service, the food, everything is so nice here. And the best thing is, it’s open until 4 pm.", "Very interesting establishment set amongst apartments and shops. Inside it's a whole different feel to the outside and to what I have seen in Pula, which is very comforting and reminds me of other international cafes, and those special couple of cafes in Zagreb too. The food is so good, healthy and very thoughtful recipes. Veg will be happy. Oat milk available."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "kebab", "burgers", "fries", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Adi", "phone": "+385 52 383 756", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 09:00-02:00,; Sa 10:00-02:00; Su 18:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "6", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A simple city-centre fast food spot best known for its kebabs, with quick service and classic takeaway options like tortillas, burgers and fries.", "reviews": ["Food was great. Service was fast and personalized. They accommodated my food allergy. No air conditioning so its a little hot inside.", "Really good kebab, one of the best in Pula.", "Favorite kebab spot in Pula! The food is excellent, the lepinja especially is very good here. The spot is no frills takeout, but always extremely clean and very fast. Cheap too! We love Kebab Adi!"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
4. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}
7. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
8. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
9. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": null, "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bar Cuba Libre", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "20", "addr:street": "Cesta Prekomorskih Brigada", "rating": 4.3, "description": null, "reviews": ["Very hospitable and smiling staff, pleasant tables to sit at under the shade with a view of the marina. We had iced coffee which was very good! One recommendation for the bar: please do not serve plasyic straws :)", "Delicious macchiato, comfy chairs, great service and a pretty view! Will definitely come back. My friends ordered the mojito and enjoyed It!", "A now local, already “traditional” Pula café. Great coffee, great crew, and a positive vibe. A pleasant view in both summer and winter."], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
8. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "music"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cinderela", "phone": "+385 52 540 777", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "23A", "addr:street": "Pazinska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-running café known for quality coffee, drinks, music, and a lively yet relaxed atmosphere, with regular events and a comfortable terrace.", "reviews": ["We had coffee, it was delicious. Food bought from the bakery across the street can be eaten in the café.", "Good tasting espresso, and they also have things like oat-milk for a cappuccino if you can't handle the cow milk.", "Great for a coffee break or getting with friends. My car service is nearby so I usually wait there to pick up my car."], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
10. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
9. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Titov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "events", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central waterfront park in Pula, known for its memorial monuments, shaded walking areas, city model, and lively social atmosphere with seasonal events.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Tito's Park in Pula is a prominent public park that serves as a green oasis in the heart of the city. Named after Josip Broz Tito, the former Yugoslav leader, the park is a popular area for both locals and tourists seeking relaxation and recreation. There's also a miniature model on one side of the park.", "Nice park next to the water with many busts of famous partisans, including Tito. The main monument is also dedicated to the partisans. Worth a few pictures.", "A piece of more recent Croatian history. Has some statues, a place for kids to play, a few benches and a model of the city."]}}

1. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Funcic Apartments", "tags": ["apartment", "pool", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking"], "description": null, "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["Magnificent bed and breakfast just a few kilometers from Pula. The property consists of three small apartments arranged in a horseshoe shape, with a shared pool in the center. The property also includes an American bar and a large grill. Ljuba, the owner, is very helpful and kind.", "Incredibly beautiful apartment, Ljuba is very nice. It's worth coming here; it's in a very quiet location close to the sea, only about 1.5 km away.", "Clean, comfortable, and practical accommodation. The pool is also lovely. The hostess speaks perfect Italian and is very helpful. We will definitely be back."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
5. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Greenhill", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "garden"], "description": "Modern one-bedroom apartment in Pula with a terrace, garden, free parking, and airport transfer, located close to the Arena and city centre.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Very nicely furnished apartment, has everything you need for a good vacation, very friendly hosts, always at hand for any questions.", "The apartment itself was equipped with everything I needed for more stay and more. It was located really close to the city which meant getting to it was no issue.", "Very nice host. I can only recommend this place. :) Thank you for everything"]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "SWEET APARTMENT TONY", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Comfortable apartment in Pula with a terrace, balcony, free private parking, and a fully equipped kitchen, set a short drive from the Arena.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Family was help-full and kind. Even gave us a homemade cake :) We had all we needs in their apartment. Close to the apartment is shopping mall with all variety of shops. 3 min by car, maybe 10 by foot.", "Everything was perfect! The owner was super helpful and friendly! They helped us with bringing the suit see and provided everything we needed. The apartment is super well equipped and kids friendly. Supermarket, city center and beaches are nearby. The best part was AC in this hot summer! Sofa bed could be better but manageable", "Very nice apartment with big bathroom, well equipped kitchen, air conditioning in each room, large terrace."]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["regional", "italian", "mediterranean", "meat", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Amfiteatar", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "6", "addr:street": "Amfiteatarska", "rating": 3.5, "description": null, "reviews": ["Awesome dinner experience. For starters we had beef carpaccio and Croatian pasta with truffles. For our main courses we had grilled seabass and beefsteak with truffles. Everything was awesome and the waitstaff was very attentive to our table. Everyone should stop by when they are open. You won't be disappointed.", "We enjoyed our vegan salads. The sunflower seed nuggets were really tasty. Though the actual salad was pretty boring and the menu said it came with loads of stuff it didn't (carrot, guacamole pea etc...)."], "price": null}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["chinese", "asian", "meat", "seafood", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Peking", "phone": "+385 52 392 256", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "21", "addr:street": "Monte Paradiso", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A long-running Chinese restaurant, offering a broad menu of classic Chinese dishes including noodles, rice, duck, beef, pork, chicken, seafood, soups, and fried starters, with dine-in and takeout options.", "reviews": ["Staying in Pula for a few days and the restaurant is very close by, I read the reviews which are certainly mixed but thought we would give it a try. It seems that there is one guy cooking and one lady serving so we had to wait a long time for drinks and food but the food when it arrived was lovely, one of the best Chinese meals we’ve ever had. Give the place a try but expect a wait for your food! Just have a beer whilst waiting 😉", "Very good food. Good Chinese with lots of choice. Would recommend it to anyone. Nice service. The outside terrace is a bit dated and noisy due to the amount of cars that drive past so it is recommended to eat inside and it looks nice there.", "Ordered a takeaway away to be delivered. Came within 30 minutes. Nice food and very good value for money with big portions."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "brunch", "salads", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Street Food Two", "phone": "+385 52 203 236", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "2A", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A modern street food spot in the city center of Pula, offers fresh, colorful, and healthier fast meals, with plenty of salads, bowls, burritos, and vegetarian options.", "reviews": ["Fresh, delicious and surprisingly versatile – highly recommended! The food was consistently fresh and top-quality – you immediately notice that they work with high-quality ingredients. The Service was super friendly, attentive and competent. We were particularly surprised by the selection of vegetarian dishes, which is really great by Croatian standards. Vegan options are also available and lovingly prepared. A place that perfectly combines pleasure, quality and hospitality.", "As a vegetarian finding healthy, vegan and vegetarian options in Croatia is simply too rare to be picky. However, this spot is simple, very nice and the food super fine. We had the tofu poke and the kids the tortellini. Everyone was happy. The staff was extremely friendly!", "Some great fresh healthy options here and amazing tasting food. We had the chickpea patties and tofu poke bowl which was so delicious! Flavours were fab & lovely staff!", "Yum, yum, yum. So fresh and cooked with love. Our first time trying this (we are new to Pula and it's close to our apartment) and it really delivered . I had the prawn and pumpkin risotto and my husband ordered the beef burrito. The taste was great and the portion large, the price reasonable for how much food you get. The service was positive and the server was smiling and happy. Quick stop, we hardly waited. We will be back. Thank you for a lovely, healthy lunch."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "italian", "seafood", "pasta", "pizza", "grill", "burgers", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Old City", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual restaurant in the center of Pula offering a wide variety of dishes, including seafood, grilled meat, burgers, pasta, pizza, salads, and vegetarian options. It is a good choice for both full meals and drinks, with a menu that combines local Istrian flavors, fish specialties, and classic international dishes.", "reviews": ["Food is excellent 😊 staff are super friendly and the atmosphere is great 🙋‍♀️🌸 and Spezial orders are no problem 😂😂 we tried nearly the whole Menü between all of us and we recommend it all …… we still say all the above …. But hier too the prices have exploded since the Euro !!!!!", "Awesome place for lunch. The food was delicious, the staff was really great, the location is excellent. If you're in Pula, please visit Old City Bar - you won't be disappointed."], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "italian", "seafood", "pasta", "meat", "salads", "desserts", "wine", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Alighieri", "phone": "+385 52 381 984", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-22:30; Sa-Su 12:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual bistro in Pula’s old town with a central square terrace, serves Mediterranean and Istrian dishes, daily lunch menus, fish, meat, pasta and salads in a relaxed city setting.", "reviews": ["A lovely little bistro near the fountain square. We had a wonderful lunch here and tried the traditional noodles with truffle sauce - absolutely delicious. We also ordered Istrian red wine, which I can definitely recommend. The staff were lovely and the service was ok. The atmosphere was good.", "This platter was delicious and beautifully presented. The mix of cheeses, cured meats, olives, and fresh tomatoes was perfect. Everything tasted fresh and well-balanced, and the crunchy breadsticks added a nice touch. A great appetizer to share — simple, tasty, and satisfying.", "Absolutely amazing food and service at Bistro Alighieri in Pula! We enjoyed perfectly cooked calamari, baby octopus, and the local pasta Pljukanci with creamy truffle sauce. The tuna cappuccio starter and Croatian wine made it a perfect evening. Highly recommended!", "The best Cuttlefish Risotto I've ever tasted. It was so good, I forgot to photograph it. The restaurant service is great, food is hot and freshly cooked. Serving staff are friendly. This is a restaurant where the food quality speaks for itself. Nice prices, excellent food. Simple"], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Dva ferala", "phone": "+385 52 223 365", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-21:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "32", "addr:street": "Kandlerova", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual restaurant in city center, located on the main street near the cathedral, serving grilled dishes, seafood, meat plates, and other Mediterranean-style local favorites in a relaxed setting with a terrace.", "reviews": ["We had a double fish platter . It did not disappoint. The selection was incredible. We would like to draw particular attention to the tuna. As well traveled as we are , nothing tasted like it . Incredible! My husband got a standing aviation for filleting the fish. Wine came in a tumbler , which complimented the fish beautifully. Thank you! We felt very welcome", "We went to eat there twice during the holidays, once truffle noodles and Plescavica. Both were excellent. Good draft beer, what more could you want:)", "The fish platter was excellent! Very fresh and delicious! The service was great! The drinks were good too!Highly recommended!"], "price": null}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
6. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
4. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}
7. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
8. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
9. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
2. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
3. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
5. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "MONTE ZARO", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern hostel in Pula with private bathrooms, breakfast, free parking, and a convenient location close to city attractions.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["We were here in August 2025 And it was perfect, receptionists were always nice and helpfull, the breakfast was delicious, the room was clean, new and quite nice. The location is perfect, we were 10 minutes away from the city center. So basically, i recommend this hostel to anyone, who don’t want to Pay big cash, but do want to spend time in comfort accommodation.", "Nice apartment for one night stay. Walking distance from city centre, Arena. Useful kitchen. Good value for money.", "Perfect location if you want to explore the city of Pula by foot. The room was clean and the staff was very helpful. Walls are quite thin and you can hear other people in the hall."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Greenhill", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "garden"], "description": "Modern one-bedroom apartment in Pula with a terrace, garden, free parking, and airport transfer, located close to the Arena and city centre.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Very nicely furnished apartment, has everything you need for a good vacation, very friendly hosts, always at hand for any questions.", "The apartment itself was equipped with everything I needed for more stay and more. It was located really close to the city which meant getting to it was no issue.", "Very nice host. I can only recommend this place. :) Thank you for everything"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
9. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "meat", "vegetarian", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Epulon Food & Wine", "phone": "+385 98 949 9023", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Epulonova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A stylish wine and food bar in central Pula, Epulon combines traditional Istrian cuisine with seasonal, more refined dishes, with a strong focus on local ingredients, wines, tapas, and a relaxed indoor terrace setting.", "reviews": ["Hospitality was excellent. Service and food was delicious. I felt like at home.", "Great restaurant, food was delicious and very friendly stuff...", "The place is spectacular for an outing of any kind. The atmosphere is very nice and refined. The furniture, the sweetness of the wench... all perfect. Good prices.", "Absolutely LOVED the place! The waitress was lovely, easy to talk to and helped me pick exactly what I wanted. I came back the second time because of her:) The food was delicious and nicely served. I didn't have to wait much. The atmosphere, music - everything was great. This place is a hidden gem, recommend to those who'd like to eat and relax 💎"], "price": "high"}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
5. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "brunch", "burgers", "music", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "The Shipyard Pub", "phone": "+385 91 181 0630", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 08:00-02:00; Fr 08:00-03:00; Sa 10:00-03:00; Su 10:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Svetog Teodora", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Lively pub on the Riva with burgers, pub food, cocktails, beer, and a spacious terrace. A popular evening spot known for music, DJ sets, quiz nights, and other events in a casual, social atmosphere.", "reviews": ["We stayed here once for a drink and once for dinner. The Service was fast, friendly and accommodating in both cases. The Aperol Spritz was just as delicious as the burgers. These were juicy with very tasty sauces and the caramelized onions rounded it off with a great taste. The fries were also well seasoned and perfectly crispy. The dressing of the ceasar salad was a bit unusual and not quite typical but also incredibly delicious, we would love to come back. Value for money was also reasonable, so what more could you want.", "Friendly and efficient staff with delicious food. The burger was very good and my wife really enjoyed the noodles. Worth a stop. Plenty of seating inside and the vibes were relaxing.", "Great little bar in the heart of Pula! The atmosphere is warm and relaxed, and the staff were incredibly friendly. The music was just right for chatting without shouting, and prices were very reasonable compared to other spots in town. Perfect place to stop for a drink after sightseeing. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a cozy and authentic bar experience in Pula"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "pasta", "cocktails", "coffee", "desserts", "wine"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Yacht Restaurant & Lounge Bar", "phone": "+385 91 633 3359", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 10:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "17", "addr:street": "Verudela", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A stylish seaside bar and restaurant in a tourist resort in Pula, set by the hotels and the sea, offering local and international dishes, drinks, coffee, and desserts.", "reviews": ["Great place with lovely food and cocktails and a great view. We always managed to secure a table without a reservation and staff were helpful", "We enjoyed this restaurant so much that we returned a few nights later to try it again. The views are spectacular. The food was delicious and the staff were friendly and knowledgeable about the food and wine. The only downside was the toilets were a bit grubby.", "Lovely little restaurant overlooking the sea and surrounding area in Pula. Firstly the staff and service was excellent! Everyone was so welcoming, our waiter had brilliant recommendations which we went for and the food was so good! The local white wine was so nice too! Desert and coffees were also lovely of course and the view from our table was awesome! We had a really lovely evening which was made better by the staff and the setting. Thank you all!"], "price": "high"}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "pasta", "wine", "cocktails", "hotel_restaurant"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Vela Nera", "phone": "+385 52 300 620", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "3b", "addr:street": "Franje Mošnja", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A stylish hotel restaurant in Šišan near Pula, serving Mediterranean and Istrian cuisine, local wines, cocktails, business lunches, and catering in an elegant setting.", "reviews": ["Everything was impressive, we stayed for a couple of days and we had a really good time. In addition the food from the breakfast and the restaurant was delicious with an excellent presentation. Finally, the staff was super friendly and really professional!", "This is a gem! A great family run hotel with amazing food. The service is just wonderful with an attitude that makes everything possible. I stayed 8 nights in a very spacious super clean room. I enjoyed the pool and the fabulous food. It was truly a home away from home. For me the location was great, easy drives into the main tourist areas for work while I could enjoy the off the beaten track feel of the calm village. I am hoping to go back for leisure with my family.", "Went for food as part of our wedding anniversary celebrations. The service was fantastic, the food was absolutely brilliant. We had beef steak and tuna steak which were both cooked to perfection. The deserts were wonderful, apple strudel and a chocolate souffle. Great evening in a fantastic setting to watch the sun go down over a tasty bottle of wine which was superbly recommended by our waiter."], "price": "high"}}
8. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar San Antonio", "phone": "+385 98 924 4222", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "24", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 3.1, "description": "A casual café bar set directly above the Pula Arena, known for its terrace with a unique view of the amphitheatre. It serves coffee, beer, soft drinks, ice cream, and other classic café-bar refreshments in a relaxed open-air setting.", "reviews": ["Aperol Spritz are the best in Pula! Ice cream are just melting in mouth. The view is amazing", "Best view, good coffee", "Good coffee. Waitress semi friendly"], "price": "high"}}
9. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
10. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}

1. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
2. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
5. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}

1. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "Dječje igralište Viška ulica", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Neighbourhood playground in Pula with basic play equipment, a fenced play area, and a family-friendly setting near Fort Casoni Vecchi and St. Paul’s Church.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
6. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "SWEET APARTMENT TONY", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Comfortable apartment in Pula with a terrace, balcony, free private parking, and a fully equipped kitchen, set a short drive from the Arena.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Family was help-full and kind. Even gave us a homemade cake :) We had all we needs in their apartment. Close to the apartment is shopping mall with all variety of shops. 3 min by car, maybe 10 by foot.", "Everything was perfect! The owner was super helpful and friendly! They helped us with bringing the suit see and provided everything we needed. The apartment is super well equipped and kids friendly. Supermarket, city center and beaches are nearby. The best part was AC in this hot summer! Sofa bed could be better but manageable", "Very nice apartment with big bathroom, well equipped kitchen, air conditioning in each room, large terrace."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park žrtava fašizma", "tags": ["park", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Neighbourhood park in Šijana, Pula, with a children’s playground, benches, and a pleasant green space for everyday relaxation.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "burgers", "meat", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Odisej", "phone": "+385 52 223 288", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-23:00; Sa-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Arsenalska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual grill restaurant with a terrace, offering hearty meat dishes, burgers, barbecue specialties, and a comfortable setting for relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["We were welcomed the minute we sat down. Got the menus and she took the order after a few minutes of deciding what to eat. We chose the mean plate for 2. When we got it it was huge. Took some time to finish for sure. It tasted great. I can only recommend.", "First of all, best service ever! You are really friendly greated here and get all the recommendations you need from beer over food. We had the grill plate for two persons and we couldn' finish it. A lot of meat, fresh typical bread, fries and dips. You can get a taste of croatia over here! Recommended!", "Big generous portions of freshly grilled meat - exactly what you need for a traditional lunch in a place not filled with tourists."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "grill", "seafood", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Galeb", "phone": "+385 52 386 361", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Su 10:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "37", "addr:street": "Osječka", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual bistro and grill restaurant serving grilled meat dishes, ćevapi, steaks, mixed platters, fried and grilled squid, whole fish, and seafood specialties.", "reviews": ["Service courteous, eat very delicious at a relatively low price and the beer is on tap. What more could you want", "The service was excellent, always there when you needed something. The food was fresh and extremely delicious, the music was nice, and the overall atmosphere was calm.", "I had the seafood pasta and it was absolutely delicious. It was a very light red cream sauce. I don’t know all the different kinds of seafood that was in it, but there was a big variety and it was delicious. I eat here on August 13 and it was quite warm outside, and I sat on the patio which is covered and shaded and has bands and wasfine to sit in. I’ll be a bit warm. Service was OK but just fine. It’s off the beaten path, so it felt not so part of the hustle and bustle with a little more private."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "grill", "meat", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Dva ferala", "phone": "+385 52 223 365", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-21:00; Sa-Su 09:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "32", "addr:street": "Kandlerova", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual restaurant in city center, located on the main street near the cathedral, serving grilled dishes, seafood, meat plates, and other Mediterranean-style local favorites in a relaxed setting with a terrace.", "reviews": ["We had a double fish platter . It did not disappoint. The selection was incredible. We would like to draw particular attention to the tuna. As well traveled as we are , nothing tasted like it . Incredible! My husband got a standing aviation for filleting the fish. Wine came in a tumbler , which complimented the fish beautifully. Thank you! We felt very welcome", "We went to eat there twice during the holidays, once truffle noodles and Plescavica. Both were excellent. Good draft beer, what more could you want:)", "The fish platter was excellent! Very fresh and delicious! The service was great! The drinks were good too!Highly recommended!"], "price": null}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "burgers", "meat", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Smoked", "phone": "+385 91 510 2567", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "67", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual BBQ restaurant with a terrace, offering smoked and grilled meats, burgers, ribs, steaks, vegan options, desserts, and a good selection of drinks.", "reviews": ["Amazing experience on this restaurant..the food was perfect,meat was more than impressive from the quality to the way of been cooked.service was also perfect but the food..the food was more than everything..", "Awesome place! The platter for two was super tasty and the crème brûlée was just perfect. Everything was great — definitely coming back next time we’re in Pula!", "We had a fantastic experience at Smoked Bar & BBQ in Pula. The food was outstanding – cooked to perfection, beautifully presented, and full of rich, smoky flavours. Every dish had great attention to detail and was bursting with taste. The service was equally impressive: friendly, attentive, and made the whole evening feel really relaxed and welcoming. If you’re in Pula and love quality BBQ with excellent flavours and presentation, this is definitely a spot worth visiting!"], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["vegetarian", "self_service", "daily_menu"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Biberon Fine Food", "phone": "+385 99 731 0226", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:30-18:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Šijanska cesta", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A self-service restaurant in the Konzum shopping center, offering ready-made daily meals with quick service and convenient parking.", "reviews": ["Self-service canteen with already made food. No waiting, parking available. The portions are not large and prices are not that cheap.", "Food is good, prices are fair, except for the drinks, service is just fine, soup should be with more ingredients and denser. But comparing to other places, excelent"], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Valkane", "phone": "+385 52 387 589", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Lungomare", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant on the Lungomare promenade, next to the tennis courts, serving Croatian and Istrian cuisine with terrace seating.", "reviews": ["We had some of the best food in Croatia at this restaurant, it was amazing. We had tuna steak and calamari which were both amazing!! The service was sensational as well, the waitress even offered her jacket to me as the breeze was a bit cool. I could recommend this restaurant highly enough based on our experience.", "One of the best places to eat! The food is fresh and absolutely fantastic, the atmosphere is wonderful,good price and Marijana is truly the best waitress in all of Europe. Thank you for everything! See you next year❤️", "Lovely restaurant, one of the few in the area with waterfront location. Popular with locals and tourist, great food at reasonable prices. Black rice seafood risotto, and meat plate (mixed grill) were really nice."], "price": null}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["croatian", "local", "seafood", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Cementara", "phone": "+385 99 835 2503", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Revelanteova", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local bistro, offering affordable daily lunch menus, homemade dishes, seafood and meat specialties, and relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["Very good food and very affordable! It feels very local but there isn't a lot to see around so go there if you're on a walk. Also the waitress was very helpful and cute. 10/10 would go again", "Our accommodation was nearby, so we ended up here by chance. The tomato salad, rump steak with pepper sauce and fries (€13), and the tagliatelle with truffles (€15) were all excellent and very tasty. The prices are absolutely unbeatable. The staff is super friendly. You sit on a small terrace overlooking a parking lot. That's the only downside. Otherwise, a definite thumbs up for authentic, delicious Croatian cuisine.", "A hidden gem in the Docklands. Simple, but the food is fantastic and beautifully presented. We had grilled fish, calamari, and truffle pasta. The service was also very friendly (only Croatian spoken)."], "price": "low"}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "LABIRINT MUDROSTI I ZNANJA", "tags": ["attraction", "labyrinth", "meditative", "nature", "stone"], "description": "Stone labyrinth in Šijanska šuma designed for contemplative walking and a symbolic experience associated with wisdom, learning, clarity, and personal growth.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
2. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "LABIRINT ENERGIJE", "tags": ["attraction", "labyrinth", "meditative", "nature", "stone"], "description": "Stone labyrinth in Šijanska šuma designed for mindful walking, relaxation, and an energy-focused symbolic experience in nature.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "LABIRINT MOĆI", "tags": ["attraction", "labyrinth", "meditative", "nature", "stone"], "description": "Stone labyrinth in Šijanska šuma designed for reflective walking, relaxation, and a symbolic experience connected with strength, focus, and inner balance.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "LABIRINT POVEZANOSTI", "tags": ["attraction", "labyrinth", "meditative", "nature", "stone"], "description": "Stone labyrinth in Šijanska šuma intended for reflective walking and a symbolic experience of connection, understanding, and calm in a forest environment.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
6. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "LABIRINT OSJEĆAJA", "tags": ["attraction", "labyrinth", "meditative", "nature", "stone"], "description": "Stone labyrinth in Šijanska šuma designed for reflective walking and a symbolic experience connected with emotions, sensitivity, calmness, and inner harmony.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
9. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Karmen", "tags": ["hotel", "national_park", "island", "historic", "coastal", "near_beach", "family_friendly"], "description": "Historic seaside guesthouse on Veliki Brijun, offering simple rooms with park or sea views, old-world charm, and a peaceful stay in Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 3.9, "reviews": ["This island is beautiful and has a sense of peace, even on August 15th! The property still has its 1960s furnishings, but it's clean and charming. The terrace overlooking the sea is truly beautiful and relaxing. It's true that there's no air conditioning or mini-bar, but they provided us with a couple of fans, and we managed just fine. What can I say? The island is so beautiful, it's absolutely worth it.", "Wonderful, spacious rooms, just the right amount of nostalgia. In fact, everything is reminiscent of the 60s and 70s and I think it really is from that era, except for the beds, which are new and very comfortable. Again, it's kind of logical that it should stay that way. Everything is very clean. Breakfast is perfect. Staff is very friendly.", "Great view from the balcony, 70s flair – anyone who embraces that will enjoy a lovely and relaxing holiday. Clean and the room is cleaned daily. The only drawback is the lack of air conditioning. The buffet food at Hotel Neptun is excellent."]}}
10. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
6. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Hum", "phone": "+385 97 774 5221", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-15:00; Sa 07:00-14:00; Su 07:00-13:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Fontička", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A family-run cafe in the city center, popular for morning coffee and casual drinks.", "reviews": ["Best coffee we had in Pula and our trip in Croatia! Decaf coffee was also excellent. We went every morning of our stay after breakfast. The service was really good too. The two men servers were very kind and by the 3rd day knew our order and asked if we wanted our usual! Highly recommend!", "Great spot for a quick coffee, and it was not a bad one which is great. Normal price, quick service and lots of spots to seat. Yes to this place.", "Sat down and had coffee after visiting the market nearby. Clean toilets, good coffee (also decaf options), friendly service! The shaded terrace helped with the heat 😊."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "desserts", "ice_cream"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Barbados", "phone": "+385 99 349 0555", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-22:00; Su 07:30-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "14A", "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A relaxed cafe in Max City shopping center, ideal for short breaks, long coffee sessions, and casual meetups. With a sunny terrace and laid-back atmosphere, it is a nice place to enjoy coffee, drinks, or a quiet moment with a book or newspaper.", "reviews": ["Great spot for coffee, they also have a fantastic cake selection, I like to come here every time I'm at the mall. The staff is very kind, especially the young female waiter and the young male waiter, both so so kind. I reccomand this spot to anyone passing through, by far the best coffee in the mall", "Great service. Katarina was very helpful and kind. 5/5", "They have real milkshakes made with any flavor ice cream they have! Wonderful"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "music"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cinderela", "phone": "+385 52 540 777", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "23A", "addr:street": "Pazinska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-running café known for quality coffee, drinks, music, and a lively yet relaxed atmosphere, with regular events and a comfortable terrace.", "reviews": ["We had coffee, it was delicious. Food bought from the bakery across the street can be eaten in the café.", "Good tasting espresso, and they also have things like oat-milk for a cappuccino if you can't handle the cow milk.", "Great for a coffee break or getting with friends. My car service is nearby so I usually wait there to pick up my car."], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "mediterranean", "coffee", "beer", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Diana", "phone": "+385 98 915 4270", "opening_hours": "Mo-We 08:00-01:00; Th 08:00-24:00; Fr 08:00-01:00; Sa 08:00-24:00; Su 08:00-23:30", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Café on Pula’s Forum square with a large terrace, classic coffee-and-drinks offer, and a prime spot for sitting right in the heart of the old town.", "reviews": ["Nice café in the center of Pula. Basic coffee options but good quality and reasonably priced. Pleasant spot for a quick break.", "Nice little café with reasonable prices. Their ice coffee tastes nice.", "I highly recommend this bar, service was extremly fast and our waitress was very kind. Great location and great drinks. I’ll definitely return."], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "sandwiches", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Leggiero", "phone": "+385 52 634 385", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 08:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 3.4, "description": "A modern coffee bar and snack spot in Pula City Mall, offering quality coffee, fresh juices, sandwiches, cakes and sweet treats, ideal for a relaxed coffee break while shopping.", "reviews": ["Very expensive place to drink a coffe! Really too much! A price of a coffee in a supermarket must be more cheaper than one in the centre of the city…excessively!!!", "A very relaxing place whether you sit inside or outside on the terrace, with an excellent selection of food and drinks and outstanding, dedicated staff—especially the waiter Dylan, who is very fast, helpful, friendly, and fully committed to guests at all times, regardless of the crowd and high turnover of people!", "The coffee is average, but definitely not worth €2.90. I’ve had much better coffee for less money. Judging by other reviews, I’m clearly not the only one who thinks the quality doesn’t justify the price.", "Always smiling, helpful, and quick, even when dealing with guests who can be very rude and impatient. Kudos to them for their patience—they truly make an effort and give their best to do the job as well as possible. Highly recommended!"], "price": "high"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "coffee", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar Nozi 7", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Tu 05:00-23:00; We-Su 05:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A casual café at Pula’s bus station, suitable for a quick coffee, soft drink, beer, or short stop while waiting for transport.", "reviews": ["This coffee is very close to the bus station. It's clean. The service is quick. The prices are very good 👍 It is a very good place to take a coffee when waiting for your bus :)", "Took the shuttle bus from Pula airport to Pula bus station. 30 kuna (£3.30) each. 15 mins. Hour to kill before bus to heaven ( Rovinj) so popped into this lovely cafe with attached bakery opposite. First beer of the holiday. Great place to wait. Also toilet in bus station has a pay turnstile unlike here. Tabke service for drinks; go to bakery for food. Excellent value. 88Kuna / £10 for 2 coffee and 4*0.33l beers."], "price": "low"}}
7. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}
8. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "coffee", "gallery", "cocktails", "ice_cream", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cvajner", "phone": "+385 52 216 502", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-23:00; Su 10:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 4.3, "description": "Art café and gallery on Pula’s main square, known for its striking historic interior, artistic atmosphere, and terrace overlooking the Forum and the Temple of Augustus.", "reviews": ["Great place to get some coffee and quick food; located right in Forum Square, so finding this place is super simple. Service could be a bit better and more organized, but otherwise everything was super tasty.", "Very nice iced coffee. Cozy enviroment, interesting design with restored paintings on the walls.", "This is in a great location if you sit outside. The Forum has a great buzz and is beautiful. Prices are quite reasonable for such a location (big draught beer €4.2) Most of the staff are busy and seem a bit a bit grumpy ( except one nice waitress) There are small menus on the tables and bills are clearly itemised. We saw a family leave after waiting ages to be served. Inside looks nice too with some old frescos. Locals here too. Worth a visit though.", "Gorgeous and cosy caffe... Well preserved historical charm done by keeping the original tapestry and blending it in with the new one. Drinks are well made and the staff is polite, very nice place to come to on a rainy day."], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "desserts", "gluten_free", "vegan"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cafe Frei", "phone": null, "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-21:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Jurja Žakna", "rating": 4.6, "description": "An international coffee bar located in the Kaufland complex and known for a wide range of world-inspired coffee drinks, teas, smoothies, cakes, and take-away options.", "reviews": ["This has become my regular spot for a morning coffee. The coffee is really good (regular, haven’t tried with alternative milks etc.), and they have some variations too. Oit of those I tried a few and they were also amazing. My kid had hot chocolate and it was delicious. I can only but recommend.", "One of the best coffee you can drink in Pula town. The one on the picture is the matcha pistacchio, very delicious. Service and waitress are top of the tops. Very nice looking place, good atmosphere, calm and tidy. You can choose between a variety of coffee, ice cream and desserts. I am very satisfied and can only recommend it. Go for it, 5 stars!", "Absolutely amazing service and coffee to die for. I've been coming to Pula for years on end. I'm yet to find better tasting coffee."], "price": "low"}}
10. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar San Antonio", "phone": "+385 98 924 4222", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "24", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 3.1, "description": "A casual café bar set directly above the Pula Arena, known for its terrace with a unique view of the amphitheatre. It serves coffee, beer, soft drinks, ice cream, and other classic café-bar refreshments in a relaxed open-air setting.", "reviews": ["Aperol Spritz are the best in Pula! Ice cream are just melting in mouth. The view is amazing", "Best view, good coffee", "Good coffee. Waitress semi friendly"], "price": "high"}}

1. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
2. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park žrtava fašizma", "tags": ["park", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Neighbourhood park in Šijana, Pula, with a children’s playground, benches, and a pleasant green space for everyday relaxation.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
10. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "Dječje igralište Viška ulica", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Neighbourhood playground in Pula with basic play equipment, a fenced play area, and a family-friendly setting near Fort Casoni Vecchi and St. Paul’s Church.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Amfiteatar", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "Boutique hotel in central Pula, just steps from the Arena, offering modern rooms, a well-known restaurant, and easy access to the old town and waterfront.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel, great location, very central. Lovely staff and extremely helpful with suggestions to eat and drink and booking a taxi to the airport. Room 101 was great, really spacious with bathrobes and slippers. Tea and coffee making facilities in the room. Great choice of both hot and cold food at breakfast. Would definitely stay again.", "I can’t get over what a great place this is! Location of course, front desk service, comfort, and value. I would highly recommend this facility for any type of visit to Pula.", "Great experience staying here! Location is superb and the staff is super friendly. We accidentally broke the tap in the bathroom while staying here, but the hotel staff just exchanged it during the day and it was fixed when we got back in the afternoon. Would definitely recommend staying here!"]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
3. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "regional", "istrian", "pasta", "grill", "meat", "seafood"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Konoba Veruda", "phone": "+385 52 721 302", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 11:00-22:00; Su 11:00-17:00", "addr:housenumber": "27", "addr:street": "Tomasinijeva", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A traditional tavern in Veruda serving authentic Istrian cuisine in a warm, rustic setting. The menu focuses on homemade pasta, goulash, grilled meat, seafood, truffle dishes, and other local specialties, making it a great place to try classic regional food.", "reviews": ["The atmosphere of the place, ambient, and friendliness of our waitress was so wonderful. But even more impressive was the amazing food! Marvelous experience", "We took a chance on this place and were completely blown away by the quality and quantity of food. Our final dinner in Pula before heading home was amazing. The steaks and fish dishes are superior and everything prepared with care and attention. The mangold side (which we thought was spinach) is devine. We were treated to free shots of the home-brewed liquor before leaving. Fabulous!", "If you're visiting Pula and looking for a spot with great service, generous portions, and good value for money, this restaurant is a must-try. Conveniently located near our hotel, it offered a welcoming atmosphere. While it's not within walking distance of the city center, it's easily accessible via bus 2A, taking only about 10-15 minutes. The food was delicious, with portions larger than expected, making it perfect for those with a hearty appetite. Overall, this place combines quality dining with affordability, making it a top recommendation for anyone visiting Pula."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Scaletta", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "free_parking", "near_attractions"], "description": "Quaint hotel in central Pula near the Arena, offering comfortable rooms, breakfast, parking, and easy access to the city’s historic sights.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Small hotel ,central -5' from the amphitheater ,10' from the historic center of the pleasant town of Pula to walk along the tree-lined Rambla between arches small squares churches from the soaring bell towers to the port.Like the city - bright clean and cozy -so the small hotel in retro style ', slightly French proves safe and fulfilling. It is true that the external stairs lead to the familiar reception and that breakfast is served on the room overlooking the street, -I think a former very chic restaurant whose dishes and crockery now serve an essential breakfast - but the pleasure is given by the central heart just a stone's throw from the Colosseum, magnificent!", "We cannot thank the lovely owners enough for all their help with finding a car for us yesterday. The hotel is a real find and value for money and close to the ferry and the city centre. Lovely breakfast also."]}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Hostel Joyce", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "historic"], "description": "Boutique hostel in the heart of Pula, set beside the Arch of the Sergii and known for its modern rooms, historic character, and walkable location.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wonderful hotel with modern rooms, comfortable beds, spectacular views and an unbeatable location. Staff was warm and inviting and had everything prepared for us. Check in and check out was a breeze! Much more affordable than other 4- star hotels in comparable tourist-centric cities (especially during seasonal rush). Will definitely return.", "I strongly recommend this hotel: my room was large and clean, Nikola, the boy at the reception desk, was very helpful. Furthermore, guests have a 20 % discount at the adjacent restaurant!", "Despite the room being quite small, it was ideal for an overnight stay, was reasonably priced and in a fantastic location. The staff were incredibly friendly and helpful. The room was very clean, quiet and comfortable (the AC was very welcome!). It's in the perfect location to see all the main sights and is also a short walk from restaurants, bars and a bus stop. Thanks for a lovely stay!", "I would describe the hotel accommodation as practical, picturesque and modern. Our room was quite small but it was absolutely everything we needed. The bed was very comfortable, the air conditioning was very welcome and the view from the window was of the Triumphal Arch. The hotel is in the centre of Pula, so it is a short walk to the sights, good food and the bus stop to the beach or the station. There is also a great restaurant downstairs for brunch. Thank you very much, the stay was wonderful."]}}
8. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
9. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
2. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
3. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Četvrt Sv. Teodora u Puli", "tags": ["board", "archaeological_site", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions", "roman"], "description": "A historic quarter in the northeastern corner of Pula’s old town, known for its exceptionally rich archaeological layers that reveal nearly 3,000 years of urban history. Excavations uncovered remains from prehistoric times, Roman temples, a domus, baths, early Christian churches and one of the largest amphora finds in the Mediterranean, making this area one of the city’s most important archaeological zones.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["A discovery of numerous remains from various cultural periods during the three-thousand-years long history of the city of Pula. They're pretty old and run down, not taller than a foot or two; only worth walking through if you're already in the area.", "A true hidden gem in the heart of Pula. The San Teodoro neighborhood is a fascinating archaeological site, where you literally walk through centuries of history: from Roman ruins to the Middle Ages, passing by the Temple of Hercules and the ancient amphorae discovered there. It's not a huge area nor overly touristy, but it's perfect for those who love archaeology and want to discover something authentic and peaceful. I recommend a guided tour to fully appreciate it!"]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Mozaik - Kažnjavanje Dirke", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula featuring the Roman mosaic of the Punishment of Dirce, a rare and finely preserved mythological floor mosaic discovered near St. Mary Formosa.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Kind of hard to find. You have to go around the back of the main street and through a parking lot. It almost looks like you are walking into someone's driveway. It is not well lit so if you want better pictures, go during the day.", "Very nice but looks like in a hidden area. You can follow the sign as well as use Google Maps. You may enter any time during the day at no charge.", "Absolutely go and see it - a beautifully preserved mosaic from I believe the 2nd or 3rd century AD within it's own protective room. No entry fee or anything; just observe the mosaic from street level and it is about 3-4 feet below street level. A little bit off the beaten track and the street signs aren't clear, but regardless it's a quiet and nice area so definitely make the detour."]}}
5. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
6. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Malo rimsko kazalište", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "historic", "events", "concerts", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman theatre in the heart of Pula, dating back to the 1st century, today restored as a unique open-air archaeological site and performance venue that combines ancient heritage with contemporary cultural events.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I attended a Ludovico Einaudi concert at the Small Roman Theatre in Pula and it was amazing. The venue is intimate and historic, giving the performance a magical atmosphere. Perfect for enjoying music up close in a unique setting.", "Really not much to be seen here, just an outdoor amphitheatre that's typically empty otherwise; the route here appears a bit difficult, seems like you're walking on private property inbetween buildings.", "Awesome venue for concerts. It's best to bring your own seat cushion or pillow for comfort!"]}}
7. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Rimski mauzolej", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "ancient", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Ancient remains of an octagonal Roman mausoleum dating from the 1st century, located near the Twin Gates, the Archaeological Museum of Istria and the old city walls. Only the lower part is preserved today, but it still reflects the architectural elegance and funerary traditions of Roman Pula, making it an interesting stop for visitors exploring the city’s archaeological heritage.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["The mausoleum is actually a funerary monument, it should only be understood for this purpose. What is still visible is the base of the one used by the Romans, it being much taller, richly ornamented and placed outside the walls of the Roman city for reasons related to the legislation of the time regarding the burial of the dead. All the explanations, photographs and sketches help you understand and imagine what this construction was. Currently it is in a small park, across the road from the Gemini Gate", "This octagonal wonder from the 1st century stands as a testament to Pula's rich Roman roots. It's right by a few buildings / cafe, and beside the park - aside from the stone structure itself, not much to see or do.", "Everyone's running towards the double arch opposite... hmm... I found the octagonal mausoleum much better. Unfortunately, the explanatory plaque is missing. It's easily accessible. It's an excavation, and you're looking down at the structure from above!"]}}
8. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Tragovi dinosaura", "tags": ["attraction", "geopaleontological_site", "prehistoric", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A remarkable geopaleontological attraction where preserved dinosaur footprints reveal that ancient reptiles once walked this area around 130 to 100 million years ago. More than 200 footprints have been discovered across Brijuni, with visitor-accessible tracks on Veliki Brijun offering a rare and valuable glimpse into the prehistoric past.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["At first glance, nothing 'special' but when do you ever see real dinosaur footprints? I thought it was cool that they had a matching dinosaur statue next to it. If you're on the island, you should stop by there, too.", "Traces 100 million years old. Super exciting.", "It was simply amazing to see something like that. When and where else do you get the chance to admire original dinosaur footprints!? And the best part was, I was completely alone there (off-season, early June, around 5 pm), simply wonderful."]}}
9. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Arheološki muzej Istre", "tags": ["museum", "archeology", "historic", "city_center"], "description": "Major archaeological museum in Pula focused on Istria’s heritage, with collections and exhibitions across multiple locations while its main building is under renovation.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Learning something new is amazing. Those tunnels were built long time ago even before my grandpa's time. Just to see that things are not always what seems to be, gives you time to reflect and appreciate what you have now. History is teaching us a good lesson let's don't make the same mistake again. If visit Pula this location gives you a 360 view over the city. The Colosseum is on the East side of the fort.", "Pretty great museum if you like history and museums, there's a few rooms on the main level of the citadel. Otherwise, I'd say it's nothing special and the other levels and underground of the citadel are more fascinating.", "Hilltop fort in the center of the city. It now houses a museum dedicated, by in large to the occupation of the city, and of Croatia, in second world war. The upper levels provide for excellent view points of the city. It's not expensive to enter and worth a visit during your time in Pula."]}}
10. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "burgers", "meat", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Odisej", "phone": "+385 52 223 288", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-23:00; Sa-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Arsenalska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual grill restaurant with a terrace, offering hearty meat dishes, burgers, barbecue specialties, and a comfortable setting for relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["We were welcomed the minute we sat down. Got the menus and she took the order after a few minutes of deciding what to eat. We chose the mean plate for 2. When we got it it was huge. Took some time to finish for sure. It tasted great. I can only recommend.", "First of all, best service ever! You are really friendly greated here and get all the recommendations you need from beer over food. We had the grill plate for two persons and we couldn' finish it. A lot of meat, fresh typical bread, fries and dips. You can get a taste of croatia over here! Recommended!", "Big generous portions of freshly grilled meat - exactly what you need for a traditional lunch in a place not filled with tourists."], "price": null}}
2. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "burgers", "meat", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Smoked", "phone": "+385 91 510 2567", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "67", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual BBQ restaurant with a terrace, offering smoked and grilled meats, burgers, ribs, steaks, vegan options, desserts, and a good selection of drinks.", "reviews": ["Amazing experience on this restaurant..the food was perfect,meat was more than impressive from the quality to the way of been cooked.service was also perfect but the food..the food was more than everything..", "Awesome place! The platter for two was super tasty and the crème brûlée was just perfect. Everything was great — definitely coming back next time we’re in Pula!", "We had a fantastic experience at Smoked Bar & BBQ in Pula. The food was outstanding – cooked to perfection, beautifully presented, and full of rich, smoky flavours. Every dish had great attention to detail and was bursting with taste. The service was equally impressive: friendly, attentive, and made the whole evening feel really relaxed and welcoming. If you’re in Pula and love quality BBQ with excellent flavours and presentation, this is definitely a spot worth visiting!"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["croatian", "local", "seafood", "grill"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Cementara", "phone": "+385 99 835 2503", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-17:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Revelanteova", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local bistro, offering affordable daily lunch menus, homemade dishes, seafood and meat specialties, and relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["Very good food and very affordable! It feels very local but there isn't a lot to see around so go there if you're on a walk. Also the waitress was very helpful and cute. 10/10 would go again", "Our accommodation was nearby, so we ended up here by chance. The tomato salad, rump steak with pepper sauce and fries (€13), and the tagliatelle with truffles (€15) were all excellent and very tasty. The prices are absolutely unbeatable. The staff is super friendly. You sit on a small terrace overlooking a parking lot. That's the only downside. Otherwise, a definite thumbs up for authentic, delicious Croatian cuisine.", "A hidden gem in the Docklands. Simple, but the food is fantastic and beautifully presented. We had grilled fish, calamari, and truffle pasta. The service was also very friendly (only Croatian spoken)."], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "grill", "seafood", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Galeb", "phone": "+385 52 386 361", "opening_hours": "Mo off; Tu-Su 10:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "37", "addr:street": "Osječka", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual bistro and grill restaurant serving grilled meat dishes, ćevapi, steaks, mixed platters, fried and grilled squid, whole fish, and seafood specialties.", "reviews": ["Service courteous, eat very delicious at a relatively low price and the beer is on tap. What more could you want", "The service was excellent, always there when you needed something. The food was fresh and extremely delicious, the music was nice, and the overall atmosphere was calm.", "I had the seafood pasta and it was absolutely delicious. It was a very light red cream sauce. I don’t know all the different kinds of seafood that was in it, but there was a big variety and it was delicious. I eat here on August 13 and it was quite warm outside, and I sat on the patio which is covered and shaded and has bands and wasfine to sit in. I’ll be a bit warm. Service was OK but just fine. It’s off the beaten path, so it felt not so part of the hustle and bustle with a little more private."], "price": null}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "meat", "cevapi"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Kod Kadre", "phone": "+385 91 637 0470", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 10:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "50A", "addr:street": "Nikole Tesle", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual local grill restaurant known for traditional Balkan-style grilled meat dishes, hearty portions, and a relaxed, no-frills atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Very delicious food. Affordable. Calm atmosphere. The Cevapcici were delicious. The fries portion big. The bread was also very delicious", "Kod Kadre is a great place to spend a pleasant evening with friends. The venue is clean and welcoming, with an ideal temperature and no smells coming from the kitchen. The cuisine is simple and authentic, with tasty traditional dishes served with a cheerful touch. The staff are friendly, polite, and always attentive to customers’ needs. Prices are very reasonable. I would recommend it to anyone looking for a relaxing evening with good food at affordable prices.", "We came in to get some good Croatian food, we got the cevapi and some gnocchi gulash, and everything was delish. On top of that the waitress was the cutest nicest ever ! I'd definitely comeback there !", "We had lunch here today. The waitress was very kind and helpful, the menu offers a wide selection, and the food was truly delicious. The desserts are spectacular. The wait for the main courses was really short. Highly recommended."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "grill", "seafood", "pasta"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Restaurant & Bar Gardelin", "phone": "+385 52 534 618", "opening_hours": "Mo 09:00-21:30; Tu-We 10:00-21:30; Th-Sa 10:00-21:00; Su off ", "addr:housenumber": "2", "addr:street": "Paduljski put", "rating": 4.1, "description": "A long-running family restaurant and guesthouse on Veli Vrh, known for regional cuisine, charcoal-grilled meat and fish, homemade pasta, a spacious terrace, and weekend live music.", "reviews": ["Highly recommended. If you want to eat well, inexpensively and in a nice atmosphere, you should definitely visit this pub. The prices are more than fair, the place is a very nice looking place and the menu selection is great. The food tastes great and the waiters are just as friendly. The pork on bbq is just amazing!", "Bloody gorgeous place!! We saw this place on the way to Rovinj and it looked great. Read the reviews and thought oh maybe not so good BUT forget the negative reviews- this place is great, lovely food, time is on your side and it beats all the places on pula central who pretty much sell the same menu. You also feel like you are having a local experience - try it and love it!!!", "It was our first food stop while visiting Pula. The fish is perfectly cooked, and the potatoes with chard is very good. The fries were cooked well."], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "barbecue", "meat", "cevapi", "burgers", "brunch", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Batak", "phone": "+385 52 511 511", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 11:00-23:00; Sa 09:00.23:00; Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.5, "description": "Modern grill restaurant in Pula City Mall offering a wide range of meat dishes, steaks and comfort food in a stylish, contemporary setting.", "reviews": ["Very good food and excellent service. We had ćevapi and the stuffed pork steak. The ćevapi were juicy and well grilled, with soft lepinja. The stuffed pork steak was rich and well prepared. Homemade potatoes with melted cheese and crispy bacon were a great side. Apple tart was a solid dessert, not too sweet. Service was the highlight. Fast, professional, and friendly. Make a reservation, this place gets busy.", "Everything we had was amazing! Everything. You must do reservation over web page. Fancy but with very REASONABLE prices! Quality! I was more than surprised over the whole package! You cannot compare this prices and quality to some / most restaurants in Pula. We’ve been in Zagreb in one od your restaurants couple of years ago, but this one left us speechless. Compliments 😻👏🏻🥇", "We went in for a light meal, food was fantastic. What stands out even more was their service. Extremely friendly and kind service! We really loved the time spent there. Interiors were cozy and elegant! And in the end, they also gave a little peppa pig present for my little daughter!"], "price": "high"}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
4. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Greenhill", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "garden"], "description": "Modern one-bedroom apartment in Pula with a terrace, garden, free parking, and airport transfer, located close to the Arena and city centre.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Very nicely furnished apartment, has everything you need for a good vacation, very friendly hosts, always at hand for any questions.", "The apartment itself was equipped with everything I needed for more stay and more. It was located really close to the city which meant getting to it was no issue.", "Very nice host. I can only recommend this place. :) Thank you for everything"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
6. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Tourist Info Centre", "tags": ["information", "office", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Tourist information office in the heart of Pula on the Forum, offering maps, travel information, and visitor services from a historic building in the city’s main square.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Great, friendly service. Printed our boarding passes without charge when the EasyJet App did not work at the airport. Excellent", "For the first time, just a phone conversation. The employee was extremely kind, warm. She answered all my questions without any hesitation, simply and clearly. Thank you very much.", "Excellently trained and friendly team of employees always ready to help with information. A good team greatly contributes to the tourist offer of the city of Pula. Well done and keep up the good work."]}}
7. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
9. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
2. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Zvonimira", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "playground", "family_friendly", "memorial"], "description": "Peaceful waterfront park in Pula with shaded benches, a children’s playground, and cultural landmarks including the Marulić monument and the Balašević bench.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A beautiful green space with several seating areas offering stunning views of the sea, shaded by beautiful trees. The lawn is beautiful and well-kept, and the surrounding area is very clean. Definitely a recommended spot for a lovely stroll."]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
7. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Verudela Art Park", "tags": ["park", "sculpture", "family_friendly", "near_beach"], "description": "Contemporary art park on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, featuring large sculptural installations, walking paths, and an open-air setting near Ambrela Beach designed for relaxation, play, and socialising.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Discovered by accident, the park has the bare bones of an excellent experience but is now in need of new and more exhibits. Location is great and good place to escape from the beach on a hot and busy day. Maybe time to partner up with similar organisations in other countries?", "In Verudela, near Pula, there's a charming place called Verudela Art Park. It's a series of original installations set up in an empty lot between the beach, a parking lot, a restaurant, and sports fields. The meaning of these art objects isn't described anywhere, but they're surrounded by a rusty (purposefully) metal wall stenciled with the names of seas and oceans, hinting at their significance. The whole thing looks especially striking in the backlit evening light.", "Beauty. Simplicity. Twist some metal ropes and it looks amazing."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Titov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "events", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central waterfront park in Pula, known for its memorial monuments, shaded walking areas, city model, and lively social atmosphere with seasonal events.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Tito's Park in Pula is a prominent public park that serves as a green oasis in the heart of the city. Named after Josip Broz Tito, the former Yugoslav leader, the park is a popular area for both locals and tourists seeking relaxation and recreation. There's also a miniature model on one side of the park.", "Nice park next to the water with many busts of famous partisans, including Tito. The main monument is also dedicated to the partisans. Worth a few pictures.", "A piece of more recent Croatian history. Has some statues, a place for kids to play, a few benches and a model of the city."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
4. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "HI Hostel Pula", "tags": ["hostel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Beachside hostel in a pine-forest setting near Valsaline, offering simple budget accommodation a short drive from Pula’s old town and Arena. It is a practical choice for solo travellers, groups and school trips, with shared social spaces, a terrace, free WiFi, free public parking and easy access to the sea, Lungomare promenade and outdoor activities.", "rating": 3.6, "reviews": ["I loved everything!! The staff was very lovely and helpful in every way!! Everyone around was very friendly, I definitely plan to come back soon!!, even tho I booked the cheapest room the receptionist made sure I had the most comfortable and safe stay as a solo traveler woman. The beautiful beach is not too far from the city center, you can take a bus and it's only 15min away from the main bus station.", "location right at the beach, available free parking, serve breakfast, yet be realistic they match the price i.e. they give cheap bread, butter jam cereals cheap coffee that's it (value 1-2 euros). no kitchen there. nearly no night life. you have to drive or take bike to the center Pula.", "I arrived here after a long day of traveling, at dusk, exhausted. Given its location and the lack of many dining options nearby, my dinner consisted of two beers, a bag of chips, and ice cream. The sunset views were incredible. I thought it was a beautiful place. Now for the downsides: it was super noisy. The rooms smelled awful, felt dirty, and the showers were poorly maintained. It's very far from the center. It took me an hour to find it. The breakfast was mediocre. The staff was extremely unfriendly."]}}
5. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Karmen", "tags": ["hotel", "national_park", "island", "historic", "coastal", "near_beach", "family_friendly"], "description": "Historic seaside guesthouse on Veliki Brijun, offering simple rooms with park or sea views, old-world charm, and a peaceful stay in Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 3.9, "reviews": ["This island is beautiful and has a sense of peace, even on August 15th! The property still has its 1960s furnishings, but it's clean and charming. The terrace overlooking the sea is truly beautiful and relaxing. It's true that there's no air conditioning or mini-bar, but they provided us with a couple of fans, and we managed just fine. What can I say? The island is so beautiful, it's absolutely worth it.", "Wonderful, spacious rooms, just the right amount of nostalgia. In fact, everything is reminiscent of the 60s and 70s and I think it really is from that era, except for the beds, which are new and very comfortable. Again, it's kind of logical that it should stay that way. Everything is very clean. Breakfast is perfect. Staff is very friendly.", "Great view from the balcony, 70s flair – anyone who embraces that will enjoy a lovely and relaxing holiday. Clean and the room is cleaned daily. The only drawback is the lack of air conditioning. The buffet food at Hotel Neptun is excellent."]}}
9. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
10. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}

1. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "nightlife", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Old City Bar", "phone": "+385 52 222 944", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 06:30-02:30; Sa 07:00-02:00; Su 08:30-2:30", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Danteov trg", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A pub located in the center of Pula, offering a relaxed atmosphere during the day and lively parties at night. It is a popular spot for drinks, socializing, and weekend nightlife.", "reviews": ["Great service, Marcus was attentive and funny and made our night!! Drinks were all very good and really enjoyed the theatrics of the different shots and cocktails.", "Best Cocktails in town and super cool service personal, Marcus is our man! Come here! ✨🙌", "The service in this place cannot be compared to anything I've experienced so far of my nine days in Croatia. Not the cheapest, but the persistence and effort by Marco is why you pay a premium. The live music was also quite good. Awsome Bloody Mary if you're into that, and a selection of craft beer if that is your thing. (To Marco's employer, you should give this man a raise)"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Greenhill", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "garden"], "description": "Modern one-bedroom apartment in Pula with a terrace, garden, free parking, and airport transfer, located close to the Arena and city centre.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Very nicely furnished apartment, has everything you need for a good vacation, very friendly hosts, always at hand for any questions.", "The apartment itself was equipped with everything I needed for more stay and more. It was located really close to the city which meant getting to it was no issue.", "Very nice host. I can only recommend this place. :) Thank you for everything"]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Mar Mar Apartments", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment in Pula offering a fully equipped kitchen, free WiFi, free parking, and a convenient location close to Valkane Beach, the Arena, and other main city attractions.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment for two people is quite welcoming, tidy, clean, and cared for down to the smallest details.", "Cool apartment, great location, very nice landlords and excellent service", "We are currently staying in the MarMar apartments. It is extremely clean and tidy.  We met the wife and she showed us around the apartment and were everything is.  Honestly no complaints at all - both her and Mario have been so friendly and helpful and considerate. The only thing I would add, though it doesnt affect the review or amount of stars, but from personal experience of owning rental units - I would provide papertowel and serviettes/napkins.  Something so minor. But so far, we are loving the apartment! Great experience and great comfort.  The bed is so extremely comfortable. 10/10 all around :)"]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Funcic Apartments", "tags": ["apartment", "pool", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking"], "description": null, "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["Magnificent bed and breakfast just a few kilometers from Pula. The property consists of three small apartments arranged in a horseshoe shape, with a shared pool in the center. The property also includes an American bar and a large grill. Ljuba, the owner, is very helpful and kind.", "Incredibly beautiful apartment, Ljuba is very nice. It's worth coming here; it's in a very quiet location close to the sea, only about 1.5 km away.", "Clean, comfortable, and practical accommodation. The pool is also lovely. The hostess speaks perfect Italian and is very helpful. We will definitely be back."]}}
8. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
9. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
10. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
2. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Ovine", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "coastal"], "description": "Abandoned Austro-Hungarian coastal fort in the Valovine area, known for its atmospheric tunnels, overgrown walls, and striking rooftop views over the sea.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["It was a small ruin with an entrance, a hallway, some rooms and a tunnel to a small katacomb. The dark tunnel which looks like the entrance of a katacomb has a slight slope and is slippery. Unfortunately some of the rooms were used as toilets - no understanding for that... The parking lots are kind off in front of fort and very busy. So make shure to plan your visit in the morning.", "Nothing special about this place, I have only visited the exterior though. I don't know if I suggest the visit. There is a civil guard near the entrance", "A fortification overgrown in the rock. Large areas are empty and dark. For those who enjoy extreme sports, this is for you."]}}
5. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Mate Parlov", "tags": ["sculpture", "statue", "monument", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A public sculpture dedicated to one of Pula’s most celebrated athletes and a legendary figure in Croatian boxing. Located on Giardini, it honors his lasting connection to the city and keeps the memory of his sporting legacy alive in the heart of Pula.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["The appearance of the statue doesn't give away that it's a boxer. Too bad.", "A nice gesture and thanks from the city of Pula and its citizens"]}}
6. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort San Giorgio", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century circular hilltop fort in Pula, built as part of the Austro-Hungarian defence system and known for its strong military character.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A beautiful fort which is worth a 5 star rating! HOWEVER, completely ruined by graffiti and rubbish, see pictures. Government please preserve this amazing object", "Nice view, a special scent from the plants when entering, but a little sad that Croatia doesn't take more care of this place that is part of their heritage."]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
9. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
10. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "Dječje igralište Viška ulica", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Neighbourhood playground in Pula with basic play equipment, a fenced play area, and a family-friendly setting near Fort Casoni Vecchi and St. Paul’s Church.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
2. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Marko Marulić", "tags": ["statue", "sculpture", "monument", "park", "artwork", "city_center"], "description": "A bronze public sculpture dedicated to one of the most important figures of Croatian literature, placed in a small park near the waterfront and the railway station. Its calm, dignified form reflects the intellectual and cultural legacy of the Renaissance writer, adding a literary and commemorative note to the surrounding urban landscape.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": null}}
3. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Mate Parlov", "tags": ["sculpture", "statue", "monument", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A public sculpture dedicated to one of Pula’s most celebrated athletes and a legendary figure in Croatian boxing. Located on Giardini, it honors his lasting connection to the city and keeps the memory of his sporting legacy alive in the heart of Pula.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["The appearance of the statue doesn't give away that it's a boxer. Too bad.", "A nice gesture and thanks from the city of Pula and its citizens"]}}
4. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Spomenik Sonyju", "tags": ["sculpture", "memorial", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Life-size elephant memorial sculpture placed on a hill near the harbor, created in memory of a beloved elephant that lived on Brijuni for many years. The artwork is hand-carved and decorated with map motifs symbolizing the places connected to its life and journey.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Golub mira", "tags": ["artwork", "sculpture", "memorial", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A symbolic outdoor sculpture created by Dušan Džamonja and donated to the Brijuni archipelago in memory of Josip Broz Tito. Made of corten and formed from welded iron chains, it was conceived as a powerful expression of peace and freedom, combining modern artistic form with historical remembrance.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
6. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Spomenik streljanim mornarima", "tags": ["sculpture", "monument", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Memorial sculpture in Valerijin park in Pula, dedicated to the sailor and associated with the remembrance of the 1918 sailors’ revolt in the Bay of Kotor.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
7. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Borcima narodnooslobodilačke borbe i žrtvama fašizma 1941-1945", "tags": ["artwork", "monument", "memorial", "sculpture", "historic", "city_center"], "description": "Expressive memorial artwork in Tito’s Park near the Pula waterfront, dedicated to anti-fascist fighters and victims of wartime violence. Its dramatic sculptural composition symbolizes suffering, resistance, remembrance and hope, making it an important commemorative landmark in the city.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
8. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Žena s mijehom", "tags": ["artwork", "sculpture", "island", "national_park", "monument"], "description": "Žena s mijehom is a bronze sculpture by Frane Kršinić, created in 1956 and located in Brijuni National Park as part of the Živa voda memorial site. The sculpture depicts a woman bending forward and pouring water from a goatskin bag into a stone basin below, symbolizing the importance of fresh water on the island. It is both an artistic landmark and a memorial to the technical achievement of discovering and drawing underground spring water on Brijuni.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
9. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Josip Broz Tito", "tags": "bust", "description": null, "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
10. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "Josip Broz Tito", "tags": "bust", "description": null, "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
2. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Park Plaza Histria Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Premium seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea and marina views, indoor and outdoor pools, a large wellness and spa area, and easy access to the beach and city centre.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Nice hotel in a good location on the outskirts of town. Especially popular with tennis players. Great rooms, upscale amenities. Food is mediocre. Otherwise highly recommended.", "Top hotel in Pula. Great location, plenty of things to do and to see", "Great place to be close to the water and tennis/pickleball courts. Breakfast was great with many options and the bar was always popular with the bartenders taking time to answer questions and get to know the many different clients and all spoke multiple languages proficiently. Manuela was our favorite suggesting new drinks and asking if we needed anything.", "It is situated in one of the most beautiful spots on the Verudela Peninsula. The spa and wellness center is perfect for relaxation, and the massage services are top-notch. With the on-site shopping street and various dining options, you don't even feel the need to leave the hotel. Watching the sunset by the pool in the evening is truly priceless. While there are suitable areas for families with children, the overall atmosphere is calm and prestigious. If you want to visit the historic center of Pula, you can reach it in about 10-15 minutes by public transport or taxi. The only thing that disappointed me was that I booked a room in the 5-star section of the hotel through Booking, but when I arrived, they gave us rooms in the older hotel buildings. Despite being an old building, the rooms had been renovated and were comfortable."]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Modo", "tags": ["hotel", "seaside", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "restaurant"], "description": "A modern seaside hotel in Pula set between the bays of Stoja and Valovine, offering sea-view rooms with balconies, free WiFi, free parking and easy access to nearby beaches. Its quiet location and convenient connection to the city make it suitable for families, couples and business travellers.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Great little hotel in a great location. The staff is very professional and friendly. The premises are modernly decorated and clean. A rich selection of food for breakfast.", "Cosy hotel, spacious room with balcony overlooking the sea. The manager on our arrival was friendly and explained what to visit in Pula and nearby. In addition he suggested (and we went there on the last day) to visit Motovun, castle and village where you eat dishes with truffles. The breakfast of the hotel is great, varied both savory and sweet. At night absolute silence, very relaxing.", "The location was amazing ! We had a balcony that was perfect for watching the sunsets . We easily walked into town ( there also is a bus option ) the rooms were clean and comfortable . My only negative was the AC shut off randomly . The front desk said it turned off every 2 hours and needed to be reset . This was not a great for a cool night sleep without getting up a number of times to reset the AC . Breakfast was very good and it was lovely to eat out on the deck . Staff was friendly and helpful ."]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Park Plaza Verudela", "tags": ["resort", "apartments", "family_friendly", "pool", "near_beach", "free_parking", "coastal"], "description": "A modern seaside resort on the Verudela peninsula offering well-equipped apartments, beautiful coastal views and easy access to the beach. Known for its seawater pools, family-friendly atmosphere and convenient location near Pula, it is a great choice for guests who want the flexibility of apartment accommodation with resort-style amenities.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["All praise for a real little paradise in the embrace of the sea. The location is truly inspiring, beautiful and unusual. The staff, service and facilities are great. Kudos to the people who clean and maintain the rooms. Cleanliness is up to the task. The friendliness of the people at the reception is commendable.", "This is our second time here. It's very quiet in the off-season, yet truly beautiful. The complex is large and offers plenty of variety. The apartments are well-equipped; we had two bathrooms and ample space. I can easily imagine coming back a third time.", "Beautiful location surrounded by greenery and close to the sea, creating a relaxing atmosphere throughout the stay. The food was good with a nice variety, and the hotel is conveniently located just a short distance from Pula’s old town, making it easy to explore the historic sights while still enjoying a peaceful setting."]}}
7. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Ribarska Koliba Resort", "tags": ["hotel", "resort", "coastal", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pool", "restaurant", "events"], "description": "A stylish seaside resort in Pula known for its long hospitality tradition, elegant rooms and scenic setting near Marina Veruda and Marina Bunarina. It offers a quiet stay close to beaches, the aquarium and major city sights, with modern amenities such as free WiFi, parking and a pool area.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I've been here a few times, with friends and family and I've been very satisfied every time. The rooms are spacious, clean and well laid out. The breakfast is excellent with a lot of choice and a beautiful view of the marina. The staff is friendly and fantastic, to be commended for their flexibility regarding check-in and check-out and all the necessary services and information. Real value for money!", "Lovely euro boutique hotel that exceeds expectations. Great close in views of the marina from the third floor. Rooms are great, functional and have all the amenities. Very nice outdoor deck. On site Michelin restaurant is a bonus. You will have to Uber bus or drive to the Pula old town. There is a fine sea walk and beaches nearby and a few luxury hotels with nice eating options. Recommended.", "Incredible stay. We stayed for 5 nights as part of our honeymoon journey throughout Croatia. We were kindly upgraded to the 'Fuoco 1' apartment and it was superb, immaculately clean, spacious with fantastic views of the marina from the private balcony. The staff were so friendly and helpful when my wife required some medical attention for her infected insect bite they signposted us to the tourist hospital. We dined at the on-site restaurant twice because the quality of food was so good and was reasonably priced. Aperol spritz only 8€ as an example. Highly reccomended and we hope to visit again in future anniversaries."]}}
9. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}

1. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
3. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartmani Pula Arena", "tags": ["apartment", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Modern apartments in central Pula near the Arena, offering equipped kitchens, free WiFi, and easy access to the city’s main sights.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment is perfectly located (right next to the Arena of Pula) to explore the city. Also it is very close to the ferry terminal which is convenient if you travel onwards with the ship.", "The apartment is in an excellent location, in a dilapidated building. The interior furnishings are okay, but there's room for improvement.", "Very good location, unfortunately a forest in front obscures the view of the sea. You have to see it from the upper windows. Clean and tidy. The second level of the apartment is like a loft with beds. Quiet and pleasant."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
6. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Tourist Info Centre", "tags": ["information", "office", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Tourist information office in the heart of Pula on the Forum, offering maps, travel information, and visitor services from a historic building in the city’s main square.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Great, friendly service. Printed our boarding passes without charge when the EasyJet App did not work at the airport. Excellent", "For the first time, just a phone conversation. The employee was extremely kind, warm. She answered all my questions without any hesitation, simply and clearly. Thank you very much.", "Excellently trained and friendly team of employees always ready to help with information. A good team greatly contributes to the tourist offer of the city of Pula. Well done and keep up the good work."]}}
7. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
9. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
4. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
5. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
6. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Mar Mar Apartments", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment in Pula offering a fully equipped kitchen, free WiFi, free parking, and a convenient location close to Valkane Beach, the Arena, and other main city attractions.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["The apartment for two people is quite welcoming, tidy, clean, and cared for down to the smallest details.", "Cool apartment, great location, very nice landlords and excellent service", "We are currently staying in the MarMar apartments. It is extremely clean and tidy.  We met the wife and she showed us around the apartment and were everything is.  Honestly no complaints at all - both her and Mario have been so friendly and helpful and considerate. The only thing I would add, though it doesnt affect the review or amount of stars, but from personal experience of owning rental units - I would provide papertowel and serviettes/napkins.  Something so minor. But so far, we are loving the apartment! Great experience and great comfort.  The bed is so extremely comfortable. 10/10 all around :)"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Fresh sandwiches & salads", "phone": "+385 91 722 7712", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Anticova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Casual street food spot focused on fresh, quick, and healthier meals, with a strong choice of salads, wraps, panini, smoothies, and breakfast items. Especially good for vegetarian and vegan options, but there are meat choices too.", "reviews": ["Food was really nice, we had a wrap filled with hummus and falafel which was really nice to eat on the go while exploring Pula. Would recommend if you like vegetarian food and look for fastfood but in a healthy way. I think they also have meaty options. Price was 7€ for a wrap which was really okay!", "Amazing food. So healthy and refreshing! Super reasonable prices and fantastic service. I got the lentil wrap and LOVED IT! Great vegetarian and vegan options.", "Had two excellent tortillas and a smoothie. Have to say that the one large tortilla was filling enough for one person, so don't worry you won't have enough. For very little money, you get fresh and healthy food. Fastfood gone good 😊"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["salads", "wok", "desserts", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Mini Mini Street Food", "phone": "+385 99 445 6190", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "12", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A small street food restaurant in Pula serving freshly prepared daily lunches, colorful healthy plates, homemade pasta, dumplings, salads, desserts, and other casual dishes made with local and organic ingredients.", "reviews": ["So lovely tiny cosy place! Delicious, homemade food! Service excellent! Perfect chick &vegan options! 🤩⭐️", "Excellent food and ambient. Lots of vegetarian options, big size dishes, good price for the given quantity and quality."], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "brunch", "salads", "pasta", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "healthy", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Street Food Two", "phone": "+385 52 203 236", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-15:00; Sa-Su off", "addr:housenumber": "2A", "addr:street": "Veronska", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A modern street food spot in the city center of Pula, offers fresh, colorful, and healthier fast meals, with plenty of salads, bowls, burritos, and vegetarian options.", "reviews": ["Fresh, delicious and surprisingly versatile – highly recommended! The food was consistently fresh and top-quality – you immediately notice that they work with high-quality ingredients. The Service was super friendly, attentive and competent. We were particularly surprised by the selection of vegetarian dishes, which is really great by Croatian standards. Vegan options are also available and lovingly prepared. A place that perfectly combines pleasure, quality and hospitality.", "As a vegetarian finding healthy, vegan and vegetarian options in Croatia is simply too rare to be picky. However, this spot is simple, very nice and the food super fine. We had the tofu poke and the kids the tortellini. Everyone was happy. The staff was extremely friendly!", "Some great fresh healthy options here and amazing tasting food. We had the chickpea patties and tofu poke bowl which was so delicious! Flavours were fab & lovely staff!", "Yum, yum, yum. So fresh and cooked with love. Our first time trying this (we are new to Pula and it's close to our apartment) and it really delivered . I had the prawn and pumpkin risotto and my husband ordered the beef burrito. The taste was great and the portion large, the price reasonable for how much food you get. The service was positive and the server was smiling and happy. Quick stop, we hardly waited. We will be back. Thank you for a lovely, healthy lunch."], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "smoothies", "healthy", "brunch", "breakfast", "international", "vegan", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kavana Lattiera", "phone": "+385 91 537 4711", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-16:00; Sa-Su 09:00-15:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Trg Kralja Tomislava", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A modern cafe in Veruda known for specialty coffee, healthy breakfasts, smoothie bowls, homemade cakes, and a relaxed neighborhood atmosphere. Inspired by Berlin-style coffee culture, it is a popular spot for morning coffee, brunch, fresh juices, and casual meetups on the square.", "reviews": ["We stopped at Kavana Lattiera and really enjoyed the atmosphere. The coffee and desserts were excellent, and the place has a very nice vibe for sitting down and relaxing. One thing that stood out, though, was the wait time – we had to wait more than 30 minutes for our order, and it felt like we had been forgotten for a while. Once everything finally arrived, the quality made up for it, but the service could definitely be more attentive.", "Great place with a fresh and healthy offer! The menu is full of delicious options made from quality ingredients — from smoothie bowls and sandwiches to great breakfast choices. The açaí bowl is especially tasty and definitely worth trying. Perfect spot for a relaxed coffee or a healthy meal.", "During the vacation with my girlfriend (who only eats vegetarian and gluten free) in Croatia, we went a couple of times here. What a nice place and so many locals went there as well. The menu was only on Croatian and we had to translate but that was not a problem at all. The service, the food, everything is so nice here. And the best thing is, it’s open until 4 pm.", "Very interesting establishment set amongst apartments and shops. Inside it's a whole different feel to the outside and to what I have seen in Pula, which is very comforting and reminds me of other international cafes, and those special couple of cafes in Zagreb too. The food is so good, healthy and very thoughtful recipes. Veg will be happy. Oat milk available."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "kebab", "burgers", "fries", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Adi", "phone": "+385 52 383 756", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 09:00-02:00,; Sa 10:00-02:00; Su 18:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "6", "addr:street": "Mletačka", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A simple city-centre fast food spot best known for its kebabs, with quick service and classic takeaway options like tortillas, burgers and fries.", "reviews": ["Food was great. Service was fast and personalized. They accommodated my food allergy. No air conditioning so its a little hot inside.", "Really good kebab, one of the best in Pula.", "Favorite kebab spot in Pula! The food is excellent, the lepinja especially is very good here. The spot is no frills takeout, but always extremely clean and very fast. Cheap too! We love Kebab Adi!"], "price": "medium"}}

