1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Spomenik Vladimiru Gortanu", "tags": ["sculpture", "memorial", "monument", "historic", "near_beach", "coastal"], "description": "Memorial sculpture on Lungomare in Pula dedicated to Vladimir Gortan, an important symbol of Istrian anti-fascist resistance, placed near the site where he was executed in 1929.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Beautiful monument. What is sad, apart from the story about Gortan himself, is that it's a wild parking place with cars parked 20cm from the monument all around it."]}}
3. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Rimski mauzolej", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "ancient", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Ancient remains of an octagonal Roman mausoleum dating from the 1st century, located near the Twin Gates, the Archaeological Museum of Istria and the old city walls. Only the lower part is preserved today, but it still reflects the architectural elegance and funerary traditions of Roman Pula, making it an interesting stop for visitors exploring the city’s archaeological heritage.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["The mausoleum is actually a funerary monument, it should only be understood for this purpose. What is still visible is the base of the one used by the Romans, it being much taller, richly ornamented and placed outside the walls of the Roman city for reasons related to the legislation of the time regarding the burial of the dead. All the explanations, photographs and sketches help you understand and imagine what this construction was. Currently it is in a small park, across the road from the Gemini Gate", "This octagonal wonder from the 1st century stands as a testament to Pula's rich Roman roots. It's right by a few buildings / cafe, and beside the park - aside from the stone structure itself, not much to see or do.", "Everyone's running towards the double arch opposite... hmm... I found the octagonal mausoleum much better. Unfortunately, the explanatory plaque is missing. It's easily accessible. It's an excavation, and you're looking down at the structure from above!"]}}
5. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
6. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
7. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Arheološki muzej Istre", "tags": ["museum", "archeology", "historic", "city_center"], "description": "Major archaeological museum in Pula focused on Istria’s heritage, with collections and exhibitions across multiple locations while its main building is under renovation.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Learning something new is amazing. Those tunnels were built long time ago even before my grandpa's time. Just to see that things are not always what seems to be, gives you time to reflect and appreciate what you have now. History is teaching us a good lesson let's don't make the same mistake again. If visit Pula this location gives you a 360 view over the city. The Colosseum is on the East side of the fort.", "Pretty great museum if you like history and museums, there's a few rooms on the main level of the citadel. Otherwise, I'd say it's nothing special and the other levels and underground of the citadel are more fascinating.", "Hilltop fort in the center of the city. It now houses a museum dedicated, by in large to the occupation of the city, and of Croatia, in second world war. The upper levels provide for excellent view points of the city. It's not expensive to enter and worth a visit during your time in Pula."]}}
8. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
9. {"type": "memorial", "properties": {"name": "Lino Mariani", "tags": ["bust", "memorial", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A bronze memorial bust dedicated to an antifascist partisan, trade unionist and worker remembered for his role in the turbulent post-war history of Pula. Placed near the ancient city walls and Hercules Gate, it adds a modern historical layer to this Roman setting and commemorates local resistance, labour struggle and civic memory.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": null}}
10. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}

1. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
4. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Omir Bed & Breakfast", "tags": ["hotel", "city_center", "near_attractions", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly"], "description": "Bed and breakfast in central Pula, offering air-conditioned rooms, breakfast, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of the Arena and other main sights.", "rating": 4.0, "reviews": ["Very nice helpfull personel, they help us in car rent and give information of best restaurant in Pula. Nice clean room, good location. Sincerelly recommended.", "Very good hotel. Convenient location - close to the center and not far from the sea. Delicious breakfasts, friendly staff, clean rooms. I was pleasantly pleased by the fact that when we left early, the owner himself offered and left breakfast for us at the reception. I highly recommend", "Excellent location with incredibly nice and helpful owners! Perfect accommodation for a weekend in Pula."]}}
5. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
6. {"type": "aquarium", "properties": {"name": "Aquarium Pula", "tags": ["aquarium", "fortress", "family_friendly", "historic", "near_beach"], "description": "Aquarium in Fort Verudela and Battery San Giovanni in Pula, known for its Adriatic and exotic marine exhibits, sea turtle rescue centre, and unique setting within historic Austro-Hungarian fortifications.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["We (family of 7) visited during the holiday season. The price was excellent (half price period), there were not many people. We bought the tickets online, in advance. The whole experience was great, totally worth the trip from Rovinj. There are two exhibitions, international and mediterranean. Both were quite enjoyable. The only problem was that we have a dog, who is not allowed inside. It is absolutly understandable (however there are even zoos, where they are welcome: like in Ljubljana Zoo), and the surrounding area is excellent for walks, so we diveded our forces, and went in separately, in two groups. Not ideal, but it was a great decision not to miss the aquarium. Recommended!", "We had such a great time here. It was late September and really not too many people. The building (old fortress) ia very impressive and the perfect location for this beautiful Aquarium. It consists of two buildings, old tunnels and areas outside. Our daughter loved it and we did too. 100% recommend", "This was a wonderful surprise! I didn’t expect it to be so big and to have so many different species. My 9-month-old loved it and was fascinated by everything. I highly recommend bringing your family here and buying tickets online, as the regular line can get quite long, while the online ticket line was empty."]}}
7. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
9. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Zvonimira", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "playground", "family_friendly", "memorial"], "description": "Peaceful waterfront park in Pula with shaded benches, a children’s playground, and cultural landmarks including the Marulić monument and the Balašević bench.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A beautiful green space with several seating areas offering stunning views of the sea, shaded by beautiful trees. The lawn is beautiful and well-kept, and the surrounding area is very clean. Definitely a recommended spot for a lovely stroll."]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}
2. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda Monvidal", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic hilltop fort in Pula with a distinctive horseshoe layout, surrounded by greenery and preserving a raw reminder of the city’s military past.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["Worth checking out but nothing special", "The fortress is in very poor condition. It's completely overgrown with trees and grass; you can walk around it in five minutes. There are many interesting stories about it online, but in reality, there's nothing to see. It's a shame such a place is falling into disrepair.", "We discovered this fortress by accident during a night walk. Very few people know about it. Despite being neglected, it is a piece of history and worth seeing."]}}
5. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Kaiser Franz", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "island", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic coastal fortress on the island of Sveti Andrija in Pula, known for its circular form, layered military history, and strategic position in the middle of the harbour.", "rating": 3.8, "reviews": ["Nice fort. It's a pity that it is neglected and completely overgrown. While sightseeing, it feels like walking through a jungle. There are a lot of snakes and rats. On the roof of the fortress there are a lot of hidden ventilation holes through which you can fall, so you need to be very careful."]}}
6. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Utvrda San Michele", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area", "city_center"], "description": "Historic horseshoe-shaped fortress on the San Michele hill in Pula, built as part of the city’s defence system and known for its preserved military architecture and long later use within the hospital complex.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["One of many fortresses located in Pula, and I would say one of my favorites, sadly no one maintains them and they are falling apart. This is beautiful city with rich history and so many potetial and 0 will to restore them... who knows, maybe one day the people who manage the city will get into their heads that Pula is not only the sea and the Arena... Pula is much more...", "It could be an attraction if it wasn't completely neglected."]}}
8. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Tvrđava Muzil", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "coastal", "military_history"], "description": "Historic circular fortress on the Muzil peninsula in Pula, known for its preserved Austro-Hungarian military architecture, panoramic sea views, and prominent position above the southern coast.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["I'm happy that this most preserved Pula's fort is now locked and secured, preventing it from robbing and vandalism. Thanks.", "It was nice 'urban exploring' adventure, ruins everywhere, protected by army, but guardian is nice and army too! When sun goes down, be fast. Minutes matters. Some bushes (makija) can be spiky! Avoid them. Don't be barefoot.", "Fort Muzil is closed to free entry from December 30, 2022. The facility is protected and maintained and can only be visited with prior notice or an organized tour."]}}
9. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Turtian", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history", "closed_area"], "description": "Historic polygonal fortress near Pula, built as part of the city’s defensive ring and still standing prominently above the surrounding landscape.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A beautiful  Austro-Hungarian fortress with a beautiful sunset over Pula.", "We were there at the end of September. The only visitors to the fort were a few goats. The gate was closed to everyone else. We walked all the way around, and there's definitely no access. There's a sign at the entrance stating that the army abandoned the fort in 1992, and after that, it gradually fell into disrepair due to vandalism. Now, some local people have come together to clear out the fort, and perhaps there will be an opportunity to visit it on special days. There were no official opening hours listed. So, based on current information, it's not worth the trip."]}}
10. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Brioni Minor", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "military_history", "national_park", "island", "events"], "description": "Large Austro-Hungarian coastal fortress on Mali Brijun, known for its preserved military architecture, strategic sea-facing position, and summer theatre performances held within the fort.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["We have a chance to enjoy there as part of the King Lear play. Fortress is amasing an perfectly fitted the show.", "Amazing still standing fortress from the beginning of 20th century. Used by Ulysses theatre", "A beautiful place, lots of wonderful things to see, from rich flora and fauna to beautiful historical buildings."]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
5. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Zvonimira", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "playground", "family_friendly", "memorial"], "description": "Peaceful waterfront park in Pula with shaded benches, a children’s playground, and cultural landmarks including the Marulić monument and the Balašević bench.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A beautiful green space with several seating areas offering stunning views of the sea, shaded by beautiful trees. The lawn is beautiful and well-kept, and the surrounding area is very clean. Definitely a recommended spot for a lovely stroll."]}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
2. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Fratarski", "tags": ["camp", "island", "family_friendly", "nature"], "description": "Seasonal island campsite on Fratarski otok near Pula, known for its pine forest setting, clean sea, family-friendly beach, and relaxed summer atmosphere focused on nature, camping, and outdoor activities.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Great camping, somewhat spartan, but also very crowded. It is hard to find a decent spot in the shade.", "There should be more camps like this! Just nature, sea and tents! Perfect location :)", "Perfect way to enjoy the nature."]}}
3. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
4. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
5. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
8. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
9. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}

1. {"type": "ruins", "properties": {"name": "Grobljanska crkva sv. Antuna", "tags": ["ruins", "historic", "church", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Ruins of the former cemetery church of St. Anthony on Brijuni, a Gothic church dating from the 14th–15th century, located outside the former medieval settlement. The site includes traces of old frescoes, a stone bier inside the church, and remains of the cemetery that was in use from the Middle Ages until the 18th century.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["Old graveyard chapel that has been used for preparating the dead before the burials. Still a calm and enchanted place that should be visited with awe and respect.", "Old church, nearly fallen apart - no roof, some walls left standing. Outside the former medieval settlement was the cemetery church of St. Anton. The former residents of Brijuni found their final resting place around the church."]}}
2. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Muzej / galerija - Crkva Srca Isusova i Marijina (Sveta Srca)", "tags": ["gallery", "museum", "historic", "city_center", "events"], "description": "Former church in Pula’s old town, now a museum-gallery space hosting exhibitions, cultural events, and multimedia programmes.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["A little gem hidden in the old town of Pula. Free, quiet, on two levels, eclectic exhibits, special worksheets for children. Loved it.", "Free entry, quiet and calm vibes in an old church with multiple levels of art. Would definitely recommend but don't need to spend more than 20-30 minutes here", "Free entry. Currently occupied by a selection of highlights from a main art museum in Zagreb, which is undergoing a seismic retrofit. Beautiful space, nicely presented pieces. We were the only people there which is a shame - it deserves more visibility."]}}
3. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
5. {"type": "information", "properties": {"name": "Četvrt Sv. Teodora u Puli", "tags": ["board", "archaeological_site", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions", "roman"], "description": "A historic quarter in the northeastern corner of Pula’s old town, known for its exceptionally rich archaeological layers that reveal nearly 3,000 years of urban history. Excavations uncovered remains from prehistoric times, Roman temples, a domus, baths, early Christian churches and one of the largest amphora finds in the Mediterranean, making this area one of the city’s most important archaeological zones.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["A discovery of numerous remains from various cultural periods during the three-thousand-years long history of the city of Pula. They're pretty old and run down, not taller than a foot or two; only worth walking through if you're already in the area.", "A true hidden gem in the heart of Pula. The San Teodoro neighborhood is a fascinating archaeological site, where you literally walk through centuries of history: from Roman ruins to the Middle Ages, passing by the Temple of Hercules and the ancient amphorae discovered there. It's not a huge area nor overly touristy, but it's perfect for those who love archaeology and want to discover something authentic and peaceful. I recommend a guided tour to fully appreciate it!"]}}
6. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Bizantinski kastrum", "tags": ["archeological_site", "national_park", "historic", "ruins", "roman", "island"], "description": "Layered archaeological site on Veliki Brijun with remains of a late antique settlement, Byzantine-period fortifications, and centuries of continuous life within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["This is definitely one of the most interesting attractions on the island. The conservation of some of the stones and structures is very impressive and gives an idea of what life and work was on those times. These are the remains of an ancient settlement from the 4th century, inhabited even during Venetian rule.", "An impressive archeological site. Read the info-panel and walk around, try to imagine the life and architecture of this settlement.", "Absolutely recommendable for archaeologically interested visitors. There is still so much to see and explore. One of the best archaeological sites on the island.", "If you're cycling around the island, would definitely recommend stopping here on the way around - the size and scale of the preserved castle foundations are quite staggering"]}}
7. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Mozaik - Kažnjavanje Dirke", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula featuring the Roman mosaic of the Punishment of Dirce, a rare and finely preserved mythological floor mosaic discovered near St. Mary Formosa.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Kind of hard to find. You have to go around the back of the main street and through a parking lot. It almost looks like you are walking into someone's driveway. It is not well lit so if you want better pictures, go during the day.", "Very nice but looks like in a hidden area. You can follow the sign as well as use Google Maps. You may enter any time during the day at no charge.", "Absolutely go and see it - a beautifully preserved mosaic from I believe the 2nd or 3rd century AD within it's own protective room. No entry fee or anything; just observe the mosaic from street level and it is about 3-4 feet below street level. A little bit off the beaten track and the street signs aren't clear, but regardless it's a quiet and nice area so definitely make the detour."]}}
8. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
9. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
10. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Povijesni i pomorski muzej Istre", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "city_center", "fortress", "family_friendly"], "description": "Historic and maritime museum in Pula, housed in the 17th-century Venetian fortress on Kaštel, known for its collections on Istrian history, seafaring heritage, and commanding views over the city.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I appreciated the outstanding view but I think they should give you an audio guide as the museum ticket has a price but then looking inside you are just on your own hopping to understand correctly the long readings on the rooms.", "Learning something new is amazing. Those tunnels were built long time ago even before my grandpa's time. Just to see that things are not always what seems to be, gives you time to reflect and appreciate what you have now. History is teaching us a good lesson let's don't make the same mistake again. If visit Pula this location gives you a 360 view over the city. The Colosseum is on the East side of the fort.", "Pretty great museum if you like history and museums, there's a few rooms on the main level of the citadel. Otherwise, I'd say it's nothing special and the other levels and underground of the citadel are more fascinating."]}}

1. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["seafood", "burgers", "grill", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "69 Food", "phone": "+385 97 610 5322", "opening_hours": "Mo 12:00-21:00; Tu off; We-Su 12:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "18", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A city-center street food spot on main street, known for seafood specialties, burgers, grilled chicken, and a modern fast-food concept with a strong local identity.", "reviews": ["Cosy bar, wine measure was very generous with great, fast service same for the food orders. Lovely setting at the start of the old town. Food was very tasty.", "Mood, food and value for money absolutely TOP. For a small snack or a delicious burger during the city stroll in Pula stop there again and again.", "Very happy with this experience. Nice staff, fresh produce and well worked. Very good beer. If you’re looking to take a little break to eat don’t hesitate!", "The food is amazing and so so delicious. I had problems deciding which main to order and ended up having the tuna steak burger which was crazy good. As the portions are quite big, I didn't take something else but was looking at the tables around me and all of their menu items looked just mouthwatering. Their draft beers are also on point. The staff is also extremely polite, fast in service and greets everyone with a bit of jokes and small talk, which i totally liked. Highly recommend this place!"], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "burgers", "meat", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Smoked", "phone": "+385 91 510 2567", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "67", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual BBQ restaurant with a terrace, offering smoked and grilled meats, burgers, ribs, steaks, vegan options, desserts, and a good selection of drinks.", "reviews": ["Amazing experience on this restaurant..the food was perfect,meat was more than impressive from the quality to the way of been cooked.service was also perfect but the food..the food was more than everything..", "Awesome place! The platter for two was super tasty and the crème brûlée was just perfect. Everything was great — definitely coming back next time we’re in Pula!", "We had a fantastic experience at Smoked Bar & BBQ in Pula. The food was outstanding – cooked to perfection, beautifully presented, and full of rich, smoky flavours. Every dish had great attention to detail and was bursting with taste. The service was equally impressive: friendly, attentive, and made the whole evening feel really relaxed and welcoming. If you’re in Pula and love quality BBQ with excellent flavours and presentation, this is definitely a spot worth visiting!"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "cevapi", "beer", "vegetarian", "gluten_free"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Grill bar & Steak House Campo", "phone": "+385 52 517 327", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "21", "addr:street": "Fortin", "rating": 4.7, "description": "Modern grill and steakhouse known for premium steaks, generous mixed grill platters, ćevapi, burgers, and a wide range of meat specialties in a relaxed, contemporary setting.", "reviews": ["It was delicius. The food was a bomb. It was so freakin good. The staff was awesom and the service was very nice and he did put infos in to the steak. He really explained the different Steaks very very well. The menu was so various. You had the decision of the night. It really did deserve the five stars. Thanks for the great evening guys. The atmossphere was astronomical. Really qiuet. But still you could talk really nicely. It was the best experience of the many. Love the Restaurant. Worth the drive. It had so much drinks and food.", "We loved the place and service by Ivan. Had a selection of steaks with some fantastic sauces and little potatos with feta cheese. Kids had lovely grilled chicken. Ribs were also just sensational! The chef made it perfectly medium rare. Would definitely come back!", "An Istrian Jewel. Great food, great service, free schnapps. Highly recommended. Fantastic menu selection and reasonably priced. Visited for evening dinner and a lunch.", "We had the grill plate for two. The size was really enough and there was a large selection of meat. Everything tasted very good, including the flatbread. The service was very nice. The wait was a little longer because it was busy, but it was still ok. We'd love to go again."], "price": "high"}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "grill", "barbecue", "meat", "cevapi", "burgers", "brunch", "desserts"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Batak", "phone": "+385 52 511 511", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 11:00-23:00; Sa 09:00.23:00; Su 09:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.5, "description": "Modern grill restaurant in Pula City Mall offering a wide range of meat dishes, steaks and comfort food in a stylish, contemporary setting.", "reviews": ["Very good food and excellent service. We had ćevapi and the stuffed pork steak. The ćevapi were juicy and well grilled, with soft lepinja. The stuffed pork steak was rich and well prepared. Homemade potatoes with melted cheese and crispy bacon were a great side. Apple tart was a solid dessert, not too sweet. Service was the highlight. Fast, professional, and friendly. Make a reservation, this place gets busy.", "Everything we had was amazing! Everything. You must do reservation over web page. Fancy but with very REASONABLE prices! Quality! I was more than surprised over the whole package! You cannot compare this prices and quality to some / most restaurants in Pula. We’ve been in Zagreb in one od your restaurants couple of years ago, but this one left us speechless. Compliments 😻👏🏻🥇", "We went in for a light meal, food was fantastic. What stands out even more was their service. Extremely friendly and kind service! We really loved the time spent there. Interiors were cozy and elegant! And in the end, they also gave a little peppa pig present for my little daughter!"], "price": "high"}}
9. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "brunch", "burgers", "music", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "The Shipyard Pub", "phone": "+385 91 181 0630", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 08:00-02:00; Fr 08:00-03:00; Sa 10:00-03:00; Su 10:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Svetog Teodora", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Lively pub on the Riva with burgers, pub food, cocktails, beer, and a spacious terrace. A popular evening spot known for music, DJ sets, quiz nights, and other events in a casual, social atmosphere.", "reviews": ["We stayed here once for a drink and once for dinner. The Service was fast, friendly and accommodating in both cases. The Aperol Spritz was just as delicious as the burgers. These were juicy with very tasty sauces and the caramelized onions rounded it off with a great taste. The fries were also well seasoned and perfectly crispy. The dressing of the ceasar salad was a bit unusual and not quite typical but also incredibly delicious, we would love to come back. Value for money was also reasonable, so what more could you want.", "Friendly and efficient staff with delicious food. The burger was very good and my wife really enjoyed the noodles. Worth a stop. Plenty of seating inside and the vibes were relaxing.", "Great little bar in the heart of Pula! The atmosphere is warm and relaxed, and the staff were incredibly friendly. The music was just right for chatting without shouting, and prices were very reasonable compared to other spots in town. Perfect place to stop for a drink after sightseeing. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a cozy and authentic bar experience in Pula"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["balkan", "grill", "barbecue", "burgers", "meat", "beer"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Bistro Odisej", "phone": "+385 52 223 288", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 08:00-23:00; Sa-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Arsenalska", "rating": 4.4, "description": "A casual grill restaurant with a terrace, offering hearty meat dishes, burgers, barbecue specialties, and a comfortable setting for relaxed dining.", "reviews": ["We were welcomed the minute we sat down. Got the menus and she took the order after a few minutes of deciding what to eat. We chose the mean plate for 2. When we got it it was huge. Took some time to finish for sure. It tasted great. I can only recommend.", "First of all, best service ever! You are really friendly greated here and get all the recommendations you need from beer over food. We had the grill plate for two persons and we couldn' finish it. A lot of meat, fresh typical bread, fries and dips. You can get a taste of croatia over here! Recommended!", "Big generous portions of freshly grilled meat - exactly what you need for a traditional lunch in a place not filled with tourists."], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Lost Beach", "tags": ["beach", "sandy", "pet_friendly", "nature", "family_friendly"], "description": "Hidden sandy beach near Štinjan, known for its quiet natural setting, turquoise water, and relaxed atmosphere tucked away in a sheltered bay.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["If you're near Pula, you need to visit the Lost Beach. Had a weeks holiday in Stinjan/Pula and we visited The lost Beach twice! Pleasant walk down to the beach and bar, both visits it was quiet and plenty of space to sit and sun bath, water is clear and warm, view is amazing and the atmosphere is perfect. It exceeded all expectations! It was amazing. It really is a picture perfect Adriatic Cove. A must visit!", "A definite quiet beach to visit, hardly anyone here. No facilities unfortunately but to be fair there was a bar being built when we arrived but yet to open the following weekend.", "Gorgeous little bay with the most atmospheric beach bar. Came in both daytime and nighttime and neither disappointed. Vibes there are so relaxed, the chill out music and general feel of the place is definitely something you need to experience yourself "]}}
2. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Havajska", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy"], "description": "Tiny pebble beach surrounded by cliffs & accessible by carved staircase, known for its strong waves.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Excellent free beach near Pula. We went there the last week of August, arriving around 10:00 AM. The main reef was crowded, but there were still some shaded spots available. A good spot to dive into the blue water and relax. Bring your own gear, as it's free and there are no services nearby. The water is clear, with some small fish but also many transparent jellyfish. Free parking is about a 10-minute walk away.", "The beach is beautifully located, but unfortunately very crowded. Due to the nearby hotel complexes and the popularity of the place, there are a lot of people on the beach. There are also many jellyfish there. It is purely a rocky and pebble beach, so a sleeping mat or similar may be useful for lying down.", "Great beach here, very secluded and has it's own privacy! Beach is rocky of course, but one of the better ones and very clear. Can have a great swim here. Easy to get up and down from the beach via the stairs. Shady areas to the sides."]}}
4. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Ambrela Beach", "tags": ["beach", "pebble", "crowdy", "family_friendly"], "description": "Popular pebble beach on Verudela in Pula, known for its shallow sea access, family-friendly setting, nearby parking, and a wide range of beach facilities and water activities.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["It was crowded, even though we were here after rain. It gets deep quickly, there were thousands of small jellyfish in the water, it was strange at first, but you get used to it. We were able to park for free at ARTPARK, although it is difficult to find a free space. Nice, clean beach, there is a side beach, showers are free.", "Clean water, pebble beach. But very crowded in summer.", "A gorgeous beach. The surrounding area is beautiful and clean. There's a couple of meters of sandy entry into the water. Otherwise, there are rocks all around, so protect your feet!", "A very nice beach. Crystal-clear water. Not cold. A food and drink stand. Restrooms. Everything you need for a day out."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
7. {"type": "marina", "properties": {"name": "ACI Marina Pula", "tags": ["marina", "city_center", "restaurant", "near_attractions"], "description": "City marina in the heart of Pula, known for its protected harbour setting, full nautical services, boat rentals, and unique views of the Roman Arena.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["ACI Marina in Pula is a top-notch spot for boaters and visitors alike. Well-maintained docks, friendly staff, and beautiful views make it perfect for sailing, relaxing by the water, or enjoying nearby cafes and restaurants.", "Very good Marina restaurant, helpful and friendly Marinero. Clean sanitary facilities, in the middle of the city. Can be noisy sometimes. Marina ist best contacted if you are already quite near if via VHF. Mobile phone is also possible.", "The marina is nice and spacious. You can walk above the coast and admire the boats and views."]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
9. {"type": "castle", "properties": {"name": "Fort Valmaggiore", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "military_history", "near_beach"], "description": "Historic Austro-Hungarian fortress in the Valmaggiore area near Štinjan, known for its robust military architecture, underground tunnel, and abandoned setting close to the coast.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Cool fort to visit. The fort has many rooms near the entrance, with two tunnels leading to a deeper bunker that has openings for shooting. Of course, some bats live inside, so please don’t disturb them. You can fully explore the fort in about 20 to 25 minutes. Some corridors are closed, and there’s no old equipment left inside the bunker. There is no parking nearby, the closest parking is a 10min hike. If you're into exploring or world war history I would recommend visiting.", "One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. As others it was conserved with EU funds few years ago but it is obviously left to decay after that. Very interesting nevertheless. I suggest going here in a pair or a group as some of the spaces are obviously used by drug consumers.", "Spooky place if you’re alone there, but still fun to investigate. Worth to visit if you in these parts. Parking is before bike sign, short walk from there."]}}
10. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}

1. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "fries", "vegetarian", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Piantina Fine Fast Food", "phone": "+385 91 578 7970", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Sa 12:00-23:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Zadarska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast food spot in Pula serving burgers, grilled sandwiches, salads and fries, with a menu that mixes classic comfort food with a few more creative options.", "reviews": ["The food was delicious and the Service was great. We felt very comfortable.The burgers are fried before our eyes. The salads and bread are also fresh and very delicious. Gluten-free options are also available.", "Good location in the centre of pula parking easy to find we found parking immediately. Very cute and nice tables and pretty inside. The burger and the salad were amazing! I recommend and the waiter was really nice and welcoming😁", "14.90€ for a combo: Burger of choice, french fries, and a drink of choice. I went with a 'smoker' and it was so good. The patty was juicy, and the fries were fine.", "We are there for 5 adults and 3 young children on a rainy Monday and we had a great time. The plates are quite generous ! We ate hamburgers, cheeseburger, honey chicken sandwich and a chicken salad with some fries and it was good. The cook was very friendly with the kids and even gave us a free iced tea. Thank you again for that !"], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "cevapi", "kebab", "fries", "salads"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Fast Food Station 0 - Dva asa", "phone": "+385 52 235 324", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:30; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Trg I istarske brigade", "rating": 4.5, "description": "A casual fast-food spot at the main bus station in Pula, serving burgers, ćevapi, kebabs, tortillas, toast sandwiches, fries, and quick drinks for an easy meal on the go.", "reviews": ["Very friendly and helpful service, and large portions at a very good price. The food was delicious; a great recommendation for quick travel food! Unfortunately, there were no vegetarian options besides fries and salad.", "Amazing food for super cheap. Fries were incredible, chicken wrap was really good. Chef was super nice and hard working. Great experience overall would highly recommend for cheap travel food :)"], "price": "low"}}
3. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
4. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["kebab", "burgers", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kebab & Burger Pula", "phone": "+385 91 612 0199", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 11:00-01:00; Fr-Sa 11:00-03:00; Su 11:00-01:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.8, "description": "A casual kebab and burger bar near the Pula Arena, known for XXL portions, freshly prepared meat, and quick, satisfying street food. The menu includes kebabs, tortillas, burgers, falafel options, fries, and drinks, making it a convenient stop for a fast meal close to one of the city’s main landmarks.", "reviews": ["Big portions and delicious food! We had the veggie falafel tortillas and veggie burgers — both were super tasty and fresh. The fries were perfectly crisp. Definitely worth a visit!", "Great Donair restaurant near arena. There is some tables inside to eat at if not doing take out. The portions are huge and the prices are very reasonable. Highly recommend.", "One of the best chicken kebabs I ever did eat. Lovely lads working in the grill and the food is great. Never thought I would have one of my best kebabs in Pula. But, hey! These guys do it so well.", "Amazingly tasty chicken kebabs, very very big portions, and the sweet and spicy sauce was delicious! Staff were lovely and funny, and quick! Would absolutely go again on next visit"], "price": "low"}}
5. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["seafood", "burgers", "grill", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "69 Food", "phone": "+385 97 610 5322", "opening_hours": "Mo 12:00-21:00; Tu off; We-Su 12:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "18", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A city-center street food spot on main street, known for seafood specialties, burgers, grilled chicken, and a modern fast-food concept with a strong local identity.", "reviews": ["Cosy bar, wine measure was very generous with great, fast service same for the food orders. Lovely setting at the start of the old town. Food was very tasty.", "Mood, food and value for money absolutely TOP. For a small snack or a delicious burger during the city stroll in Pula stop there again and again.", "Very happy with this experience. Nice staff, fresh produce and well worked. Very good beer. If you’re looking to take a little break to eat don’t hesitate!", "The food is amazing and so so delicious. I had problems deciding which main to order and ended up having the tuna steak burger which was crazy good. As the portions are quite big, I didn't take something else but was looking at the tables around me and all of their menu items looked just mouthwatering. Their draft beers are also on point. The staff is also extremely polite, fast in service and greets everyone with a bit of jokes and small talk, which i totally liked. Highly recommend this place!"], "price": null}}
6. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "fries", "desserts", "coffee", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "McDonald's", "phone": "+385 52 496 476", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "101", "addr:street": "Ulica Rimske Centurijacije", "rating": 4.0, "description": "Classic, long-running fast-food chain located next to a shopping center, known for its burgers and fries", "reviews": ["🍟 Everyone knows McDonald’s, so I really don’t need to write much about it. The food tastes the same almost everywhere. Even though we came from Germany, it tastes the same here in Croatia (Pula) = fast food. However, in this evening I would like to focus more on the team in this review tonight. I even think it was the shop manager or his deputy (at the McCafe stand) who was so nice and accommodating, it was about a little milk for the kids and we were immediately offered milk in a to-go cup for on the go. Thank you very much, because that doesn't happen often these days!", "It is situated right next to a parking lot for buses so ideal for bus to stop - just across. The entrance is disabled people friendly since the restaurant is on flat ground. It has kids section on the terrace that is separated from the road so they are safe. We came with bus full of students, the service was immaculate and fast (off season!)", "Just your standard McDonald’s. Service was fast, food was delicious. As an English person I was very pleased to find a sundae which is discontinued in my country."], "price": null}}
7. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "ice_cream", "coffee"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": false, "name": "Stoja Fast Food", "phone": null, "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Stoja", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot near the beach in Stoja, offering burgers, sandwiches, coffee, soft drinks, ice cream, with covered outdoor seating and sea views.", "reviews": ["Great little fast food restaurant, with very fair prices and decent choice of food, drink and ice-cream. Parking nearby (free). Had food went for a swim and returned for ice-cream and cold drink", "Best Ice cream in Pula and around. Coffee is out of this world good. Food is great as well. Very pleasent place and staff is very kind, especially young blond server. We are very frequent guests and our friends are very pleased as well.", "Amazing food, waiters came quickly the ice cream is very good, yiu cab pay by cash or card"], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Green", "phone": "+385 52 356 444", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 10:00-22:00; Su 14:00-22:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 4.2, "description": "A casual fast-food spot in Pula’s city center, known for burgers, toast sandwiches, tortillas, salads, and quick meals.", "reviews": ["Great service. We had a Fried Chicken Wrap which was very delicious and perfectly rolled. Even spread filling from top to bottom. Perfect place for a fast snack to go.", "We ordered a falafel and chicken wrap. Both super good quality and value for money. Also the toast were large, can easily share one for 2 kids.", "Perfect food whatever you take, for the price and quality is far ahead best place to eat in Pula. Went to few restaurants but Green is far ahead comparing quality, amount you get and prices. Nothing but best for Green.👏🏼"], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "salads", "seafood", "vegetarian", "desserts", "pancakes"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Sandwich Club", "phone": "+385 52 386 182", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Sisplac", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A casual fast-food diner in Pula, offering fresh snacks and meals, outdoor seating, vegan and vegetarian options, and a kids’ corner.", "reviews": ["Good fast food with burger options, sandwiches and unique dishes. Friendly staff, fast service. Tables also outside and takeaway. Good value for money.", "I had a wonderful experience at this restaurant. The dishes were delicious and reasonably priced. The staff was very friendly and attentive. I will definitely be coming back!", "Stopped in at Sandwich Club 🥪 yesterday before heading to Aquarium Pula. The food was excellent (try the Cubanito, they have nice Coffee too ☕), the service fantastic (staff were very friendly & good company) & the atmosphere was great (the Spotify playlist having been expertly selected by the team). Couldn't find fault with this place at all - great value for a very reasonable price."], "price": null}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Arena Pula", "tags": ["amphitheatre", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "landmark", "events", "concerts"], "description": "Roman amphitheatre from the 1st century and one of Pula’s most iconic landmarks, known for its monumental architecture, rich history, and major cultural events.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Incredibly well preserved ruins in a very cool part of town. So much to see around and inside. They also use the middle for various things. They had an ice rink there when I went.", "Pula is a small town, so seeing such a grandiose structure from the era of the great Roman Empire here is both unexpected and impressive. There are far fewer visitors than at the Roman Colosseum, so everyone has the unique opportunity to find a secluded spot, stand, and reflect on eternity, on how times, customs, and games have changed over the centuries. Don't miss the small but fascinating museum located in the arena's underground chambers—it's dedicated primarily to olive oil production in Istria.", "Gorgeous arena. A must see when in Pula. Beautiful weather helped to get some beautiful shots. More than 2000 years old and one of six biggest amphitheatres still standing.. breathtakingly stunning.", "What a site to see! Amazing roman arena built between 27–68 AD. Sixth largest in the world. There is a fee to enter and you are free to walk around once inside. There are QR codes that provide a self guided tour using your phone. Bring ear buds or headphones for the audio. This is one of the best preserved amphitheaters in the world. This is a must see."]}}
2. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Malo rimsko kazalište", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "historic", "events", "concerts", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman theatre in the heart of Pula, dating back to the 1st century, today restored as a unique open-air archaeological site and performance venue that combines ancient heritage with contemporary cultural events.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I attended a Ludovico Einaudi concert at the Small Roman Theatre in Pula and it was amazing. The venue is intimate and historic, giving the performance a magical atmosphere. Perfect for enjoying music up close in a unique setting.", "Really not much to be seen here, just an outdoor amphitheatre that's typically empty otherwise; the route here appears a bit difficult, seems like you're walking on private property inbetween buildings.", "Awesome venue for concerts. It's best to bring your own seat cushion or pillow for comfort!"]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Scala", "phone": "+385 98 898 484", "opening_hours": null, "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Ozad Arene", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A simple café bar right next to the Pula Arena, best known for its unique terrace with a direct view of the amphitheatre. It is a relaxed spot for coffee or a drink in one of the city’s most iconic locations.", "reviews": ["Perfect place to watch the Arena and enjoy a cold drink! Personnel is nice and friendly. Prices are regular. Have you never visited Croatia before? Try Pasareta, a real Croatian drink! 💪🏼 with lots of ice cubes, perfect! We only had drinks, no food. They have a lot of ice creams!", "Great coffee bar / drinks. Best spot in the area for a quiet coffee and to enjoy the arena. The staff all spoke many languages and were very helpful on giving local recommendations.", "Service extremely friendly and attentive. Nice ambience (with music from the amphitheater). Just perfect, where you feel comfortable and enjoy the sunset. Can only recommend👌"], "price": "medium"}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
8. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Titov Cadillac", "tags": ["attraction", "museum", "national_park", "historic", "island"], "description": "Historic Cadillac Eldorado Cabriolet on Brijuni, displayed as one of the park’s best-known attractions and associated with Josip Broz Tito, who used it to drive around the island with numerous distinguished guests.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Nice car in excellent condition like it’s new fully restored.", "Excellent model with top-notch equipment for that time. Preserved and in excellent condition. Can be rented for driving"]}}
9. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
10. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
4. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Mozaik - Kažnjavanje Dirke", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula featuring the Roman mosaic of the Punishment of Dirce, a rare and finely preserved mythological floor mosaic discovered near St. Mary Formosa.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Kind of hard to find. You have to go around the back of the main street and through a parking lot. It almost looks like you are walking into someone's driveway. It is not well lit so if you want better pictures, go during the day.", "Very nice but looks like in a hidden area. You can follow the sign as well as use Google Maps. You may enter any time during the day at no charge.", "Absolutely go and see it - a beautifully preserved mosaic from I believe the 2nd or 3rd century AD within it's own protective room. No entry fee or anything; just observe the mosaic from street level and it is about 3-4 feet below street level. A little bit off the beaten track and the street signs aren't clear, but regardless it's a quiet and nice area so definitely make the detour."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
6. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
7. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Zerostrasse", "tags": ["museum", "historic", "military_history", "city_center", "near_attractions", "family_friendly"], "description": "Underground tunnel complex beneath central Pula, created as a wartime shelter system during the Austro-Hungarian period and today presented as a historic site known as Zerostrasse.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Nice tunnel system that is easy to navigate. There seems to be very little information about the tunnels themselves and more information about various things that happened in Pula around the area. Tickets to the tunnel gove you access to the fort above.", "Tunnels underneath the citadel with access to the citadel included in the price if you work your way up. I did this in reverse and made my way down through the tunnels. Blissfully cool after the heat of the exterior. Fascinated by the tunnels and side rooms. Would have liked to see more information provided on their wartime use, and not just learn about the trams. Found a lovely piece of art painted onto a wall in one of the side rooms, left there by a previous resident who had tried to bring a little of the outside indoors perhaps? A little forgotten masterpiece just waiting to be discovered. Just kind of stumbled across it as I explored, but maybe should have been signposted with a bit of context provided. The tunnels exit at locations in the old town. As a tourist myself this left me almost instantly in the shopping area at the end of my visit. I am sure not the original builders intention, but very welcome for someone like myself trying to get the most out of their day.", "Fascinating underground tunnels. Zerostrasse is a network of WWI-era tunnels beneath Pula, originally built as shelters. It’s a cool and quiet escape from the summer heat, with interesting historical displays along the way. Not a long visit, but definitely worth it if you're curious about the city's wartime past."]}}
8. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
9. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Agripinina kuća", "tags": ["archeological_site", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Archaeological site in central Pula near the Roman Forum, known for its layered remains from pre-Roman to early medieval periods and for the discovery of a portrait of Agrippina the Younger.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Wild looking ruins that are right behind a liquor store. You can walk around the platforms to get better views. There are also 2 cats.", "Archaeological site, excavated house from the Roman period. A fun contrast with the modern style. Behind of a busy streets. It is nice and quiet here.", "Beautiful remains, 'hidden' between houses which i think gives it charm. There were also a lot of adorable cats"]}}
10. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Sol Garden - Hostel with a Soul", "tags": ["hostel", "near_attractions"], "description": "A simple and budget-friendly stay close to Pula Arena and the city’s historic center, offering dormitories and twin rooms with access to shared bathrooms. Guests can use a fully equipped shared kitchen, relax in the garden or on the terrace, and easily reach the waterfront, restaurants, bars and main transport connections on foot.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["The hostel was very clean, it had a pleasant smell, and it was very quiet. It has a large kitchen and a spacious balcony. In the rooms, there are also small lockers that can be locked using the card provided by the reception to access the doors. Nearby, there are 2–3 markets, a coffee bar, and it is also close to the Arena as well as the bus station.", "The hostel is very good, quiet, and has several places nearby such as markets, coffee bars, and other shops. It also has a nice balcony, a large kitchen, and spacious bathrooms. The rooms are clean, air-conditioned, and everything is in order.", "Location and Staff! Excellent environment"]}}

1. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
2. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
3. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
4. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "Dječje igralište Viška ulica", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Neighbourhood playground in Pula with basic play equipment, a fenced play area, and a family-friendly setting near Fort Casoni Vecchi and St. Paul’s Church.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Sfinga Verudela", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Apartment accommodation in the Verudela area of Pula, offering a terrace, free parking, free WiFi, and a convenient location within walking distance of Saccorgiana Beach.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Very lovely family holiday stay.", "Very beautiful place in a quiet part of town. Walking distance to the beach 5 min. Shopping center 5-7 min by car. The equipment of the large apartment is absolutely sufficient. The rooms and living room have their own balcony. The air conditioning unit cools all rooms sufficiently. The price corresponds to the quality and comfort. Great satisfaction."]}}
6. {"type": "guest_house", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Sunčica", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "garden", "free_parking", "playground"], "description": "A spacious and family-friendly apartment in a quiet residential area of Pula, ideal for a relaxed stay away from city noise. It offers a garden, terrace, private parking, Wi-Fi and a fully equipped kitchen, with added conveniences such as a children’s playground and easy access to the city, beaches and nearby nature areas.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Great and spacious apartment with loads of amenities.", "We stayed for two weeks in this beautiful apartment with a garden and parking spaces, equipped with every comfort. The owners, who live upstairs and have separate access, were very quiet (like ghosts). The owner welcomed us with local delicacies and wine, a fruit basket... midweek for breakfast, she offered us a platter of local cured meats and cheeses, and as we appreciated it, she also gave us vacuum-packed cured meats they make, ice cream, and sweets for the children. Highly recommended; try it and believe it", "The owner is very kind, and you can feel the love she has put into the apartment. The hygiene and amenities are of a very high standard, and the beds are comfortable. If we have the chance, we would love to return here."]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "SWEET APARTMENT TONY", "tags": ["apartment", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Comfortable apartment in Pula with a terrace, balcony, free private parking, and a fully equipped kitchen, set a short drive from the Arena.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["Family was help-full and kind. Even gave us a homemade cake :) We had all we needs in their apartment. Close to the apartment is shopping mall with all variety of shops. 3 min by car, maybe 10 by foot.", "Everything was perfect! The owner was super helpful and friendly! They helped us with bringing the suit see and provided everything we needed. The apartment is super well equipped and kids friendly. Supermarket, city center and beaches are nearby. The best part was AC in this hot summer! Sofa bed could be better but manageable", "Very nice apartment with big bathroom, well equipped kitchen, air conditioning in each room, large terrace."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park žrtava fašizma", "tags": ["park", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Neighbourhood park in Šijana, Pula, with a children’s playground, benches, and a pleasant green space for everyday relaxation.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}
10. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
2. {"type": "chalet", "properties": {"name": "Villa Elite", "tags": ["chalet", "villa", "pool", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "near_beach", "playground"], "description": "Spacious modern villa in Pula near the sea, offering two private outdoor pools, multiple en-suite bedrooms, large terraces, and family-friendly outdoor amenities for a comfortable group stay.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Amazing Villa! Had the best vacation ever, totally recommend it! Everything is clean and the people who rent are super kind.", "Fantastic villa and a very nice landlady. We had a wonderful holiday. Highly recommended!!"]}}
3. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Grand Hotel Brioni Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "family_friendly"], "description": "Luxury seaside hotel in Pula with panoramic Adriatic views, elegant rooms and suites, fine dining, spa and fitness facilities, and direct access to the beach.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Fantastic hotel! Fantastic place! Highly recommended if you really want to relax. Even though it's the same chain as the hotel near the Plaza (which I've stayed at three times), I only recommend the Brioni from now on. The Plaza is like a highway motel. I regret not discovering the Brioni sooner. The Plaza should take a cue from its neighbor, from service to comfort.", "We were here before Easter, so it was pleasantly quiet. The hotel is very clean and offers a beautiful view, even from the sauna, which is also very well-maintained and inviting. The room service was perfect and couldn't have been better. I'm not sure if the buffet selection is always so limited. For the price, we would have liked a bit more variety, especially at breakfast. However, the quality of the food was consistently very good. Overall, a lovely stay with a few minor drawbacks; we would come back.", "I really enjoyed my stay. Everything was as it should be in a hotel, I will definitely recommend this place.", "The best hotel we've been to. Great and friendly stuff, helped us with all of our questions, clean rooms and good food"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
5. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Vila Lovorka", "tags": ["hotel", "villa", "national_park", "island", "garden", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach"], "description": "Elegant seaside villa on Veliki Brijun with sea views towards Valbandon and Pula, offering spacious accommodation, a spa area, a Mediterranean garden, and a peaceful stay enriched by historic stone fragments.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": null}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Ribarska Koliba Resort", "tags": ["hotel", "resort", "coastal", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "pool", "restaurant", "events"], "description": "A stylish seaside resort in Pula known for its long hospitality tradition, elegant rooms and scenic setting near Marina Veruda and Marina Bunarina. It offers a quiet stay close to beaches, the aquarium and major city sights, with modern amenities such as free WiFi, parking and a pool area.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I've been here a few times, with friends and family and I've been very satisfied every time. The rooms are spacious, clean and well laid out. The breakfast is excellent with a lot of choice and a beautiful view of the marina. The staff is friendly and fantastic, to be commended for their flexibility regarding check-in and check-out and all the necessary services and information. Real value for money!", "Lovely euro boutique hotel that exceeds expectations. Great close in views of the marina from the third floor. Rooms are great, functional and have all the amenities. Very nice outdoor deck. On site Michelin restaurant is a bonus. You will have to Uber bus or drive to the Pula old town. There is a fine sea walk and beaches nearby and a few luxury hotels with nice eating options. Recommended.", "Incredible stay. We stayed for 5 nights as part of our honeymoon journey throughout Croatia. We were kindly upgraded to the 'Fuoco 1' apartment and it was superb, immaculately clean, spacious with fantastic views of the marina from the private balcony. The staff were so friendly and helpful when my wife required some medical attention for her infected insect bite they signposted us to the tourist hospital. We dined at the on-site restaurant twice because the quality of food was so good and was reasonably priced. Aperol spritz only 8€ as an example. Highly reccomended and we hope to visit again in future anniversaries."]}}
7. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Vea Histria Apartments Pula", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly"], "description": "Elegant and well-equipped apartments in a quieter part of Pula, designed for a comfortable and practical stay close to the city and nearby beaches. The units offer private terraces, modern kitchens, air conditioning, Wi-Fi and parking, making them a convenient choice for couples, families and guests who want easy access to both urban attractions and the coast.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Very good location, close to shops, restaurants, city center, port, Roman arena. It has its own parking which is a big plus for Croatia, where it is hard to find parking and everything is for a fee (price varies between 1.5-4 euros/hour). The beds are comfortable, apartment equipped with everything you need, it is spacious. Check-in is easy, you get the details from the owner. You are also close to the sea (which is rocky, you definitely need water shoes, otherwise you can't go).", "The apartment was comfortable and clean, spacious enough, and not too hot despite the 35°C (95°F) outside. Convenient check-in and check-out, and car parking available. The location was also convenient, very close to the ring road, for us who traveled a lot in the surrounding area. If I were to return to Pula, this would be my first choice.", "I recommend this place. The owner is always helpful. Quiet and peaceful."]}}
8. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Hotel Park Plaza Arena Pula", "tags": ["hotel", "coastal", "near_beach", "pool", "wellness", "free_parking", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Modern seaside hotel on Punta Verudela in Pula, offering sea views, saltwater pools, wellness facilities, and direct access to the beach in a pine forest setting.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Lovely hotel, with an excellent buffet breakfast, comfortable rooms, efficient laundry service, and a short walk to the sea, with a beautiful view; we would stay there again", "So far, it's been a fantastic holiday. The rooms are quite modern and perfectly adequate for two people. There's a wide selection at breakfast, and the food is very tasty. The staff is always friendly and helpful. We recommend booking bed and breakfast, as there are plenty of restaurants on this small peninsula. What bothers us personally is that no one seems to be monitoring the hotel's sunbathing area. About 50% of the people who lounge there aren't hotel guests, so it's impossible to find a spot by lunchtime. You're basically forced to reserve sunbeds early in the morning.", "What a beautiful location! The beds were very comfortable. The breakfast was amazing!"]}}
9. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartment Falu", "tags": ["apartment", "family_friendly", "pool", "playground", "free_parking"], "description": "A comfortable apartment in Štinjan with two bedrooms, a private terrace and practical amenities for a relaxed stay near the coast. Guests can enjoy an outdoor pool, children’s playground, free parking and easy access to Hidrobaza Beach, while Pula and Brijuni are both within easy reach.", "rating": null, "reviews": ["We had a wonderful stay at Apartment Falu for our family holiday to Istria. Martina and Rob were the most kind and hospitable hosts.. The apartment was well equipped with everything we needed and was very clean. The pool was our personal favourite and we made good use of it during our stay. I would definitely return to Apartment Falu and would recommend it to others. Thank you Martina and Rob", "We were greeted very warmly with freshly baked pastries. The hosts are helpful but not intrusive. The apartment is beautifully, practically, and lovingly furnished; we had the pool completely to ourselves."]}}
10. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Modo", "tags": ["hotel", "seaside", "near_beach", "family_friendly", "free_parking", "restaurant"], "description": "A modern seaside hotel in Pula set between the bays of Stoja and Valovine, offering sea-view rooms with balconies, free WiFi, free parking and easy access to nearby beaches. Its quiet location and convenient connection to the city make it suitable for families, couples and business travellers.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Great little hotel in a great location. The staff is very professional and friendly. The premises are modernly decorated and clean. A rich selection of food for breakfast.", "Cosy hotel, spacious room with balcony overlooking the sea. The manager on our arrival was friendly and explained what to visit in Pula and nearby. In addition he suggested (and we went there on the last day) to visit Motovun, castle and village where you eat dishes with truffles. The breakfast of the hotel is great, varied both savory and sweet. At night absolute silence, very relaxing.", "The location was amazing ! We had a balcony that was perfect for watching the sunsets . We easily walked into town ( there also is a bus option ) the rooms were clean and comfortable . My only negative was the AC shut off randomly . The front desk said it turned off every 2 hours and needed to be reset . This was not a great for a cool night sleep without getting up a number of times to reset the AC . Breakfast was very good and it was lovely to eat out on the deck . Staff was friendly and helpful ."]}}

