5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "vegan", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Giardino Bar", "phone": "+385 99 403 4680", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-24:00; Sa 07:00-01:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "3", "addr:street": "Giardini", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A cozy café in the center of Pula, ideal for coffee, ice cream, drinks, and a relaxing break.", "reviews": ["Nice place, great drink (teragino), the music wasn't loud, so it wasn't a problem to hear each other. And we got free chips and nuts with the drink.", "Great location and atmosphere and an extremely polite and helpful waiter, a real refreshment!", "Good music, delicious coffee, even a vegan milk option, and clean bathrooms."], "price": "low"}}
6. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["chinese", "asian", "meat", "seafood", "vegetarian"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Peking", "phone": "+385 52 392 256", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "21", "addr:street": "Monte Paradiso", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A long-running Chinese restaurant, offering a broad menu of classic Chinese dishes including noodles, rice, duck, beef, pork, chicken, seafood, soups, and fried starters, with dine-in and takeout options.", "reviews": ["Staying in Pula for a few days and the restaurant is very close by, I read the reviews which are certainly mixed but thought we would give it a try. It seems that there is one guy cooking and one lady serving so we had to wait a long time for drinks and food but the food when it arrived was lovely, one of the best Chinese meals we’ve ever had. Give the place a try but expect a wait for your food! Just have a beer whilst waiting 😉", "Very good food. Good Chinese with lots of choice. Would recommend it to anyone. Nice service. The outside terrace is a bit dated and noisy due to the amount of cars that drive past so it is recommended to eat inside and it looks nice there.", "Ordered a takeaway away to be delivered. Came within 30 minutes. Nice food and very good value for money with big portions."], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "meat", "wine", "vegetarian", "vegan", "gluten_free", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kantina", "phone": "+385 52 214 054", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "16", "addr:street": "Flanatička", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Classic Mediterranean eatery with stone walls & a terrace serving seafood, meat dishes & wine.", "reviews": ["Excellent food, friendly and prompt staff. Highly recommand. It is also 8 minutes walk from The Arena and 5 minutes from the beautiful center.", "Impeccable Service (they speak Italian), the place is quiet and out of the confusion, we were offered an appetizer with cheese and truffles which was delicious, then we had salmon and white fish and they were really exceptional. Great value for money. We arrived on foot walking through the center but if you want there is also a convenient parking. Highly recommended!", "Kantina Restaurant was a very beautiful surprise! We found the restaurant based on other very good reviews and we were more than satisfied. The restaurant is located a few hundred meters from Paula's center, and is very easy to reach. We had a full meal based on truffle dishes that were delicious. The waiter was extremely professional and kind and, in addition to our order, we have received a starter and a small amaro at the end of the dinner. Highly recommend!", "Dining at Restaurant Kantina in Pula was an absolute delight from start to finish. The whole fish I ordered was nothing short of spectacular—fresh, perfectly cooked, and bursting with authentic Mediterranean flavors that truly showcased the quality of local seafood. What made the experience even more memorable was the impeccable service. The staff delivered a level of fine dining hospitality that felt both professional and warmly personal."], "price": "high"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "meat"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Bistro Valkane", "phone": "+385 52 387 589", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Lungomare", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A modern restaurant on the Lungomare promenade, next to the tennis courts, serving Croatian and Istrian cuisine with terrace seating.", "reviews": ["We had some of the best food in Croatia at this restaurant, it was amazing. We had tuna steak and calamari which were both amazing!! The service was sensational as well, the waitress even offered her jacket to me as the breeze was a bit cool. I could recommend this restaurant highly enough based on our experience.", "One of the best places to eat! The food is fresh and absolutely fantastic, the atmosphere is wonderful,good price and Marijana is truly the best waitress in all of Europe. Thank you for everything! See you next year❤️", "Lovely restaurant, one of the few in the area with waterfront location. Popular with locals and tourist, great food at reasonable prices. Black rice seafood risotto, and meat plate (mixed grill) were really nice."], "price": null}}
9. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "meat", "vegetarian", "wine", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": null, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Epulon Food & Wine", "phone": "+385 98 949 9023", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 12:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Epulonova", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A stylish wine and food bar in central Pula, Epulon combines traditional Istrian cuisine with seasonal, more refined dishes, with a strong focus on local ingredients, wines, tapas, and a relaxed indoor terrace setting.", "reviews": ["Hospitality was excellent. Service and food was delicious. I felt like at home.", "Great restaurant, food was delicious and very friendly stuff...", "The place is spectacular for an outing of any kind. The atmosphere is very nice and refined. The furniture, the sweetness of the wench... all perfect. Good prices.", "Absolutely LOVED the place! The waitress was lovely, easy to talk to and helped me pick exactly what I wanted. I came back the second time because of her:) The food was delicious and nicely served. I didn't have to wait much. The atmosphere, music - everything was great. This place is a hidden gem, recommend to those who'd like to eat and relax 💎"], "price": "high"}}
10. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["mediterranean", "seafood", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Furia Restaurant", "phone": "+385 97 683 9992", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 08:00-15:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "9", "addr:street": "Narodni trg", "rating": 4.7, "description": "A local seafood spot inside Pula’s market building, Furia is known for fresh, fast, and affordable fish dishes and simple Adriatic specialties.", "reviews": ["A bit spartan, but very good. Fish definitely fresh and very tasty. Friendly and friendly staff.", "Very freshly prepared, very tasty and at a more than fair price on an outdoor terrace. Highly recommended!!", "4 stars. Located on the top floor of the marketplace building. Offers seating inside the building or on the balcony. Food was nice and fresh. Understandably not everything on the menu was in season / available. We had the octopus salad and a couple of pieces of fish. Fresh and cooked well. Washed down with a lovely glass of local white wine. €30 for 2 people. Can't fault the value. Happily recommend this place.", "A place to eat fish in centre of town. They have wild fish in daly offer, as well as grown. Prices are totally acceptable. The staff is amazing, chef is encrideble! Sometimes you have to wait for the table a while, but it is completely worth it. Every time we ate here it was great 🤍🌊🌞"], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
2. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
3. {"type": "fountain", "properties": {"name": "Maketa Pule", "tags": ["tactile_model", "city_center", "interactive", "family_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Interactive tactile model of Pula in the city centre, offering a detailed 3D overview of the city layout, waterways, and key landmarks in a quick and educational way.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["I love seeing the miniature cities; and this one is even cooler because it has water spouting where the Adriatic Sea is; really neat.", "Small model of the city of Pula, with water. Good for exploring the city. Made of metal.", "A visual miniature of the charming city of Pula. It's a great introduction to general knowledge. I highly recommend it."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
5. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
6. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
7. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Tragovi dinosaura", "tags": ["attraction", "geopaleontological_site", "prehistoric", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A remarkable geopaleontological attraction where preserved dinosaur footprints reveal that ancient reptiles once walked this area around 130 to 100 million years ago. More than 200 footprints have been discovered across Brijuni, with visitor-accessible tracks on Veliki Brijun offering a rare and valuable glimpse into the prehistoric past.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["At first glance, nothing 'special' but when do you ever see real dinosaur footprints? I thought it was cool that they had a matching dinosaur statue next to it. If you're on the island, you should stop by there, too.", "Traces 100 million years old. Super exciting.", "It was simply amazing to see something like that. When and where else do you get the chance to admire original dinosaur footprints!? And the best part was, I was completely alone there (off-season, early June, around 5 pm), simply wonderful."]}}
8. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "MEMO Museum of good Memories", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "family_friendly", "near_attractions", "city_center"], "description": "Interactive multimedia museum in Pula near the Arena, dedicated to everyday life from the 1950s to the 1980s, with nostalgic objects, reconstructed interiors, and hands-on exhibits.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["We adored this little museum as we could compare our childhood experience with one in a different country. Plenty to see and some exhibits could be handled. We could also take our dog, which was a definite bonus! Tickets were not expensive. Very enjoyable!", "If you were born in 1970 - 1980 and you would like to remind, how it looked like in your home, just go and visit this museum. There is lot of stuff, which was used in those years and in fact, comparing to today, the life is much easier, but quicker. This museum is located on the way from Amfitheater to the city centrum, so you should not miss it with your mobile navigation. It is worth to visit.", "Very interesting museum if you are nostalgic person. We spend half hour inside. You can try and touch things. You can feel life from the past."]}}
9. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Titov Cadillac", "tags": ["attraction", "museum", "national_park", "historic", "island"], "description": "Historic Cadillac Eldorado Cabriolet on Brijuni, displayed as one of the park’s best-known attractions and associated with Josip Broz Tito, who used it to drive around the island with numerous distinguished guests.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Nice car in excellent condition like it’s new fully restored.", "Excellent model with top-notch equipment for that time. Preserved and in excellent condition. Can be rented for driving"]}}
10. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Avion-vjetrokaz", "tags": ["attraction", "aviation"], "description": "Outdoor aviation attraction near Pula at the Medulin sports airfield, featuring a former light aircraft mounted as a wind vane and memorial display celebrating local flying heritage.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Villa Bubi", "tags": ["apartment", "near_beach", "free_parking", "pet_friendly", "family_friendly", "wheelchair_accessible"], "description": "Comfortable apartments near the beach in Pula, offering terraces, free parking, barbecue facilities, and easy access to the city and Brijuni.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["Great helpful staff, nice and welcoming place. Close to the coast (5-10 minutes on foot), with great beaches. Guarded parking, air conditioning, garden grill. I recommend it to everyone!", "If you’re looking for a nice and quiet place to stay, with beautiful garden, this is place for you. Clean, cozy, pet friendly.. great host.. there is a parking lot, bikes to rent..", "This apartment is at a beautiful location, near to the beach, with nice and clean, well-equipped rooms (air conditioner, balcony). The host is very friendly and helpful. I would totally recommend to book a room in Villa Bubi! :)"]}}
2. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Safari park", "tags": ["safari_park", "zoo", "national_park", "family_friendly", "animals", "island"], "description": "Family-friendly safari park on Veliki Brijun with exotic and native animals, an ethno park, and a scenic train ride within Brijuni National Park.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Brijuni Safari Park is one of the most interesting attractions on the island of Veliki (Great) Brijun. Visitors mostly explore the park through a ride on a train and they can see various animals including zebras, ostriches, llamas, and peacocks. There are also sacred Indian cows (zebu), sea turtles and goats. However, the most impressive animal here is the Asian elephant Lanka who arrived on the island in 1972 as a gift from Indian Prime Minister Indira Gandhi.", "In my next life, I want to be born as an animal on Brijuni. The place is so beautiful, with the view on the sea. The grass is green, the animals all seem healthy and happy! Lenka (the elephant) is one of the longest living elephants (she's in her 60s).", "I recently had an unforgettable safari experience at the Brijuni Islands in Croatia. The natural beauty of the park is breathtaking, with lush landscapes, diverse wildlife, and stunning views all around. The safari tour was well-organized, and we had the chance to see various animals up close, making it an incredible adventure for nature lovers. One important tip: the ferry ride to the island costs only €10, so make sure you're not overcharged. Be cautious of potential scams, especially from people trying to sell overpriced tickets or unnecessary services outside the official vendors. Other than that, it was a fantastic trip, and I highly recommend it to anyone visiting Croatia!", "We really liked our stroll around Brijuni island. The safari park is a nice addition. Definitely check the tickets for the ferry to the island in advance. They sell out fast."]}}
3. {"type": "zoo", "properties": {"name": "Fazanerija", "tags": ["zoo", "animals", "family_friendly", "national_park", "island"], "description": "Small animal and bird area where visitors can see peacocks, turkeys, guinea fowl, parrots, and other birds, while the site also serves as a recovery and temporary care center for wild animals.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Don’t miss seeing this bird! Easy to find, unique experience", "Koji is awesome! He knows a few words, best one being 'tito'", "The animals seem content, and the facility was well-maintained. Of course, the buildings are old, and it's not a large zoo. But it's definitely worth a visit."]}}
4. {"type": "camp_site", "properties": {"name": "Arena Stoja", "tags": ["camp", "family_friendly", "coastal", "near_beach", "pet_friendly"], "description": "Seaside campsite on the Stoja peninsula in Pula, offering sea-view pitches, a peaceful natural setting, and direct access to the rocky coast.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Beautiful campsite on the Adriatic coast. We watched the dolphins in the evenings, which was very impressive. There's a very good restaurant on site, and everything is very clean. The staff at reception are very friendly, and the sanitary facilities are constantly cleaned. The bus to Pula stops right in front of the campsite, and you can also easily walk to the Colosseum in 35 minutes. We really enjoyed our stay here and would love to come back. The only minor drawback is that, unlike most campsites, there are no dog waste bags available anywhere on the grounds. A dog costs €7 per day.", "During our Istria tour in April 2026, we stayed here for two nights in our campervan. Five stars are well-deserved. Everything was clean and very nice. We were parked in the first row right by the sea and enjoyed the sunset. It was very quiet at night, and the staff were very friendly. We would gladly come back.", "Beautiful campsite by the sea. Clean and excellent sanitary facilities. Friendly welcome. Many facilities. Good price."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Valerijin park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "city_center", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic triangular park below the Pula Arena, known for its landscaped greenery, Mediterranean plants, and long connection to the city’s urban heritage.", "rating": 3.3, "reviews": ["This is a park located between two major attractions of Pula. There are a playground, some statues, benches to sit down, trees that provide shades, etc."]}}
6. {"type": "hotel", "properties": {"name": "Villa Carla", "tags": ["apartment", "hotel", "near_beach", "pool", "pet_friendly", "free_parking", "family_friendly"], "description": "Spacious villa apartment in Pula near Verudela, offering sea views, a shared pool, parking, and easy access to beaches, restaurants, and city attractions.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Robert was fantastic. He was extremely welcoming during our stay and helped us with anything we needed. The place was great and easily big enough for the 7 of us. 100% would come back. Thanks Robert", "Robert welcomed us on arrival and gave us a tour of the apartment. Such a nice and friendly soul. Very helpful and thoughtful and we made plans to speak to Robert during our stay so he could advise us of places to go and trips to do. Our first evening we spent at a restaurant just a few yards away and his recommendation was spot on. We returned there several times during our stay (Sopranos). Our stay was fantastic - the pool area is relatively small and is sometimes shaded but is a lovely spot. The front of the accommodation has a purpose built bbq area (covered) that we also made good use of a couple of evenings. The local grocery store is a two minute walk away. Go to the butchers section - you’ll be amazed at the quality and price of the fresh meat on offer. A 15 minute walk got us into Pula itself - the nearest beach is 10 minutes away and we were able to have a boat trip a day out in Rovinj and threw some fun on inflatables and quad bikes for good measure. A great stay.", "Truly exceptional hosts. So friendly and helpful, we were made to feel like family. The apartment had everything we needed and was a good base location for the things we wanted to explore. Hope to visit again one day!"]}}
7. {"type": "hostel", "properties": {"name": "Art Hostel Pipištrelo", "tags": ["hostel", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "near_attractions"], "description": "Hostel Pipištrelo is a small, stylish hostel in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Forum, Arena, Kastel and other main sights of the old town. It offers air-conditioned rooms, free WiFi, a shared lounge and a shared kitchen, combining a central location with a simple, comfortable stay. With only a few rooms and artistic details throughout the interior, the hostel has a more intimate, boutique feel than a classic budget hostel.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Always ready for help with anything or any need. Maybe a little tomuch aerosols but I air the room before .", "Perfect location with a view of the water from our room, 1km from amphitheater, and only minutes to walk to all restaurants and shops. Beaches 10 mins by bus. It was hot during our stay, and communal areas do not have aircon.", "Great location walking distance to plenty of bars/restaurants. Clean rooms and very responsive host. Highly recommend!"]}}
8. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
10. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}

1. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Arena Pula", "tags": ["amphitheatre", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "landmark", "events", "concerts"], "description": "Roman amphitheatre from the 1st century and one of Pula’s most iconic landmarks, known for its monumental architecture, rich history, and major cultural events.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Incredibly well preserved ruins in a very cool part of town. So much to see around and inside. They also use the middle for various things. They had an ice rink there when I went.", "Pula is a small town, so seeing such a grandiose structure from the era of the great Roman Empire here is both unexpected and impressive. There are far fewer visitors than at the Roman Colosseum, so everyone has the unique opportunity to find a secluded spot, stand, and reflect on eternity, on how times, customs, and games have changed over the centuries. Don't miss the small but fascinating museum located in the arena's underground chambers—it's dedicated primarily to olive oil production in Istria.", "Gorgeous arena. A must see when in Pula. Beautiful weather helped to get some beautiful shots. More than 2000 years old and one of six biggest amphitheatres still standing.. breathtakingly stunning.", "What a site to see! Amazing roman arena built between 27–68 AD. Sixth largest in the world. There is a fee to enter and you are free to walk around once inside. There are QR codes that provide a self guided tour using your phone. Bring ear buds or headphones for the audio. This is one of the best preserved amphitheaters in the world. This is a must see."]}}
2. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Istrian Olive Oil Museum", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Museum in central Pula near the Arena, dedicated to the history and culture of Istrian olive oil, with interactive exhibits, guided tastings, and a shop featuring award-winning local products.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["Definitely recommend the tour including tasting. Museum is quite small but still you can learn a lot of interesting stuff about olive oil and its history. But the tasting was the most catchy part!", "Lovely museum with very interesting information. Highly recommend the extended (gold) tasting, as you get to try a lot of different flavours. Not doing any tasting when you go here means that you are missing out. The people working there were very nice and spoke good English."]}}
3. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
4. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "MEMO Museum of good Memories", "tags": ["museum", "interactive", "family_friendly", "near_attractions", "city_center"], "description": "Interactive multimedia museum in Pula near the Arena, dedicated to everyday life from the 1950s to the 1980s, with nostalgic objects, reconstructed interiors, and hands-on exhibits.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["We adored this little museum as we could compare our childhood experience with one in a different country. Plenty to see and some exhibits could be handled. We could also take our dog, which was a definite bonus! Tickets were not expensive. Very enjoyable!", "If you were born in 1970 - 1980 and you would like to remind, how it looked like in your home, just go and visit this museum. There is lot of stuff, which was used in those years and in fact, comparing to today, the life is much easier, but quicker. This museum is located on the way from Amfitheater to the city centrum, so you should not miss it with your mobile navigation. It is worth to visit.", "Very interesting museum if you are nostalgic person. We spend half hour inside. You can try and touch things. You can feel life from the past."]}}
5. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Malo rimsko kazalište", "tags": ["archaeological_site", "roman", "historic", "events", "concerts", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman theatre in the heart of Pula, dating back to the 1st century, today restored as a unique open-air archaeological site and performance venue that combines ancient heritage with contemporary cultural events.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["I attended a Ludovico Einaudi concert at the Small Roman Theatre in Pula and it was amazing. The venue is intimate and historic, giving the performance a magical atmosphere. Perfect for enjoying music up close in a unique setting.", "Really not much to be seen here, just an outdoor amphitheatre that's typically empty otherwise; the route here appears a bit difficult, seems like you're walking on private property inbetween buildings.", "Awesome venue for concerts. It's best to bring your own seat cushion or pillow for comfort!"]}}
6. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
7. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Titov Cadillac", "tags": ["attraction", "museum", "national_park", "historic", "island"], "description": "Historic Cadillac Eldorado Cabriolet on Brijuni, displayed as one of the park’s best-known attractions and associated with Josip Broz Tito, who used it to drive around the island with numerous distinguished guests.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Nice car in excellent condition like it’s new fully restored.", "Excellent model with top-notch equipment for that time. Preserved and in excellent condition. Can be rented for driving"]}}
8. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
9. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Tragovi dinosaura", "tags": ["attraction", "geopaleontological_site", "prehistoric", "national_park", "island"], "description": "A remarkable geopaleontological attraction where preserved dinosaur footprints reveal that ancient reptiles once walked this area around 130 to 100 million years ago. More than 200 footprints have been discovered across Brijuni, with visitor-accessible tracks on Veliki Brijun offering a rare and valuable glimpse into the prehistoric past.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["At first glance, nothing 'special' but when do you ever see real dinosaur footprints? I thought it was cool that they had a matching dinosaur statue next to it. If you're on the island, you should stop by there, too.", "Traces 100 million years old. Super exciting.", "It was simply amazing to see something like that. When and where else do you get the chance to admire original dinosaur footprints!? And the best part was, I was completely alone there (off-season, early June, around 5 pm), simply wonderful."]}}
10. {"type": "museum", "properties": {"name": "Čamčarnica", "tags": ["museum", "national_park", "island", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "Interactive permanent exhibition in the historic Boats House on Veliki Brijun, presenting the natural and cultural heritage of Brijuni through multimedia, themed rooms, and hands-on displays.", "rating": 3.5, "reviews": ["Definitely something great for kids"]}}

1. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "brunch", "breakfast", "burgers", "desserts", "cocktails"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cabahia", "phone": "+385 91 640 6330", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:30-24:00; Su 09:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "4", "addr:street": "Širolina", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-standing Veruda café recently refreshed into a snack bar, known for quality coffee, a wide beer selection, brunch dishes, burgers, bao buns, tortillas, desserts, and a relaxed local atmosphere.", "reviews": ["Great food, atmosphere, staff, and prices. I paid €12.80 for two bao buns, sweet potato fries, and a small macchiato. The other day I ordered a veggie tortilla and a hot dog with guacamole sauce via Wolt—each one better than the other. My sincere recommendation for this place!", "Currently the best snack bar in Pula, especially considering they offer a wide range of breakfast/brunch options that lean on the healthier side. The prices are also affordable and justified. The tortilla is large and excellent, the English muffin is my top choice, and the croque madame is also great. Any reviews below 4–5 stars aren’t accurate and can easily be ignored, because every time I’ve been here, it’s been even better than the previous visit.", "Excellent food, great service—an exceptionally kind and professional waiter. A warm and nicely decorated space, which is unfortunately unnecessarily crowded with tables."], "price": "medium"}}
2. {"type": "pub", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "brunch", "burgers", "music", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "The Shipyard Pub", "phone": "+385 91 181 0630", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 08:00-02:00; Fr 08:00-03:00; Sa 10:00-03:00; Su 10:00-02:00", "addr:housenumber": "1", "addr:street": "Svetog Teodora", "rating": 4.4, "description": "Lively pub on the Riva with burgers, pub food, cocktails, beer, and a spacious terrace. A popular evening spot known for music, DJ sets, quiz nights, and other events in a casual, social atmosphere.", "reviews": ["We stayed here once for a drink and once for dinner. The Service was fast, friendly and accommodating in both cases. The Aperol Spritz was just as delicious as the burgers. These were juicy with very tasty sauces and the caramelized onions rounded it off with a great taste. The fries were also well seasoned and perfectly crispy. The dressing of the ceasar salad was a bit unusual and not quite typical but also incredibly delicious, we would love to come back. Value for money was also reasonable, so what more could you want.", "Friendly and efficient staff with delicious food. The burger was very good and my wife really enjoyed the noodles. Worth a stop. Plenty of seating inside and the vibes were relaxing.", "Great little bar in the heart of Pula! The atmosphere is warm and relaxed, and the staff were incredibly friendly. The music was just right for chatting without shouting, and prices were very reasonable compared to other spots in town. Perfect place to stop for a drink after sightseeing. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a cozy and authentic bar experience in Pula"], "price": "medium"}}
3. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "desserts", "cocktails", "city_center", "breakfast", "brunch"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Aperitivo bar Galerija", "phone": "+385 98 435 580", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-17:00", "addr:housenumber": "26", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 3.9, "description": "A charming cafe located right above the Pula Arena, ideal for breakfast, coffee, cocktails, drinks, or ice cream with a unique historic backdrop. Its setting next to the ancient amphitheater makes it a great stop for a relaxed break in one of the city’s most iconic spots.", "reviews": ["A beautiful place next to the walls of the Great Arena. The service was very friendly and fast, and the food was even better. We had breakfast and got coffee with it and freshly squeezed orange included in the price, the croissants were warm and wonderful with cappuccino. Really worth a visit, all compliments and wonderful experience 🥐", "Friendly service. Cool atmosphere. There's a restroom inside. 🚻", "And it's great here. We climbed up and ordered ice cream for the kids. The ice cream was super tasty and the portions were large. The service was friendly. The garden by the Colosseum was great. I recommend it."], "price": null}}
4. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["wine", "cocktails", "beer", "breakfast", "brunch", "sandwiches", "desserts", "ice_cream", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Enoteca Istriana", "phone": "+385 99 323 6541", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 09:00-21:00", "addr:housenumber": "11", "addr:street": "Forum", "rating": 3.6, "description": "A wine and coffee bar in the heart of Pula’s old town, right on Forum square by the Temple of Augustus, known for its wide selection of Istrian wines and craft beers.", "reviews": ["Visited this wine bar 4 times during our stay in Pula for coffee, wine, ice cream and sandwiches in a relaxed warm friendly atmosphere. The service was fast and efficient provided by staff who were friendly and accommodating. I highly recommend this wine bar will revisit on a return to Pula.", "Very good place for coffee and verry kind staff. Breakfast is good , this is the best place of the square!"], "price": null}}
5. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "beer", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Caffe Bar San Antonio", "phone": "+385 98 924 4222", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 07:00-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "24", "addr:street": "Scalierova", "rating": 3.1, "description": "A casual café bar set directly above the Pula Arena, known for its terrace with a unique view of the amphitheatre. It serves coffee, beer, soft drinks, ice cream, and other classic café-bar refreshments in a relaxed open-air setting.", "reviews": ["Aperol Spritz are the best in Pula! Ice cream are just melting in mouth. The view is amazing", "Best view, good coffee", "Good coffee. Waitress semi friendly"], "price": "high"}}
6. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "desserts", "ice_cream", "sandwiches", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Milan 1967", "phone": "+385 52 383 296", "opening_hours": "Mo-Fr 07:00-19:00; Sa 07:00-14:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": null, "addr:street": "Trg 1. Svibnja", "rating": 4.3, "description": "A popular café by the city market, known as a longtime local meeting spot for coffee, juices, desserts, and light snacks.", "reviews": ["For my taste best coffee in pula and the lemonade fab, staff are friendly and the best thing they are now open till 6pm during the week so after the beach I can get another coffee. Thank You 😊 …", "A great place to sit and watch people pass by. Very friendly waitresses. Selection of snacks and cakes. Fountain nearby where kids can play without danger.", "Nice coffee, desserts and service, a bit expensive though. Atmosphere could be more cosy (for my taste)"], "price": "medium"}}
7. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "cocktails", "beer", "music"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Cinderela", "phone": "+385 52 540 777", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su off", "addr:housenumber": "23A", "addr:street": "Pazinska", "rating": 4.6, "description": "A long-running café known for quality coffee, drinks, music, and a lively yet relaxed atmosphere, with regular events and a comfortable terrace.", "reviews": ["We had coffee, it was delicious. Food bought from the bakery across the street can be eaten in the café.", "Good tasting espresso, and they also have things like oat-milk for a cappuccino if you can't handle the cow milk.", "Great for a coffee break or getting with friends. My car service is nearby so I usually wait there to pick up my car."], "price": "low"}}
8. {"type": "restaurant", "properties": {"tags": ["international", "barbecue", "grill", "meat", "burgers", "fries", "cocktails", "beer", "vegetarian", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": null, "name": "Agrippina Street Food", "phone": "+385 91 725 8544", "opening_hours": "Mo-Su 11:00-22:30", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Sergijevaca", "rating": 4.9, "description": "A lively street food restaurant in the center of old town, close to the main square. It is known for creative burgers, BBQ dishes, cocktails, and a casual atmosphere, making it a popular spot for quick meals, drinks, and relaxed evenings in the historic center.", "reviews": ["Food was great, probably the best burgers in the city. Considering the location, popularity and pactfulness of the place it is logical why there is a longer waiting period for the table and food, but in the end it pays off. I'd definetly encourage anyone to book the place a several days in advance should you plan on coming in the afternoon/evening hours.", "Coming back 3 Years in a row,every year some new things on the menu! I tried this year smashed caligula with homemade strawbery jam,great comination of flavours,Well diserved first place!", "Agrippina Imeprial burger is out of this world,wagyu steak is just melting! Very friendly staff and good vibes! I will be back defintly", "Great food, very good burgers (a lot of choice) and fries. Very polite and super friendly service. Dogs friendly. Central location.", "Great atmosphere and very welcoming staff. The food was fresh, tasty, and nicely presented, with portions just right. Service was quick and friendly, and the prices were fair for the quality. Definitely a place I’d recommend and visit again."], "price": "medium"}}
9. {"type": "fast_food", "properties": {"tags": ["burgers", "sandwiches", "fries", "salads", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": false, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Tanja 3", "phone": "+385 52 210 333", "opening_hours": "Mo-Sa 09:00-24:00; Su 10:00-24:00", "addr:housenumber": "5", "addr:street": "Dubrovačke bratovštine", "rating": 3.8, "description": "A classic city-center fast-food spot in Pula, popular for late-night burgers, fries, and quick comfort food.", "reviews": ["Wow. Small local place always have such a nice food. Two ladies inside. Very polite. Food was amazing. And cheep. Lot of people is coming and eating there. Local hit"], "price": "medium"}}
10. {"type": "cafe", "properties": {"tags": ["coffee", "ice_cream", "cocktails", "sandwiches", "desserts", "city_center"], "outdoor_seating": true, "indoor_seating": true, "name": "Kukuriku", "phone": "+385 52 210 498", "opening_hours": "Mo-Th 07:00-23:00; Fr-Sa 07:00-24:00; Su 07:30-23:00", "addr:housenumber": "7", "addr:street": "Istarska", "rating": 4.0, "description": "A relaxed city-center café, offering coffee, cocktails and casual sweet and savory snacks in a pleasant outdoor setting.", "reviews": ["Nice place, friendly waiter and really tasty food", "Loved this place! It has really good chocolate croissants and the cappuccino is also very good.", "Nice place in city center. A bit pricey. Aperol spritz 8eur, Hugo the same. Staff was nice and professional."], "price": "medium"}}

1. {"type": "monument", "properties": {"name": "Slavoluk Sergijevaca", "tags": ["monument", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman arch in central Pula, known as the Arch of the Sergii or Golden Gate, famous for its ornate reliefs and long-standing civic significance.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["The Golden Gate in Pula is a beautifully preserved historic landmark. Its Roman architecture and detailed stonework make it a must-see in the city center. A great spot for a quick walk, photos, and soaking in the ancient atmosphere.", "A Roman triumphal arch, beautifully intact through the ages. Its intricate carvings reflect the artistry of the Augustan era, while its enduring form stands as a testament to the power and legacy of ancient Rome.", "Beautiful Roman arch in the heart of Pula. The Arch of the Sergii is a stunning reminder of the city's ancient past. Great spot for photos and easy to find while walking through the old town.", "Another beautiful piece of history which must be seen to be appreciated when you’re in Pula. Seems to be the main entrance essentially to the late ish night shops and restaurants/bars etc. Did have a nice jazz band situated here one night too!"]}}
2. {"type": "city_gate", "properties": {"name": "Herkulova vrata", "tags": ["city_gate", "monument", "roman", "historic", "city_center", "landmark"], "description": "Ancient Roman city gate in Pula, known as the city’s oldest preserved Roman architectural monument, with a carved head of Hercules and an inscription linked to the founding of the Roman colony.", "rating": 4.3, "reviews": ["Small but historic. The Hercules Gate is easy to miss, but worth a quick stop. Ancient Roman carvings still visible—great for history lovers!", "Cool history, worth routing your walking path on your way to some of the more popular spots in Pula.", "The historical plaque is on the inside of the gate, making it hard to find, but still very picturesque."]}}
3. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
5. {"type": "artwork", "properties": {"name": "James Joyce", "tags": ["artwork", "statue", "historic", "city_center", "landmark", "near_attractions"], "description": "Bronze statue of James Joyce in central Pula near the Arch of the Sergii, commemorating the famous Irish writer’s stay in the city and its place in his early literary life.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["This statue made we search more about this Irish novelist. He was an important writer whose books are read today. Here you can take selfies with the statue and enjoy a cup of coffee in a table next to the statue.", "Nice sculpture. Beside a restaurant. If not known, or checked carefully, one can miss it for a person waiting outside a restaurant.", "Nice statue. You can sit with him."]}}
6. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
8. {"type": "archaeological_site", "properties": {"name": "Augustov Hram", "tags": ["temple", "roman", "historic", "landmark", "city_center"], "description": "Historic Roman temple on Pula’s Forum, admired for its classical architecture, monumental columns, and lasting connection to the city’s ancient past.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A remarkably well-preserved gem of Roman architecture, built during the reign of Emperor Augustus, it stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s ancient past. Its elegant columns, finely carved details, and harmonious proportions make it one of the best surviving examples of a Roman temple outside Italy. Inside, the temple houses a small collection of Roman sculptures.", "For a couple euro you get to turn back the clock to the time of Christ and envision what the Roman Empire resembled from an architectural perspective and from the statues of that period. Nice little stop in old town Pula.", "Loved the temple. Many interesting and beautiful pieces. Good explanation of tenples history. Also, it is a very welcoming stuff that could tell more if you are interested.", "The ancient building was bombed during WWII and has been restored with a lot of effort, hard work, and love. 2€ to get in and while it’s small inside it’s a contribution to maintain.."]}}
9. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Arena Pula", "tags": ["amphitheatre", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "landmark", "events", "concerts"], "description": "Roman amphitheatre from the 1st century and one of Pula’s most iconic landmarks, known for its monumental architecture, rich history, and major cultural events.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Incredibly well preserved ruins in a very cool part of town. So much to see around and inside. They also use the middle for various things. They had an ice rink there when I went.", "Pula is a small town, so seeing such a grandiose structure from the era of the great Roman Empire here is both unexpected and impressive. There are far fewer visitors than at the Roman Colosseum, so everyone has the unique opportunity to find a secluded spot, stand, and reflect on eternity, on how times, customs, and games have changed over the centuries. Don't miss the small but fascinating museum located in the arena's underground chambers—it's dedicated primarily to olive oil production in Istria.", "Gorgeous arena. A must see when in Pula. Beautiful weather helped to get some beautiful shots. More than 2000 years old and one of six biggest amphitheatres still standing.. breathtakingly stunning.", "What a site to see! Amazing roman arena built between 27–68 AD. Sixth largest in the world. There is a fee to enter and you are free to walk around once inside. There are QR codes that provide a self guided tour using your phone. Bring ear buds or headphones for the audio. This is one of the best preserved amphitheaters in the world. This is a must see."]}}
10. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "Titov Cadillac", "tags": ["attraction", "museum", "national_park", "historic", "island"], "description": "Historic Cadillac Eldorado Cabriolet on Brijuni, displayed as one of the park’s best-known attractions and associated with Josip Broz Tito, who used it to drive around the island with numerous distinguished guests.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Nice car in excellent condition like it’s new fully restored.", "Excellent model with top-notch equipment for that time. Preserved and in excellent condition. Can be rented for driving"]}}

1. {"type": "viewpoint", "properties": {"name": "Vidikovac Javornik", "tags": ["viewpoint", "national_park", "island", "historic", "nature"], "description": "Restored historic viewpoint on Veliki Brijun, known for its Austro-Hungarian metal structure, peaceful forest setting, and panoramic views over the island, sea, and nearby islets.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["Pretty great spot for a look out - multi layered observation tower in the middle of the forest, easy to climb up, and lots of space on top to view all around. There's several benches. It is a bit more overgrown with trees, so views somewhat obstructed. This place is a bit difficult to get to, no clear signs - there's only one main trail from the north, it's not paved; you do not have access from the side of the villas.", "Forest covered most of the view but still very nice to visit as it has few benches on the top of the tower to relax and enjoy the view and the breeze.", "Nice place, not much of a view since surrounding forest outgrew the structure - on the plus side, very quiet and peaceful place"]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
3. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
4. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Bourguignon", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "coastal", "events", "military_history"], "description": "19th-century coastal fortress in Pula, known for its circular design, military history, and cultural events.", "rating": 4.2, "reviews": ["Beautiful Austro-Hungarian fortress which is preserved, but abandoned. In my opinion the most beautiful one in Pula. Unfortunately it is closed for visitors. I recommend to visit in early morning (between 6:00-7:00 AM) because there are not any people around and sunlight is perfect for photography.", "Very nice place to visit. Not crowdy. 10 minutes slow walk from free parking space on front of resort ( on right side from the main gate). To reach te place we used wide route on right side of resort entrance on the bushes."]}}
5. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Monte Zaro", "tags": ["park", "historic", "hilltop", "observatory", "city_center", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Largest historic park in Pula, set on a hill around the observatory, with fountains, Mediterranean trees, and scenic views over the city and harbour.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I didn’t expect much, but Montezaro Park turned out to be such a nice surprise. It’s quiet, full and perfect when you need a break from the heat and crowds. I grabbed a coffee and just walked around for a bit…. really relaxing spot with a great local feel.", "The roots of Montezaro Park are deeply embedded in Pula’s past. Originally designed in the 19th century, it was a retreat for nobility and a symbol of prestige. Small park that has a fountain, many trails to get around, and plenty of flora areas to enjoy. It's on a small hill so you can get some views of the surrounding area.", "A quiet city park on a hill overlooking Pula harbour, a welcome escape far from the madding crowd."]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
7. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Fort Grosso", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "hilltop", "military_history"], "description": "Historic hilltop fortress on Monte Grosso near Štinjan, known for its early military role in Pula’s defence system, preserved circular form, forest setting, and wide views towards the Brijuni area.", "rating": 4.6, "reviews": ["One of the 19th century artillery forts around Pula. Partly conserved, it is possible to enter and explore it and to climb the staircase to the platform. It is still astonishing despite being neglected in all ways.", "Quite far from Pula. There are some nice places for mountain biking around here. To get to the fort you'll need to go off the main road at a point. There, Google Maps will get a little lost but just keep going on this dirt road. At a point you will find a sign with some info about the fort and there you are. Don't let the closed blue gate scare you, the entrance to the fort is to it's right. Quite the nice place. Awesome views.", "A majestic view from here! I think it's the best view among all those local towers. It is a few steps from Stinjan, but worth visiting, as well as going further to the fort closer to the sea (Valmaggiore)", "Nestled atop the city’s lush hill, the fortress offers a glimpse into Pula’s captivating past, intertwined with stories of power, conquest, and resilience. When I visited not long ago, the wear and tear were evident, and parts of the fortress have collapsed. While it poses certain risks, history enthusiasts may find the journey worthwhile. However, if you choose to visit, please proceed at your own risk and exercise caution, but those who go there will not regret it."]}}
8. {"type": "fort", "properties": {"name": "Mletačka utvrda", "tags": ["fortress", "historic", "panoramic_view", "city_center", "events", "concerts"], "description": "French-style defensive fortress built by the Venetians in the 1600s, with views of the city & bay.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["Amazing views from the top - panoramic of the whole site - was helpful as my first look of the city to get my bearings. Loved that the ticket also included use of the undercity tunnel network - helpful as it was raining on and off (visited a couple of days ago!)", "Very beautiful views. Nice fortress, with a tower from where the views are even more wonderful. The entrance fee is 7 euros.", "I like history and I've been to quite a few other fortresses and the design follows other fortress designs because you're trying to defend and required similar designs and systems. The fortress has been disarmed and the museums/displays on site are bright with information and displays but I found some lack.....that is not a bad comment, just a minor con. There has obviously been a lot of work to maintain the integrity of the stone work and that is definitely a pro. Definitely worth the time for a visit. I rate this 4 stars."]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Petra Krešimira IV", "tags": ["park", "historic", "roman", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "Central city park in Pula with a fountain, Roman mausoleum remains, flower beds, and a peaceful atmosphere close to the waterfront.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["A very nice, well-kept, well-maintained little place in the heart of the city. If you go here, you can sit on one of the small benches and breathe some fresh air while looking at the trees and flowers.", "A beautiful little park near Pula's historic center. The fountain in the center, made from a strange rock, is unique and remarkable. Otherwise, this green space is very well-maintained and has a good number of benches for a peaceful rest in the shade."]}}
10. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}

1. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Mornarički Park", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "playground"], "description": "Historic 19th-century park in Pula and the city’s oldest public park, known for its botanical richness, shaded paths, and children’s play areas.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Very nice park with fountains and children playground. Quiet place near main street, ideal for relax during hiking around Pula.", "Great place for stop and chill during walking through Pula."]}}
2. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Franje Josipa I.", "tags": ["park", "historic", "family_friendly", "city_center", "playground", "near_attractions"], "description": "Historic waterfront park in Pula, known for its shaded paths, palm trees, family-friendly atmosphere, and relaxed setting near the Riva.", "rating": 4.9, "reviews": ["A beautifully situated park right next to the port of Pula. Thanks to the tall trees, the playground remains shaded even in summer until after midday. A constant sea breeze makes it pleasantly cool despite the high temperatures. Highly recommended. Paid parking is available nearby.", "A good place to relax with beautiful views and palm trees all around. There are playgrounds and are close to many tourist attractions in Pula. I recommend it for those with children.", "A wonderful park by the harbor in Pula. With plenty of places to relax and a playground for the little ones. Beautifully landscaped and clean."]}}
3. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Brioni", "tags": ["beach", "family_friendly", "pebble", "concrete", "rocky"], "description": "Popular beach on the Verudela peninsula in Pula, known for its mix of rocky, concrete, and pebble areas, clear water, family-friendly setting, and wide range of beach facilities and water sports.", "rating": 4.4, "reviews": ["Yes, pleasant memories, wonderful places to visit. I highly recommend it.", "The beach is overrun with 'sea nuts' that look like jellyfish (but aren't stinging), making a peaceful swim impossible.", "Beautiful spot for a week off.  Enjoyed the watersports and had laughs>"]}}
4. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Huguesov park", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "memorial", "historic", "family_friendly"], "description": "City park in Pula known for its greenery, quiet central setting, and a bust of Nikola Tesla that gives the space memorial significance.", "rating": 4.7, "reviews": ["A lovely little park with a monument to Nikola Tesla.", "Great benches and perfect place to come with a book. Best during sunny days as there is a lot of shade and the breeze is nice. Highly recommend for locals or if you are visiting nice break/chill area outside as this area isn’t crowded."]}}
5. {"type": "apartment", "properties": {"name": "Apartments Antons", "tags": ["apartment", "adults_only", "city_center", "near_attractions"], "description": "A centrally located adults-only stay in the heart of Pula, just a short walk from the Arena, Kastel and other major historic sights. It offers comfortable modern accommodation with air conditioning, a kitchenette, private bathroom and free WiFi, making it a practical choice for couples and city-break travellers.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["Just the perfect place to be, wonderful apartment and parking place in the old town, and a great host!", "Great location, very clean, fully stocked with anything you could need, very responsive and friendly hosts, lots of hooks and outlets which was appreciated. Highly recommend!", "Wonderful apartment in the old city. Centrally located for a great selection of bars, restaurants and shopping. Well equipped with plenty of useful information provided. Amazing hosts, attentive and happy to help without being intrusive. On a three night stay they checked in with us to make sure we had everything - couldn’t recommend enough . Thank you so much for a lovely stay"]}}
6. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park grada Graza", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "pet_friendly", "historic", "playground"], "description": "Central city park in Pula, created after World War II and known for its shade, archaeological fragments, and relaxed atmosphere near the Forum.", "rating": 4.5, "reviews": ["I love this little hideaway before the forum. Nice place to sit and think about life while under the shade of a small tree", "Peaceful park with ancient fragments all over the place among children’s swings makes for an interesting contrast", "Fantastic for kids! A couple of advent houses, a small funfair just right for everyone... for both the little ones and the big ones! Enough for everyone! Just right today, not crowded or too many people... The temperature is pleasant for December 2025!"]}}
7. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park Mladenaca", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "family_friendly", "memorial", "near_attractions"], "description": "Small central park in Pula near the Forum, known for its landscaped greenery, evening atmosphere, and popularity for wedding photos and sunset walks.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A great place to watch sunset.", "A small park next to the ancient temple.", "A small green space near the central Roman Forum and the Temple of Augustus. It's certainly not the best place for jogging or long walks, but it's very well-kept, both for its lawn and trees, and boasts a curious monument located within. It's certainly a great place for a relaxing break in the shade, surrounded by stunning monuments."]}}
8. {"type": "beach", "properties": {"name": "Plaža Jupiter", "tags": ["beach", "island", "stone", "paved", "national_park", "family_friendly"], "description": "Well-maintained designated beach on Veli Brijun, known for its stone-paved shore, two spacious terraces, and relaxing atmosphere. It is one of the official swimming areas on the island, appreciated for its cleanliness, safety, and beautiful sunset views.", "rating": 4.1, "reviews": ["Jupiter Beach on Brijuni Island in Croatia is a true paradise! The water is crystal clear and ideal for children to swim and play safely. For snorkeling enthusiasts, this beach is an absolute dream – you can observe countless fish in their natural habitat. A perfect place to enjoy the beauty of the underwater world. Highly recommended!", "Cozy little beach"]}}
9. {"type": "park", "properties": {"name": "Park kralja Zvonimira", "tags": ["park", "city_center", "playground", "family_friendly", "memorial"], "description": "Peaceful waterfront park in Pula with shaded benches, a children’s playground, and cultural landmarks including the Marulić monument and the Balašević bench.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["A beautiful green space with several seating areas offering stunning views of the sea, shaded by beautiful trees. The lawn is beautiful and well-kept, and the surrounding area is very clean. Definitely a recommended spot for a lovely stroll."]}}
10. {"type": "playground", "properties": {"name": "McDonald's PlayPlace", "tags": ["playground", "family_friendly"], "description": "Small children’s play area next to a fast-food restaurant, designed for family visits and casual breaks, with enclosed play equipment and a slide for younger kids.", "rating": null, "reviews": null}}

1. {"type": "sport", "properties": {"name": "Kayak Centar Pula", "tags": ["sports", "kayaking", "coastal", "family_friendly"], "description": "Kayak tours in Pula offer an active way to explore the coastline through paddling, snorkeling, and swimming, with options including island, cliff and cave tours, sunset paddles, morning tours, and kayak rentals for solo visitors, couples, or families.", "rating": 5.0, "reviews": ["We booked this tour via an enquiry through the website but received communication via Whatsapp, which was very helpful. We were able to clarify stuff and gave us confidence to book. Our guide was great, he knew the area well having grown up locally and was friendly and happy to chat with all of the group, as well as imparting his local knowledge. The kayaking route was brilliant, not too strenuous with lots of great views and a break for swimming, snorkelling (snorkel & mask provided) or relaxing. The drinks and snacks provided by the guide was a great touch. The guide also took plenty of 'action' pictures and we all received a link to download the pictures for FOC, great keepsakes. Definitely recommend.", "We had an amazing time on the 3-hour sea kayak excursion with Pula Kayak Centre! Toni, our guide, was fantastic super knowledgeable, friendly, and made the experience feel really personal. The scenery was absolutely stunning, with crystal-clear waters and beautiful coastal views. Toni took us to some hidden spots and made sure we were all comfortable and safe throughout. It was a perfect blend of adventure and relaxation. Highly recommend this tour to anyone looking for an unforgettable experience in Pula!", "Super nice! Really worth! We paid 26 euro for a 2 person Kayak in 2 hours. It was perfect time to explore some islands around Verudela!"]}}
2. {"type": "attraction", "properties": {"name": "kayak tours | pulsevents.hr", "tags": ["attraction", "kayaking", "coastal"], "description": "Guided kayak adventure in Pula offering coastal exploration, sea caves, snorkeling, and scenic views of the city’s rocky shoreline, suitable for both beginners and experienced paddlers.", "rating": 4.8, "reviews": ["It was an amazing experience with plenty of challenging activities included: kayaking, snorkeling, cliff jumping, passing through canals within the rocks. The monitors are super friendly, speakgood English and take good care of the group. It is easily doable with kids at the age of 7 and 13 in a three place kayak. The monitors made plenty of underwater photos of all member of the group with good quality cameras. Water or beers were provided at the bay when we stopped, just like the swimming Google's for snorkeling. Highly recommended.", "This was truly one of the best experiences of my life!! Jhonnes was an excellent guide who did everything he could to make it a great trip. He is also amazing at capturing picturesque moments. My family and friends that saw the pictures were in aww and asked who the photographer was. I would highly recommend this adventure to anyone considering it.", "A fantastic experience from start to finish. Well organised and very patient with us as inexperienced kayakers. We were kept updated and when our taxi left us in the wrong place a quick phonecall to them and they sorted everything to get us there on time. First class service, we were with teenagers who loved it too. Thank you"]}}
